globalThis.CYDOC_DATA={"schemaVersion":1,"name":"CyMCPSDK","version":"0.7.0","defaultLocale":"en","locales":[{"code":"en","label":"English"},{"code":"fr","label":"Français"}],"aliases":{},"pages":[{"id":"chat-lab","title":"Chat Lab controls","description":"Connect a provider, send messages and expose the demonstration app commands.","section":"Guides","parent":"overview","order":2,"revision":"8","locale":"en","html":"\u003ch2 id=\"connect\">Connect\u003ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#/en/chat-lab/connect\" aria-label=\"Link to Connect\">#\u003c/a>\u003c/h2>\u003cp>Chat opens directly. \u003cstrong>Settings\u003c/strong> contains \u003cstrong>Providers\u003c/strong>, \u003cstrong>Logs\u003c/strong> and \u003cstrong>Help\u003c/strong>. \u003cstrong>Close\u003c/strong> returns\nto the conversation and its draft. \u003cstrong>F1\u003c/strong> opens Help.\nOpen \u003cstrong>Providers\u003c/strong> to search the catalogue, select a provider and edit its own fields. Selecting\na provider keeps the other providers&#39; fields in memory for this run. Use \u003cstrong>Connect / New chat\u003c/strong>\nto open it and return to Chat, or double-click a provider card to connect directly.\u003c/p>\n\u003cfigure data-cydoc-module=\"image\" data-cydoc-id=\"provider-settings\" data-config=\"{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;provider-settings&quot;,&quot;src&quot;:&quot;assets/providers-en.png&quot;,&quot;alt&quot;:&quot;Searchable provider catalogue with the OpenAI API connection and model settings&quot;,&quot;controls&quot;:&quot;minimal&quot;}\">\u003cimg src=\"assets/providers-en.png\" alt=\"Searchable provider catalogue with the OpenAI API connection and model settings\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\">\u003c/figure>\u003cp>\u003cstrong>Automatic connection\u003c/strong>, in Providers, is enabled at startup. Chat Lab detects installed native CLIs,\nuser npm installations, running Ollama/LM Studio/compatible services at their known local\naddresses, and API keys supplied through environment variables. It prepares the first available\nconnection without sending a message. The initial offline demonstration does not block this selection.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>Native CLIs retain their own default model and account. Local services can select a text model\nfrom the actual catalogue. Remote APIs display their catalogue and wait for your model choice.\nThe model dropdown offers returned IDs; a changed selection takes effect when you click\n\u003cstrong>Connect\u003c/strong>. Availability can still depend on your account and provider.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>\u003cstrong>Detect again\u003c/strong> repeats the scan. Provider cards distinguish detected installations, active\nconnections and setup requirements. The selected provider explains missing installations,\ncredentials, endpoints or local models. No provider is installed or authenticated by the scan.\nAPI keys remain in memory. Cloud APIs are contacted only when their connection is selected.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>If a native provider reports that authentication is required, \u003cstrong>Sign in\u003c/strong> opens its own login\nin a console. Complete that login and reconnect here. This action uses the detected installation.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>Manual fields remain available in Providers with automatic mode enabled. \u003cstrong>Refresh model catalogue\u003c/strong>\nretrieves real model IDs. Model and connection changes apply to the next \u003cstrong>Connect / New chat\u003c/strong>.\nSelecting a provider pre-fills its conventional endpoint, key variable and settings, together\nwith any detected installation.\u003c/p>\n\u003cfigure data-cydoc-module=\"image\" data-cydoc-id=\"automatic-connection\" data-config=\"{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;automatic-connection&quot;,&quot;src&quot;:&quot;assets/chat-auto-en.png&quot;,&quot;alt&quot;:&quot;Earlier interface capture of automatic CLI detection and a real streamed Codex reply&quot;,&quot;controls&quot;:&quot;minimal&quot;}\">\u003cimg src=\"assets/chat-auto-en.png\" alt=\"Earlier interface capture of automatic CLI detection and a real streamed Codex reply\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\">\u003c/figure>\u003cp>\u003cstrong>Installation and connection\u003c/strong> contains the CLI path and working directory or the API endpoint/key fields.\nExpand \u003cstrong>Advanced launch settings\u003c/strong> for the JSON argument array and provider-specific settings.\nUse the actual \u003ccode>.exe\u003c/code>, or \u003ccode>node.exe\u003c/code> and its script arguments; shell wrappers are not launched.\n\u003cstrong>Advanced settings (JSON)\u003c/strong> accepts provider-specific settings. \u003cstrong>System prompt\u003c/strong>, under \u003cstrong>Conversation and history\u003c/strong>, supplies\ninstructions at session creation. See \u003ca href=\"#/en/providers/configure\">providers\u003c/a>.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"messages\">Send and stop\u003ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#/en/chat-lab/messages\" aria-label=\"Link to Send and stop\">#\u003c/a>\u003c/h2>\u003cp>Type in the composer. \u003cstrong>Enter\u003c/strong> sends; \u003cstrong>Shift+Enter\u003c/strong> inserts a line. \u003cstrong>Ctrl+Enter\u003c/strong> also sends. \u003cstrong>Attach files\u003c/strong> selects\nlocal attachments. Text streams into the Markdown transcript; activity and thinking appear\nwhen emitted by the provider. \u003cstrong>Follow responses\u003c/strong> controls automatic scrolling.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>The native input grows with the draft. Select text for the formatting toolbar, or use\nCtrl+B/I/U/E. Drafts remain editable during a response; sending while busy keeps the draft.\nUse the chat’s \u003cstrong>…\u003c/strong> menu for a rendered draft preview. \u003cstrong>Ctrl+F\u003c/strong> searches the conversation.\nPress \u003cstrong>↑\u003c/strong> in an empty composer to recall the last user message. In conversations whose history\nthe SDK manages, you can edit a sent message or confirm deletion of its turn. Both actions leave\ngeneration idle.\nHover or right-click a message to \u003cstrong>Copy message\u003c/strong> or \u003cstrong>Reply\u003c/strong>; Reply inserts a quote into\nthe draft and waits for you to send it. Native session history stays under provider control.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>Attachments have their own cards. Images decode asynchronously and enlarge inside the app.\nTo include an image in a Markdown preview, attach the document and image to the same message\nand use its unique filename, for example \u003ccode>![Result](./plot.png)\u003c/code>. Reference definitions also work.\nClick a text attachment to preview it, or \u003cstrong>Save attachment\u003c/strong> to choose a destination for its\nembedded bytes. Press \u003cstrong>Ctrl+V\u003c/strong> to paste a clipboard image or copied Explorer files. Check\nthe thumbnail and remove an attachment before sending if needed. Preview services never\nfetch arbitrary Markdown image URLs. Formats without a decoder retain their file card and Save action.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>During generation \u003cstrong>Stop\u003c/strong> appears next to \u003cstrong>Send\u003c/strong>. Cancelling preserves the partial answer.\nIf the provider rejects a turn, that reply shows the provider’s explanation, the SDK error code\nand the provider code when available. Text already received remains visible. The same diagnostic\nis available in \u003cstrong>Logs\u003c/strong>, with credentials masked. You can change the model and send another\nmessage when ready.\n\u003cstrong>Reconnect\u003c/strong> explicitly resumes the current session; it does not resend the interrupted message.\nSee \u003ca href=\"#/en/conversations\">conversations and history\u003c/a>.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"logs\">Read the journal\u003ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#/en/chat-lab/logs\" aria-label=\"Link to Read the journal\">#\u003c/a>\u003c/h2>\u003cp>Open \u003cstrong>Settings → Logs\u003c/strong>. \u003cstrong>Raw JSONL\u003c/strong> shows the same events as the session file. Scroll up\nto read earlier entries while new events arrive. Rows show the local time, provider, operation,\nevent/error code, explanation and duration. Native connection stages include protocol initialization,\naccount checks and session creation. Generation events show response start and completion.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>Use the text filter or \u003cstrong>Errors only\u003c/strong>, toggle \u003cstrong>Follow log\u003c/strong>, and use \u003cstrong>Copy log\u003c/strong> to share diagnostics.\n\u003cstrong>Open log file\u003c/strong> opens the private session file saved in \u003ccode>%LOCALAPPDATA%/CyMCPSDK/ChatLab/logs\u003c/code>.\nFile writing runs in the background. Hover the filename for its full path. \u003cstrong>Clear view\u003c/strong> clears the\non-screen rows and preserves the file. Message contents, credentials and native session IDs are excluded.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>The view retains the newest 2,000 rows. Each session file is limited to 8 MiB; a visible notice explains\nwhen it stops growing or cannot be written. Logging never cancels a conversation.\u003c/p>\n\u003cfigure data-cydoc-module=\"image\" data-cydoc-id=\"connection-journal\" data-config=\"{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;connection-journal&quot;,&quot;src&quot;:&quot;assets/logs-en.png&quot;,&quot;alt&quot;:&quot;Chat Lab log showing a model refusal reproduced with a Codex simulator&quot;,&quot;controls&quot;:&quot;minimal&quot;}\">\u003cimg src=\"assets/logs-en.png\" alt=\"Chat Lab log showing a model refusal reproduced with a Codex simulator\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\">\u003c/figure>\u003ch2 id=\"commands\">Let an AI use app commands\u003ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#/en/chat-lab/commands\" aria-label=\"Link to Let an AI use app commands\">#\u003c/a>\u003c/h2>\u003cp>In Providers, expand \u003cstrong>Permissions and app tools\u003c/strong>. The demonstration exposes \u003ccode>get_counter\u003c/code> and \u003ccode>set_counter\u003c/code>,\nwith integer values between −1,000,000 and 1,000,000. The current value is visible in the panel.\u003c/p>\n\u003col>\n\u003cli>Enable \u003cstrong>Allow counter changes\u003c/strong> if you want writes to succeed.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Enable \u003cstrong>AI may use app commands\u003c/strong>, then make a new connection to Codex or a supported API transport.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Ask the AI to set the demonstration counter and read it back.\u003c/li>\n\u003c/ol>\n\u003cp>Direct attachment supports Codex, Responses, Messages, Chat Completions/OpenRouter and Ollama.\nOther CLIs use their native MCP configuration and return \u003ccode>Unsupported\u003c/code> for this direct-attachment option.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"external\">Connect another application\u003ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#/en/chat-lab/external\" aria-label=\"Link to Connect another application\">#\u003c/a>\u003c/h2>\u003cp>\u003cstrong>Expose local MCP\u003c/strong> creates an authenticated loopback server on a free port.\nCopy the displayed endpoint and use \u003cstrong>Copy MCP token\u003c/strong> to configure your client.\nUse \u003ccode>/mcp\u003c/code> for MCP tools, or \u003ccode>/v1\u003c/code> on the same port for direct SDK JSON.\u003c/p>\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block\">\u003cdiv class=\"code-toolbar\">\u003cspan>json\u003c/span>\u003cbutton type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy\u003c/button>\u003c/div>\u003cpre>\u003ccode class=\"language-json\">\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L1\" data-line=\"1\">\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">{\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token property\">\"method\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">:\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token string\">\"invoke\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token property\">\"name\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">:\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token string\">\"get_counter\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token property\">\"arguments\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">:\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">{\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">}\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">}\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003c/code>\u003c/pre>\u003c/div>\u003cp>Both routes share the same counter and live write policy. Disabling writes does not\ndisconnect the client. Disabling the MCP server closes the endpoint; enabling it again\ncreates a new token. See \u003ca href=\"#/en/operations\">operations\u003c/a> and \u003ca href=\"#/en/permissions\">permissions\u003c/a>.\u003c/p>\n","text":"Connect # Chat opens directly. Settings contains Providers , Logs and Help . Close returns to the conversation and its draft. F1 opens Help. Open Providers to search the catalogue, select a provider and edit its own fields. Selecting a provider keeps the other providers' fields in memory for this run. Use Connect / New chat to open it and return to Chat, or double-click a provider card to connect directly. Automatic connection , in Providers, is enabled at startup. Chat Lab detects installed native CLIs, user npm installations, running Ollama/LM Studio/compatible services at their known local addresses, and API keys supplied through environment variables. It prepares the first available connection without sending a message. The initial offline demonstration does not block this selection. Native CLIs retain their own default model and account. Local services can select a text model from the actual catalogue. Remote APIs display their catalogue and wait for your model choice. The model dropdown offers returned IDs; a changed selection takes effect when you click Connect . Availability can still depend on your account and provider. Detect again repeats the scan. Provider cards distinguish detected installations, active connections and setup requirements. The selected provider explains missing installations, credentials, endpoints or local models. No provider is installed or authenticated by the scan. API keys remain in memory. Cloud APIs are contacted only when their connection is selected. If a native provider reports that authentication is required, Sign in opens its own login in a console. Complete that login and reconnect here. This action uses the detected installation. Manual fields remain available in Providers with automatic mode enabled. Refresh model catalogue retrieves real model IDs. Model and connection changes apply to the next Connect / New chat . Selecting a provider pre-fills its conventional endpoint, key variable and settings, together with any detected installation. Installation and connection contains the CLI path and working directory or the API endpoint/key fields. Expand Advanced launch settings for the JSON argument array and provider-specific settings. Use the actual .exe , or node.exe and its script arguments; shell wrappers are not launched. Advanced settings (JSON) accepts provider-specific settings. System prompt , under Conversation and history , supplies instructions at session creation. See providers . Send and stop # Type in the composer. Enter sends; Shift+Enter inserts a line. Ctrl+Enter also sends. Attach files selects local attachments. Text streams into the Markdown transcript; activity and thinking appear when emitted by the provider. Follow responses controls automatic scrolling. The native input grows with the draft. Select text for the formatting toolbar, or use Ctrl+B/I/U/E. Drafts remain editable during a response; sending while busy keeps the draft. Use the chat’s … menu for a rendered draft preview. Ctrl+F searches the conversation. Press ↑ in an empty composer to recall the last user message. In conversations whose history the SDK manages, you can edit a sent message or confirm deletion of its turn. Both actions leave generation idle. Hover or right-click a message to Copy message or Reply ; Reply inserts a quote into the draft and waits for you to send it. Native session history stays under provider control. Attachments have their own cards. Images decode asynchronously and enlarge inside the app. To include an image in a Markdown preview, attach the document and image to the same message and use its unique filename, for example ![Result](./plot.png) . Reference definitions also work. Click a text attachment to preview it, or Save attachment to choose a destination for its embedded bytes. Press Ctrl+V to paste a clipboard image or copied Explorer files. Check the thumbnail and remove an attachment before sending if needed. Preview services never fetch arbitrary Markdown image URLs. Formats without a decoder retain their file card and Save action. During generation Stop appears next to Send . Cancelling preserves the partial answer. If the provider rejects a turn, that reply shows the provider’s explanation, the SDK error code and the provider code when available. Text already received remains visible. The same diagnostic is available in Logs , with credentials masked. You can change the model and send another message when ready. Reconnect explicitly resumes the current session; it does not resend the interrupted message. See conversations and history . Read the journal # Open Settings → Logs . Raw JSONL shows the same events as the session file. Scroll up to read earlier entries while new events arrive. Rows show the local time, provider, operation, event/error code, explanation and duration. Native connection stages include protocol initialization, account checks and session creation. Generation events show response start and completion. Use the text filter or Errors only , toggle Follow log , and use Copy log to share diagnostics. Open log file opens the private session file saved in %LOCALAPPDATA%/CyMCPSDK/ChatLab/logs . File writing runs in the background. Hover the filename for its full path. Clear view clears the on-screen rows and preserves the file. Message contents, credentials and native session IDs are excluded. The view retains the newest 2,000 rows. Each session file is limited to 8 MiB; a visible notice explains when it stops growing or cannot be written. Logging never cancels a conversation. Let an AI use app commands # In Providers, expand Permissions and app tools . The demonstration exposes get_counter and set_counter , with integer values between −1,000,000 and 1,000,000. The current value is visible in the panel. Enable Allow counter changes if you want writes to succeed. Enable AI may use app commands , then make a new connection to Codex or a supported API transport. Ask the AI to set the demonstration counter and read it back. Direct attachment supports Codex, Responses, Messages, Chat Completions/OpenRouter and Ollama. Other CLIs use their native MCP configuration and return Unsupported for this direct-attachment option. Connect another application # Expose local MCP creates an authenticated loopback server on a free port. Copy the displayed endpoint and use Copy MCP token to configure your client. Use /mcp for MCP tools, or /v1 on the same port for direct SDK JSON. json Copy { \"method\" : \"invoke\" , \"name\" : \"get_counter\" , \"arguments\" : { } } Both routes share the same counter and live write policy. Disabling writes does not disconnect the client. Disabling the MCP server closes the endpoint; enabling it again creates a new token. See operations and permissions . {\"method\":\"invoke\",\"name\":\"get_counter\",\"arguments\":{}}","headings":[{"id":"connect","text":"Connect","level":2},{"id":"messages","text":"Send and stop","level":2},{"id":"logs","text":"Read the journal","level":2},{"id":"commands","text":"Let an AI use app commands","level":2},{"id":"external","text":"Connect another application","level":2}],"anchors":["L1"],"languages":["json"],"code":"{\"method\":\"invoke\",\"name\":\"get_counter\",\"arguments\":{}}","assets":["assets/providers-en.png","assets/chat-auto-en.png","assets/logs-en.png"],"links":["#/en/providers/configure","#/en/conversations","#/en/operations","#/en/permissions"],"kind":"media"},{"id":"conversations","title":"Conversations and history","description":"Attach files, cancel a turn and restore an exact conversation without replaying it.","section":"Guides","parent":"chat-lab","order":2,"revision":"2","locale":"en","html":"\u003ch2 id=\"attachments\">Attachments\u003ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#/en/conversations/attachments\" aria-label=\"Link to Attachments\">#\u003c/a>\u003c/h2>\u003cp>\u003cstrong>Attach files\u003c/strong> snapshots the selected local files on the worker. Supported types include images,\naudio and text/PDF resources, depending on the transport and model. The panel lists attachment names;\nrich media preview requires resource services supplied by the host application.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>The composer grows with the text and accepts up to 256 files. File/content budgets and MIME/base64\nvalidation also apply. Unsupported content is rejected explicitly. A model receiving an image\ndoes not imply support for audio or documents.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"history\">Preserve a conversation\u003ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#/en/conversations/history\" aria-label=\"Link to Preserve a conversation\">#\u003c/a>\u003c/h2>\u003col>\n\u003cli>Enable \u003cstrong>Save history\u003c/strong> before connecting.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Choose a private directory and a simple history ID.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Send messages normally; each completed or interrupted turn is saved automatically.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Select the same provider/model, directory and ID, then \u003cstrong>Restore saved chat\u003c/strong>.\u003c/li>\n\u003c/ol>\n\u003cp>History is optional. It contains messages, tool results and embedded attachments: treat it as user data.\nKeys and connection configuration are not included. A storage error appears separately from a successful\ngeneration. Restoring does not resend a prompt or repeat an executed command.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"resume\">Resume and cancel\u003ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#/en/conversations/resume\" aria-label=\"Link to Resume and cancel\">#\u003c/a>\u003c/h2>\u003cp>Native providers resume their exact session when supported; stateless APIs use the host&#39;s saved history.\nIf the native session cannot be loaded, \u003ccode>SessionInvalid\u003c/code> preserves the history instead of creating a\nreplacement conversation. ACP session loading depends on the agent&#39;s negotiated capabilities.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>\u003cstrong>Stop\u003c/strong> cancels the active operation. \u003cstrong>Reconnect\u003c/strong> explicitly reopens the connection when needed.\nAfter interruption, decide whether to send another message; there is no automatic generation retry.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"api\">Public C++ API\u003ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#/en/conversations/api\" aria-label=\"Link to Public C++ API\">#\u003c/a>\u003c/h2>\u003cp>\u003ccode>Conversation::checkpoint()\u003c/code> returns a restorable snapshot. \u003ccode>ConversationStore::save(id, conversation)\u003c/code>\nwrites it privately and atomically; \u003ccode>load(id)\u003c/code> reads it for \u003ccode>Conversation::restore(snapshot)\u003c/code>.\nThe provider/model must match the snapshot. Keep provider instances and the executor alive until all\nasynchronous operations finish. Callbacks run on the calling worker, not the UI thread.\u003c/p>\n","text":"Attachments # Attach files snapshots the selected local files on the worker. Supported types include images, audio and text/PDF resources, depending on the transport and model. The panel lists attachment names; rich media preview requires resource services supplied by the host application. The composer grows with the text and accepts up to 256 files. File/content budgets and MIME/base64 validation also apply. Unsupported content is rejected explicitly. A model receiving an image does not imply support for audio or documents. Preserve a conversation # Enable Save history before connecting. Choose a private directory and a simple history ID. Send messages normally; each completed or interrupted turn is saved automatically. Select the same provider/model, directory and ID, then Restore saved chat . History is optional. It contains messages, tool results and embedded attachments: treat it as user data. Keys and connection configuration are not included. A storage error appears separately from a successful generation. Restoring does not resend a prompt or repeat an executed command. Resume and cancel # Native providers resume their exact session when supported; stateless APIs use the host's saved history. If the native session cannot be loaded, SessionInvalid preserves the history instead of creating a replacement conversation. ACP session loading depends on the agent's negotiated capabilities. Stop cancels the active operation. Reconnect explicitly reopens the connection when needed. After interruption, decide whether to send another message; there is no automatic generation retry. Public C++ API # Conversation::checkpoint() returns a restorable snapshot. ConversationStore::save(id, conversation) writes it privately and atomically; load(id) reads it for Conversation::restore(snapshot) . The provider/model must match the snapshot. Keep provider instances and the executor alive until all asynchronous operations finish. Callbacks run on the calling worker, not the UI thread.","headings":[{"id":"attachments","text":"Attachments","level":2},{"id":"history","text":"Preserve a conversation","level":2},{"id":"resume","text":"Resume and cancel","level":2},{"id":"api","text":"Public C++ API","level":2}],"anchors":[],"languages":[],"code":"","assets":[],"links":[],"kind":"guide"},{"id":"integration","title":"Integrate the C++ library","description":"Link only the modules your host needs and keep provider work outside its UI thread.","section":"SDK","order":0,"revision":"1","locale":"en","html":"\u003ch2 id=\"build\">Build requirements\u003ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#/en/integration/build\" aria-label=\"Link to Build requirements\">#\u003c/a>\u003c/h2>\u003cp>Use CMake 3.24+, C++20 and system threads. Windows uses Visual Studio 2022 C++, Windows SDK,\nWinHTTP and BCrypt. Linux/macOS use POSIX APIs and libcurl development files for HTTP(S).\nCurrent cross-platform distribution limits are listed in the source version notes.\u003c/p>\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block\">\u003cdiv class=\"code-toolbar\">\u003cspan>sh\u003c/span>\u003cbutton type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy\u003c/button>\u003c/div>\u003cpre>\u003ccode class=\"language-bash\">\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L1\" data-line=\"1\">cmake \u003cspan class=\"token parameter variable\">-S\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token builtin class-name\">.\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token parameter variable\">-B\u003c/span> build \u003cspan class=\"token parameter variable\">-DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">=\u003c/span>Release\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L2\" data-line=\"2\">cmake \u003cspan class=\"token parameter variable\">--build\u003c/span> build \u003cspan class=\"token parameter variable\">--config\u003c/span> Release \u003cspan class=\"token parameter variable\">--parallel\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token number\">4\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L3\" data-line=\"3\">cmake \u003cspan class=\"token parameter variable\">--install\u003c/span> build \u003cspan class=\"token parameter variable\">--config\u003c/span> Release \u003cspan class=\"token parameter variable\">--prefix\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token function\">install\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003c/code>\u003c/pre>\u003c/div>\u003cp>An installed host uses the exported targets:\u003c/p>\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block\">\u003cdiv class=\"code-toolbar\">\u003cspan>cmake\u003c/span>\u003cbutton type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy\u003c/button>\u003c/div>\u003cpre>\u003ccode class=\"language-cmake\">\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-2-L1\" data-line=\"1\">\u003cspan class=\"token keyword\">find_package\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">(\u003c/span>CyMCPSDK \u003cspan class=\"token number\">0.5\u003c/span> CONFIG REQUIRED\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">)\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-2-L2\" data-line=\"2\">\u003cspan class=\"token keyword\">target_link_libraries\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">(\u003c/span>my_app \u003cspan class=\"token namespace\">PRIVATE\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token inserted class-name\">CyMCP::Core\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token inserted class-name\">CyMCP::MCP\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token inserted class-name\">CyMCP::AI\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">)\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003c/code>\u003c/pre>\u003c/div>\u003cp>Alternatively use \u003ccode>add_subdirectory(external/CyMCPSDK)\u003c/code>. Disable unneeded modules with\n\u003ccode>CYMCP_BUILD_HTTP\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>CYMCP_BUILD_PLATFORM\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>CYMCP_BUILD_MCP\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>CYMCP_BUILD_AI\u003c/code> and\n\u003ccode>CYMCP_BUILD_LOCAL\u003c/code>; CMake checks dependencies. \u003ccode>core-only\u003c/code> builds the operation core.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"providers\">Create a conversation\u003ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#/en/integration/providers\" aria-label=\"Link to Create a conversation\">#\u003c/a>\u003c/h2>\u003cdiv class=\"code-block\">\u003cdiv class=\"code-toolbar\">\u003cspan>cpp\u003c/span>\u003cbutton type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy\u003c/button>\u003c/div>\u003cpre>\u003ccode class=\"language-cpp\">\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-3-L1\" data-line=\"1\">\u003cspan class=\"token macro property\">\u003cspan class=\"token directive-hash\">#\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token directive keyword\">include\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token string\">&lt;cymcp/ai.hpp>\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-3-L2\" data-line=\"2\"> \u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-3-L3\" data-line=\"3\">cymcp\u003cspan class=\"token double-colon punctuation\">::\u003c/span>ProviderRegistry providers\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-3-L4\" data-line=\"4\">cymcp\u003cspan class=\"token double-colon punctuation\">::\u003c/span>ProviderConfig config\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-3-L5\" data-line=\"5\">config\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">.\u003c/span>settings\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">[\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token string\">\"base_url\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">]\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token operator\">=\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token string\">\"http://127.0.0.1:11434\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-3-L6\" data-line=\"6\">\u003cspan class=\"token keyword\">auto\u003c/span> provider \u003cspan class=\"token operator\">=\u003c/span> providers\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">.\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token function\">create\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">(\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token string\">\"ollama\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span> config\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">)\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003c/code>\u003c/pre>\u003c/div>\u003cp>Construct \u003ccode>Conversation(provider, model_id)\u003c/code> with a real installed model ID, then call\n\u003ccode>connect()\u003c/code> and \u003ccode>send(text_block(prompt))\u003c/code>. These synchronous calls belong on a worker.\n\u003ccode>send_async(executor, content, context)\u003c/code> returns a future; keep the executor/provider alive.\n\u003ccode>CallContext.events\u003c/code> receives deltas and activity. Transfer them through an \u003ccode>EventQueue\u003c/code>\nto the UI. \u003ccode>cancel()\u003c/code> requests cancellation; \u003ccode>reconnect()\u003c/code> is explicit.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"chat-ui\">Embed the CyUI panel\u003ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#/en/integration/chat-ui\" aria-label=\"Link to Embed the CyUI panel\">#\u003c/a>\u003c/h2>\u003cp>\u003ccode>CYMCP_BUILD_CHAT_UI\u003c/code> and \u003ccode>CYMCP_BUILD_CHAT_APP\u003c/code> are off by default. The host supplies\n\u003ccode>CyUI::DocumentViews\u003c/code>, or sets \u003ccode>CYMCP_CYUI_SOURCE_DIR\u003c/code> to a compatible CyUI checkout.\nAn installed consumer creates its CyUI target before requesting \u003ccode>COMPONENTS ChatUI\u003c/code>.\u003c/p>\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block\">\u003cdiv class=\"code-toolbar\">\u003cspan>cpp\u003c/span>\u003cbutton type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy\u003c/button>\u003c/div>\u003cpre>\u003ccode class=\"language-cpp\">\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-4-L1\" data-line=\"1\">\u003cspan class=\"token macro property\">\u003cspan class=\"token directive-hash\">#\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token directive keyword\">include\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token string\">&lt;cymcp/chat_ui.hpp>\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-4-L2\" data-line=\"2\"> \u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-4-L3\" data-line=\"3\">\u003cspan class=\"token comment\">// After the host has created its ImGui context and initialized CyUI:\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-4-L4\" data-line=\"4\">cymcp\u003cspan class=\"token double-colon punctuation\">::\u003c/span>ChatController controller\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-4-L5\" data-line=\"5\">cymcp\u003cspan class=\"token double-colon punctuation\">::\u003c/span>ChatPanel \u003cspan class=\"token function\">panel\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">(\u003c/span>controller\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">)\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-4-L6\" data-line=\"6\"> \u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-4-L7\" data-line=\"7\">\u003cspan class=\"token comment\">// Inside the host window, between NewFrame and Render:\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-4-L8\" data-line=\"8\">panel\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">.\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token function\">draw\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">(\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">)\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003c/code>\u003c/pre>\u003c/div>\u003cp>\u003ccode>ChatController::open(ChatConnection)\u003c/code> schedules the connection. \u003ccode>send\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>refresh_models\u003c/code>,\n\u003ccode>save\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>disconnect\u003c/code> and \u003ccode>reconnect\u003c/code> also schedule worker operations; \u003ccode>poll\u003c/code> transfers results.\nUse the controller and its state from one host UI thread. Destroy it before the ImGui context\nand provider modules. Its destructor cancels and joins the worker.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>\u003ccode>ChatPanelOptions\u003c/code> supplies file selection, link opening and cached document resources.\nWithout a link callback, the panel offers a link to copy. Set the host&#39;s initial CyUI locale\nto \u003ccode>en\u003c/code> for English; the Windows example does so by default.\u003c/p>\n","text":"Build requirements # Use CMake 3.24+, C++20 and system threads. Windows uses Visual Studio 2022 C++, Windows SDK, WinHTTP and BCrypt. Linux/macOS use POSIX APIs and libcurl development files for HTTP(S). Current cross-platform distribution limits are listed in the source version notes. sh Copy cmake -S . -B build -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE = Release cmake --build build --config Release --parallel 4 cmake --install build --config Release --prefix install An installed host uses the exported targets: cmake Copy find_package ( CyMCPSDK 0.5 CONFIG REQUIRED ) target_link_libraries ( my_app PRIVATE CyMCP::Core CyMCP::MCP CyMCP::AI ) Alternatively use add_subdirectory(external/CyMCPSDK) . Disable unneeded modules with CYMCP_BUILD_HTTP , CYMCP_BUILD_PLATFORM , CYMCP_BUILD_MCP , CYMCP_BUILD_AI and CYMCP_BUILD_LOCAL ; CMake checks dependencies. core-only builds the operation core. Create a conversation # cpp Copy # include \u003ccymcp/ai.hpp> cymcp :: ProviderRegistry providers ; cymcp :: ProviderConfig config ; config . settings [ \"base_url\" ] = \"http://127.0.0.1:11434\" ; auto provider = providers . create ( \"ollama\" , config ) ; Construct Conversation(provider, model_id) with a real installed model ID, then call connect() and send(text_block(prompt)) . These synchronous calls belong on a worker. send_async(executor, content, context) returns a future; keep the executor/provider alive. CallContext.events receives deltas and activity. Transfer them through an EventQueue to the UI. cancel() requests cancellation; reconnect() is explicit. Embed the CyUI panel # CYMCP_BUILD_CHAT_UI and CYMCP_BUILD_CHAT_APP are off by default. The host supplies CyUI::DocumentViews , or sets CYMCP_CYUI_SOURCE_DIR to a compatible CyUI checkout. An installed consumer creates its CyUI target before requesting COMPONENTS ChatUI . cpp Copy # include \u003ccymcp/chat_ui.hpp> // After the host has created its ImGui context and initialized CyUI: cymcp :: ChatController controller ; cymcp :: ChatPanel panel ( controller ) ; // Inside the host window, between NewFrame and Render: panel . draw ( ) ; ChatController::open(ChatConnection) schedules the connection. send , refresh_models , save , disconnect and reconnect also schedule worker operations; poll transfers results. Use the controller and its state from one host UI thread. Destroy it before the ImGui context and provider modules. Its destructor cancels and joins the worker. ChatPanelOptions supplies file selection, link opening and cached document resources. Without a link callback, the panel offers a link to copy. Set the host's initial CyUI locale to en for English; the Windows example does so by default. cmake -S . -B build -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release cmake --build build --config Release --parallel 4 cmake --install build --config Release --prefix install find_package(CyMCPSDK 0.5 CONFIG REQUIRED) target_link_libraries(my_app PRIVATE CyMCP::Core CyMCP::MCP CyMCP::AI) #include \u003ccymcp/ai.hpp> cymcp::ProviderRegistry providers; cymcp::ProviderConfig config; config.settings[\"base_url\"] = \"http://127.0.0.1:11434\"; auto provider = providers.create(\"ollama\", config); #include \u003ccymcp/chat_ui.hpp> // After the host has created its ImGui context and initialized CyUI: cymcp::ChatController controller; cymcp::ChatPanel panel(controller); // Inside the host window, between NewFrame and Render: panel.draw();","headings":[{"id":"build","text":"Build requirements","level":2},{"id":"providers","text":"Create a conversation","level":2},{"id":"chat-ui","text":"Embed the CyUI panel","level":2}],"anchors":["L1","L2","L3","code-2-L1","code-2-L2","code-3-L1","code-3-L2","code-3-L3","code-3-L4","code-3-L5","code-3-L6","code-4-L1","code-4-L2","code-4-L3","code-4-L4","code-4-L5","code-4-L6","code-4-L7","code-4-L8"],"languages":["bash","cmake","cpp"],"code":"cmake -S . -B build -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release\ncmake --build build --config Release --parallel 4\ncmake --install build --config Release --prefix install\nfind_package(CyMCPSDK 0.5 CONFIG REQUIRED)\ntarget_link_libraries(my_app PRIVATE CyMCP::Core CyMCP::MCP CyMCP::AI)\n#include \u003ccymcp/ai.hpp>\n\ncymcp::ProviderRegistry providers;\ncymcp::ProviderConfig config;\nconfig.settings[\"base_url\"] = \"http://127.0.0.1:11434\";\nauto provider = providers.create(\"ollama\", config);\n#include \u003ccymcp/chat_ui.hpp>\n\n// After the host has created its ImGui context and initialized CyUI:\ncymcp::ChatController controller;\ncymcp::ChatPanel panel(controller);\n\n// Inside the host window, between NewFrame and Render:\npanel.draw();","assets":[],"links":[],"kind":"guide"},{"id":"licenses","title":"Licenses and components","description":"Understand the MIT SDK license and separately licensed optional components.","section":"Guides","parent":"overview","order":5,"revision":"1","locale":"en","html":"\u003ch2 id=\"sdk\">CyMCPSDK\u003ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#/en/licenses/sdk\" aria-label=\"Link to CyMCPSDK\">#\u003c/a>\u003c/h2>\u003cp>Copyright © 2026 Cyberalien. CyMCPSDK source is distributed under the MIT license.\nKeep the copyright and permission notice with redistributed copies. The source root&#39;s\n\u003ccode>LICENSE\u003c/code> and \u003ccode>THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md\u003c/code> contain the terms and component notices.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"components\">Components\u003ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#/en/licenses/components\" aria-label=\"Link to Components\">#\u003c/a>\u003c/h2>\u003ctable>\n\u003cthead>\n\u003ctr>\n\u003cth>Component\u003c/th>\n\u003cth>License\u003c/th>\n\u003cth>Scope\u003c/th>\n\u003c/tr>\n\u003c/thead>\n\u003ctbody>\u003ctr>\n\u003ctd>nlohmann/json 3.12.0\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>MIT\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>SDK JSON representation and validation\u003c/td>\n\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\n\u003ctd>cpp-httplib 0.66.0\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>MIT\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>Local HTTP server and test fixtures\u003c/td>\n\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\n\u003ctd>PicoSHA2\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>MIT\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>Artifact verification\u003c/td>\n\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\n\u003ctd>System libcurl\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>curl license and host TLS terms\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>HTTP(S) on Linux/macOS\u003c/td>\n\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\n\u003ctd>CyUI, Dear ImGui, MD4C\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>MIT\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>Optional native chat rendering\u003c/td>\n\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\n\u003ctd>Lexilla/Scintilla lexers\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>Their permissive notices\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>Optional code highlighting through CyUI\u003c/td>\n\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\n\u003ctd>JetBrains Mono\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>SIL Open Font License 1.1\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>CyUI&#39;s embedded font\u003c/td>\n\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\n\u003ctd>CyDoc reader\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>MIT\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>This static documentation reader\u003c/td>\n\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\n\u003ctd>marked, PrismJS, esbuild\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>MIT\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>Documentation generation tools only\u003c/td>\n\u003c/tr>\n\u003c/tbody>\u003c/table>\n\u003cp>The Windows package carries the complete optional UI notices in \u003ccode>licenses/\u003c/code>.\nThis manual includes the SDK and CyDoc MIT texts in \u003ccode>DocData/\u003c/code>.\nNo inference engine, model or GPU runtime acquires the SDK&#39;s MIT license: separately\ninstalled components and provider services retain their own terms.\u003c/p>\n","text":"CyMCPSDK # Copyright © 2026 Cyberalien. CyMCPSDK source is distributed under the MIT license. Keep the copyright and permission notice with redistributed copies. The source root's LICENSE and THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md contain the terms and component notices. Components # Component License Scope nlohmann/json 3.12.0 MIT SDK JSON representation and validation cpp-httplib 0.66.0 MIT Local HTTP server and test fixtures PicoSHA2 MIT Artifact verification System libcurl curl license and host TLS terms HTTP(S) on Linux/macOS CyUI, Dear ImGui, MD4C MIT Optional native chat rendering Lexilla/Scintilla lexers Their permissive notices Optional code highlighting through CyUI JetBrains Mono SIL Open Font License 1.1 CyUI's embedded font CyDoc reader MIT This static documentation reader marked, PrismJS, esbuild MIT Documentation generation tools only The Windows package carries the complete optional UI notices in licenses/ . This manual includes the SDK and CyDoc MIT texts in DocData/ . No inference engine, model or GPU runtime acquires the SDK's MIT license: separately installed components and provider services retain their own terms.","headings":[{"id":"sdk","text":"CyMCPSDK","level":2},{"id":"components","text":"Components","level":2}],"anchors":[],"languages":[],"code":"","assets":[],"links":[],"kind":"guide"},{"id":"local-engines","title":"Local engines and dependencies","description":"Connect an existing service or supervise an installed llama.cpp-compatible engine.","section":"SDK","parent":"integration","order":3,"revision":"2","locale":"en","html":"\u003ch2 id=\"service\">Use an existing service\u003ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#/en/local-engines/service\" aria-label=\"Link to Use an existing service\">#\u003c/a>\u003c/h2>\u003cp>Choose \u003ccode>ollama\u003c/code> for Ollama&#39;s native API, \u003ccode>lmstudio\u003c/code> for its compatible server, or \u003ccode>llama.cpp\u003c/code>\nfor an already running compatible endpoint. Set the actual service URL and a model it provides.\nChoosing a provider profile does not install or launch that product.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>Chat Lab connects to local services. It does not currently offer a model or GPU package installer.\nThe application embedding the SDK can provide its own installation workflow.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"supervise\">Supervise a native engine\u003ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#/en/local-engines/supervise\" aria-label=\"Link to Supervise a native engine\">#\u003c/a>\u003c/h2>\u003cp>\u003ccode>LocalEngine\u003c/code> owns a llama.cpp-compatible child process. Its options include the native executable,\nmodel path, private working directory, context token count, GPU layers and startup timeout.\nThe executable and model must already exist and be compatible with each other.\u003c/p>\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block\">\u003cdiv class=\"code-toolbar\">\u003cspan>cpp\u003c/span>\u003cbutton type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy\u003c/button>\u003c/div>\u003cpre>\u003ccode class=\"language-cpp\">\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L1\" data-line=\"1\">\u003cspan class=\"token macro property\">\u003cspan class=\"token directive-hash\">#\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token directive keyword\">include\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token string\">&lt;cymcp/local.hpp>\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L2\" data-line=\"2\"> \u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L3\" data-line=\"3\">\u003cspan class=\"token keyword\">void\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token function\">start_local\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">(\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token keyword\">const\u003c/span> std\u003cspan class=\"token double-colon punctuation\">::\u003c/span>filesystem\u003cspan class=\"token double-colon punctuation\">::\u003c/span>path\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">&amp;\u003c/span> server_executable\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L4\" data-line=\"4\">                 \u003cspan class=\"token keyword\">const\u003c/span> std\u003cspan class=\"token double-colon punctuation\">::\u003c/span>filesystem\u003cspan class=\"token double-colon punctuation\">::\u003c/span>path\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">&amp;\u003c/span> model\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L5\" data-line=\"5\">                 \u003cspan class=\"token keyword\">const\u003c/span> std\u003cspan class=\"token double-colon punctuation\">::\u003c/span>filesystem\u003cspan class=\"token double-colon punctuation\">::\u003c/span>path\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">&amp;\u003c/span> private_work_directory\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">)\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">{\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L6\" data-line=\"6\">    cymcp\u003cspan class=\"token double-colon punctuation\">::\u003c/span>LocalEngineOptions options\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L7\" data-line=\"7\">    options\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">.\u003c/span>process\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">.\u003c/span>executable \u003cspan class=\"token operator\">=\u003c/span> server_executable\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L8\" data-line=\"8\">    options\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">.\u003c/span>model \u003cspan class=\"token operator\">=\u003c/span> model\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L9\" data-line=\"9\">    options\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">.\u003c/span>private_work_directory \u003cspan class=\"token operator\">=\u003c/span> private_work_directory\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L10\" data-line=\"10\">    cymcp\u003cspan class=\"token double-colon punctuation\">::\u003c/span>LocalEngine \u003cspan class=\"token function\">engine\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">(\u003c/span>options\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">)\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L11\" data-line=\"11\">    engine\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">.\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token function\">start\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">(\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">)\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L12\" data-line=\"12\">    \u003cspan class=\"token comment\">// While engine remains alive, configure an API provider with\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L13\" data-line=\"13\">    \u003cspan class=\"token comment\">// engine.base_url() and engine.token(), then run the host's conversation.\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L14\" data-line=\"14\">    engine\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">.\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token function\">stop\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">(\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">)\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L15\" data-line=\"15\">\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">}\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003c/code>\u003c/pre>\u003c/div>\u003cp>Keep the engine alive until conversations finish. The supervisor checks readiness, supplies a private\nauthentication file and stops its owned process tree. It does not manage an unrelated user service.\nChoose GPU settings according to the installed engine and runtime; no GPU component is bundled.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"dependencies\">Download verified components\u003ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#/en/local-engines/dependencies\" aria-label=\"Link to Download verified components\">#\u003c/a>\u003c/h2>\u003cp>\u003ccode>DependencyManager\u003c/code> consumes a trusted host-supplied \u003ccode>Package\u003c/code> manifest containing artifact URLs,\nrelative paths, byte sizes, SHA-256 hashes and optional installer arguments. It provides \u003ccode>install\u003c/code>,\n\u003ccode>verify\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>run_installer\u003c/code> and \u003ccode>uninstall\u003c/code>. Its host policy decides whether those actions are allowed;\nan elevation callback handles installers that need it.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>Keep manifests under application control, never model output. Artifact paths stay in the configured\ncache; HTTPS and declared redirect hosts constrain downloads. External packages retain their own\nlicenses. A host may declare individual regular archive members with their destination, size and\nSHA-256. The system tar reader extracts them into a private staging area before publication.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>On Windows x64, select a local service in Chat Lab&#39;s \u003cstrong>Providers\u003c/strong> tab, open \u003cstrong>Installation and\nconnection\u003c/strong> and choose \u003cstrong>Install NVIDIA CUDA 12 runtime\u003c/strong>. Chat Lab downloads NVIDIA CUDART\n12.8.90 and its license to the user&#39;s private dependency cache. It shows the runtime directory\nwhen verification succeeds. A compatible NVIDIA driver and any other libraries required by the\nchosen engine are separate prerequisites.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>Windows and Linux x64 hosts can run the same installation on a worker and supply the directory\nto an owned engine. The supervisor applies the library search path to that child process.\u003c/p>\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block\">\u003cdiv class=\"code-toolbar\">\u003cspan>cpp\u003c/span>\u003cbutton type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy\u003c/button>\u003c/div>\u003cpre>\u003ccode class=\"language-cpp\">\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-2-L1\" data-line=\"1\">cymcp\u003cspan class=\"token double-colon punctuation\">::\u003c/span>DependencyManager \u003cspan class=\"token function\">dependencies\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">(\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">{\u003c/span>private_cache\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span> host_policy\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">}\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">)\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-2-L2\" data-line=\"2\">\u003cspan class=\"token keyword\">auto\u003c/span> installed \u003cspan class=\"token operator\">=\u003c/span> dependencies\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">.\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token function\">install\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">(\u003c/span>cymcp\u003cspan class=\"token double-colon punctuation\">::\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token function\">cuda_runtime_package\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">(\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">)\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span> context\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">)\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-2-L3\" data-line=\"3\">options\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">.\u003c/span>cuda_runtime_directory \u003cspan class=\"token operator\">=\u003c/span> installed \u003cspan class=\"token operator\">/\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token string\">\"runtime\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token comment\">// LocalEngineOptions\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003c/code>\u003c/pre>\u003c/div>\u003cp>The runtime is pinned to NVIDIA&#39;s \u003ca href=\"https://developer.download.nvidia.com/compute/cuda/redist/redistrib_12.8.1.json\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">CUDA 12.8.1 redistribution manifest\u003c/a>.\nThe installed package includes NVIDIA&#39;s license. HTTP Range resume and automatic GPU selection remain future work.\u003c/p>\n","text":"Use an existing service # Choose ollama for Ollama's native API, lmstudio for its compatible server, or llama.cpp for an already running compatible endpoint. Set the actual service URL and a model it provides. Choosing a provider profile does not install or launch that product. Chat Lab connects to local services. It does not currently offer a model or GPU package installer. The application embedding the SDK can provide its own installation workflow. Supervise a native engine # LocalEngine owns a llama.cpp-compatible child process. Its options include the native executable, model path, private working directory, context token count, GPU layers and startup timeout. The executable and model must already exist and be compatible with each other. cpp Copy # include \u003ccymcp/local.hpp> void start_local ( const std :: filesystem :: path & server_executable , const std :: filesystem :: path & model , const std :: filesystem :: path & private_work_directory ) { cymcp :: LocalEngineOptions options ; options . process . executable = server_executable ; options . model = model ; options . private_work_directory = private_work_directory ; cymcp :: LocalEngine engine ( options ) ; engine . start ( ) ; // While engine remains alive, configure an API provider with // engine.base_url() and engine.token(), then run the host's conversation. engine . stop ( ) ; } Keep the engine alive until conversations finish. The supervisor checks readiness, supplies a private authentication file and stops its owned process tree. It does not manage an unrelated user service. Choose GPU settings according to the installed engine and runtime; no GPU component is bundled. Download verified components # DependencyManager consumes a trusted host-supplied Package manifest containing artifact URLs, relative paths, byte sizes, SHA-256 hashes and optional installer arguments. It provides install , verify , run_installer and uninstall . Its host policy decides whether those actions are allowed; an elevation callback handles installers that need it. Keep manifests under application control, never model output. Artifact paths stay in the configured cache; HTTPS and declared redirect hosts constrain downloads. External packages retain their own licenses. A host may declare individual regular archive members with their destination, size and SHA-256. The system tar reader extracts them into a private staging area before publication. On Windows x64, select a local service in Chat Lab's Providers tab, open Installation and connection and choose Install NVIDIA CUDA 12 runtime . Chat Lab downloads NVIDIA CUDART 12.8.90 and its license to the user's private dependency cache. It shows the runtime directory when verification succeeds. A compatible NVIDIA driver and any other libraries required by the chosen engine are separate prerequisites. Windows and Linux x64 hosts can run the same installation on a worker and supply the directory to an owned engine. The supervisor applies the library search path to that child process. cpp Copy cymcp :: DependencyManager dependencies ( { private_cache , host_policy } ) ; auto installed = dependencies . install ( cymcp :: cuda_runtime_package ( ) , context ) ; options . cuda_runtime_directory = installed / \"runtime\" ; // LocalEngineOptions The runtime is pinned to NVIDIA's CUDA 12.8.1 redistribution manifest . The installed package includes NVIDIA's license. HTTP Range resume and automatic GPU selection remain future work. #include \u003ccymcp/local.hpp> void start_local(const std::filesystem::path& server_executable, const std::filesystem::path& model, const std::filesystem::path& private_work_directory) { cymcp::LocalEngineOptions options; options.process.executable = server_executable; options.model = model; options.private_work_directory = private_work_directory; cymcp::LocalEngine engine(options); engine.start(); // While engine remains alive, configure an API provider with // engine.base_url() and engine.token(), then run the host's conversation. engine.stop(); } cymcp::DependencyManager dependencies({private_cache, host_policy}); auto installed = dependencies.install(cymcp::cuda_runtime_package(), context); options.cuda_runtime_directory = installed / \"runtime\"; // LocalEngineOptions","headings":[{"id":"service","text":"Use an existing service","level":2},{"id":"supervise","text":"Supervise a native engine","level":2},{"id":"dependencies","text":"Download verified components","level":2}],"anchors":["L1","L2","L3","L4","L5","L6","L7","L8","L9","L10","L11","L12","L13","L14","L15","code-2-L1","code-2-L2","code-2-L3"],"languages":["cpp"],"code":"#include \u003ccymcp/local.hpp>\n\nvoid start_local(const std::filesystem::path& server_executable,\n                 const std::filesystem::path& model,\n                 const std::filesystem::path& private_work_directory) {\n    cymcp::LocalEngineOptions options;\n    options.process.executable = server_executable;\n    options.model = model;\n    options.private_work_directory = private_work_directory;\n    cymcp::LocalEngine engine(options);\n    engine.start();\n    // While engine remains alive, configure an API provider with\n    // engine.base_url() and engine.token(), then run the host's conversation.\n    engine.stop();\n}\ncymcp::DependencyManager dependencies({private_cache, host_policy});\nauto installed = dependencies.install(cymcp::cuda_runtime_package(), context);\noptions.cuda_runtime_directory = installed / \"runtime\"; // LocalEngineOptions","assets":[],"links":["https://developer.download.nvidia.com/compute/cuda/redist/redistrib_12.8.1.json"],"kind":"guide"},{"id":"operations","title":"Expose application operations","description":"Share one typed registry between native calls, SDK JSON, MCP and supported AI tools.","section":"SDK","parent":"integration","order":1,"revision":"2","locale":"en","html":"\u003ch2 id=\"registry\">Define a registry\u003ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#/en/operations/registry\" aria-label=\"Link to Define a registry\">#\u003c/a>\u003c/h2>\u003cp>An \u003ccode>Operation\u003c/code> has a portable name, a description, object input/output schemas, a read-only\nflag and a handler. The \u003ccode>Registry\u003c/code> validates inputs, applies its policy and checks declared outputs.\nThe read-only flag describes the operation; it does not override a denied policy.\u003c/p>\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block\">\u003cdiv class=\"code-toolbar\">\u003cspan>cpp\u003c/span>\u003cbutton type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy\u003c/button>\u003c/div>\u003cpre>\u003ccode class=\"language-cpp\">\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L1\" data-line=\"1\">\u003cspan class=\"token macro property\">\u003cspan class=\"token directive-hash\">#\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token directive keyword\">include\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token string\">&lt;cymcp/core.hpp>\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L2\" data-line=\"2\"> \u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L3\" data-line=\"3\">cymcp\u003cspan class=\"token double-colon punctuation\">::\u003c/span>Registry \u003cspan class=\"token function\">commands\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">(\u003c/span>cymcp\u003cspan class=\"token double-colon punctuation\">::\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token class-name\">Policy\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token double-colon punctuation\">::\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token function\">allow_all\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">(\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">)\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">)\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L4\" data-line=\"4\">commands\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">.\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token function\">add\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">(\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">{\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token string\">\"get_counter\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token string\">\"Read the demonstration counter.\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L5\" data-line=\"5\">    \u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">{\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">{\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token string\">\"type\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token string\">\"object\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">}\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">{\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token string\">\"additionalProperties\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token boolean\">false\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">}\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">}\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L6\" data-line=\"6\">    \u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">{\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">{\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token string\">\"type\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token string\">\"object\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">}\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L7\" data-line=\"7\">     \u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">{\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token string\">\"properties\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">{\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">{\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token string\">\"value\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">{\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">{\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token string\">\"type\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token string\">\"integer\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">}\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">}\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">}\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">}\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">}\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L8\" data-line=\"8\">     \u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">{\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token string\">\"required\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">{\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token string\">\"value\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">}\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">}\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">{\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token string\">\"additionalProperties\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token boolean\">false\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">}\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">}\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L9\" data-line=\"9\">    \u003cspan class=\"token boolean\">true\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L10\" data-line=\"10\">    \u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">[\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">]\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">(\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token keyword\">const\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token keyword\">auto\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">&amp;\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token keyword\">const\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token keyword\">auto\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">&amp;\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">)\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">{\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token keyword\">return\u003c/span> cymcp\u003cspan class=\"token double-colon punctuation\">::\u003c/span>Json\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">{\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">{\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token string\">\"value\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token number\">42\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">}\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">}\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">}\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">}\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">)\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L11\" data-line=\"11\">\u003cspan class=\"token keyword\">auto\u003c/span> result \u003cspan class=\"token operator\">=\u003c/span> commands\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">.\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token function\">invoke\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">(\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token string\">\"get_counter\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span> cymcp\u003cspan class=\"token double-colon punctuation\">::\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token class-name\">Json\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token double-colon punctuation\">::\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token function\">object\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">(\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">)\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">)\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003c/code>\u003c/pre>\u003c/div>\u003cp>This example explicitly permits its harmless read operation. For an editable domain, use the\nhost&#39;s policy and synchronize access to its objects. MCP handlers can run concurrently; marshal\nUI-bound mutations onto the host&#39;s event loop and keep captured state alive.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"sdk\">Direct SDK JSON\u003ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#/en/operations/sdk\" aria-label=\"Link to Direct SDK JSON\">#\u003c/a>\u003c/h2>\u003cp>\u003ccode>dispatch_app(registry, request, context)\u003c/code> accepts these application messages:\u003c/p>\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block\">\u003cdiv class=\"code-toolbar\">\u003cspan>json\u003c/span>\u003cbutton type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy\u003c/button>\u003c/div>\u003cpre>\u003ccode class=\"language-json\">\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-2-L1\" data-line=\"1\">\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">{\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token property\">\"method\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">:\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token string\">\"describe\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">}\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003c/code>\u003c/pre>\u003c/div>\u003cdiv class=\"code-block\">\u003cdiv class=\"code-toolbar\">\u003cspan>json\u003c/span>\u003cbutton type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy\u003c/button>\u003c/div>\u003cpre>\u003ccode class=\"language-json\">\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-3-L1\" data-line=\"1\">\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">{\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token property\">\"method\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">:\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token string\">\"invoke\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token property\">\"name\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">:\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token string\">\"get_counter\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token property\">\"arguments\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">:\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">{\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">}\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">}\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003c/code>\u003c/pre>\u003c/div>\u003cp>The example CLI supports \u003ccode>describe\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>invoke\u003c/code>, and application JSONL on stdin. Application JSONL\nand MCP JSON-RPC are separate protocols. In Chat Lab, the same requests go to \u003ccode>/v1\u003c/code> on its enabled\nlocal server, with \u003ccode>Content-Type: application/json\u003c/code> and the Bearer token.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"mcp\">MCP server and client\u003ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#/en/operations/mcp\" aria-label=\"Link to MCP server and client\">#\u003c/a>\u003c/h2>\u003cp>\u003ccode>McpServer(registry)\u003c/code> exposes operations as MCP tools. \u003ccode>serve_stdio(input, output)\u003c/code> serves a CLI\nconnection; \u003ccode>handle(request, context)\u003c/code> integrates with an HTTP endpoint. Keep the registry and\nserver alive for the entire connection.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>\u003ccode>McpClient(ProcessOptions)\u003c/code> connects over stdio; \u003ccode>McpClient(url, token)\u003c/code> connects to local HTTP\nwhen HTTP support is built. Call \u003ccode>connect\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>list_tools\u003c/code> and \u003ccode>call_tool(name, arguments)\u003c/code>.\nInspect an MCP result&#39;s \u003ccode>isError\u003c/code> before treating its \u003ccode>structuredContent\u003c/code> as successful output.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>To let an AI in app A use app B, connect a client to B, register explicit forwarding operations\nin A and attach that registry to a supported provider. Preserve B&#39;s schema and enforce A&#39;s policy\nbefore forwarding. Do not let model output register arbitrary new operations.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"tools\">Attach tools to a conversation\u003ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#/en/operations/tools\" aria-label=\"Link to Attach tools to a conversation\">#\u003c/a>\u003c/h2>\u003cp>Supply a shared registry in \u003ccode>ProviderConfig.tools\u003c/code> for supported API providers or Codex&#39;s dynamic\ntools. The registry owns the policy for actual app operations. For other CLIs, expose MCP and pass\ntheir provider-native MCP configuration. ACP uses \u003ccode>settings.mcp_servers\u003c/code> as an ACP-format array.\nSee \u003ca href=\"#/en/permissions\">permissions\u003c/a> before exposing mutations.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>For large registries, see \u003ca href=\"#/en/optimization\">on-demand tools, resources and grep\u003c/a>. These features\npreserve the original commands and policy while reducing what is loaded into an AI&#39;s context.\u003c/p>\n","text":"Define a registry # An Operation has a portable name, a description, object input/output schemas, a read-only flag and a handler. The Registry validates inputs, applies its policy and checks declared outputs. The read-only flag describes the operation; it does not override a denied policy. cpp Copy # include \u003ccymcp/core.hpp> cymcp :: Registry commands ( cymcp :: Policy :: allow_all ( ) ) ; commands . add ( { \"get_counter\" , \"Read the demonstration counter.\" , { { \"type\" , \"object\" } , { \"additionalProperties\" , false } } , { { \"type\" , \"object\" } , { \"properties\" , { { \"value\" , { { \"type\" , \"integer\" } } } } } , { \"required\" , { \"value\" } } , { \"additionalProperties\" , false } } , true , [ ] ( const auto & , const auto & ) { return cymcp :: Json { { \"value\" , 42 } } ; } } ) ; auto result = commands . invoke ( \"get_counter\" , cymcp :: Json :: object ( ) ) ; This example explicitly permits its harmless read operation. For an editable domain, use the host's policy and synchronize access to its objects. MCP handlers can run concurrently; marshal UI-bound mutations onto the host's event loop and keep captured state alive. Direct SDK JSON # dispatch_app(registry, request, context) accepts these application messages: json Copy { \"method\" : \"describe\" } json Copy { \"method\" : \"invoke\" , \"name\" : \"get_counter\" , \"arguments\" : { } } The example CLI supports describe , invoke , and application JSONL on stdin. Application JSONL and MCP JSON-RPC are separate protocols. In Chat Lab, the same requests go to /v1 on its enabled local server, with Content-Type: application/json and the Bearer token. MCP server and client # McpServer(registry) exposes operations as MCP tools. serve_stdio(input, output) serves a CLI connection; handle(request, context) integrates with an HTTP endpoint. Keep the registry and server alive for the entire connection. McpClient(ProcessOptions) connects over stdio; McpClient(url, token) connects to local HTTP when HTTP support is built. Call connect , list_tools and call_tool(name, arguments) . Inspect an MCP result's isError before treating its structuredContent as successful output. To let an AI in app A use app B, connect a client to B, register explicit forwarding operations in A and attach that registry to a supported provider. Preserve B's schema and enforce A's policy before forwarding. Do not let model output register arbitrary new operations. Attach tools to a conversation # Supply a shared registry in ProviderConfig.tools for supported API providers or Codex's dynamic tools. The registry owns the policy for actual app operations. For other CLIs, expose MCP and pass their provider-native MCP configuration. ACP uses settings.mcp_servers as an ACP-format array. See permissions before exposing mutations. For large registries, see on-demand tools, resources and grep . These features preserve the original commands and policy while reducing what is loaded into an AI's context. #include \u003ccymcp/core.hpp> cymcp::Registry commands(cymcp::Policy::allow_all()); commands.add({\"get_counter\", \"Read the demonstration counter.\", {{\"type\", \"object\"}, {\"additionalProperties\", false}}, {{\"type\", \"object\"}, {\"properties\", {{\"value\", {{\"type\", \"integer\"}}}}}, {\"required\", {\"value\"}}, {\"additionalProperties\", false}}, true, [](const auto&, const auto&) { return cymcp::Json{{\"value\", 42}}; }}); auto result = commands.invoke(\"get_counter\", cymcp::Json::object()); {\"method\":\"describe\"} {\"method\":\"invoke\",\"name\":\"get_counter\",\"arguments\":{}}","headings":[{"id":"registry","text":"Define a registry","level":2},{"id":"sdk","text":"Direct SDK JSON","level":2},{"id":"mcp","text":"MCP server and client","level":2},{"id":"tools","text":"Attach tools to a conversation","level":2}],"anchors":["L1","L2","L3","L4","L5","L6","L7","L8","L9","L10","L11","code-2-L1","code-3-L1"],"languages":["cpp","json"],"code":"#include \u003ccymcp/core.hpp>\n\ncymcp::Registry commands(cymcp::Policy::allow_all());\ncommands.add({\"get_counter\", \"Read the demonstration counter.\",\n    {{\"type\", \"object\"}, {\"additionalProperties\", false}},\n    {{\"type\", \"object\"},\n     {\"properties\", {{\"value\", {{\"type\", \"integer\"}}}}},\n     {\"required\", {\"value\"}}, {\"additionalProperties\", false}},\n    true,\n    [](const auto&, const auto&) { return cymcp::Json{{\"value\", 42}}; }});\nauto result = commands.invoke(\"get_counter\", cymcp::Json::object());\n{\"method\":\"describe\"}\n{\"method\":\"invoke\",\"name\":\"get_counter\",\"arguments\":{}}","assets":[],"links":["#/en/permissions","#/en/optimization"],"kind":"guide"},{"id":"optimization","title":"On-demand tools, resources and grep","description":"Keep every app command accessible while reducing catalogue and result traffic.","section":"SDK","parent":"integration","order":2,"revision":"2","locale":"en","html":"\u003ch2 id=\"tools\">Discover without losing capabilities\u003ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#/en/optimization/tools\" aria-label=\"Link to Discover without losing capabilities\">#\u003c/a>\u003c/h2>\u003cp>Optional \u003ca href=\"#/en/runtime-options\">disk storage, performance logs, change subscriptions and API context windows\u003c/a>\nextend these facilities without changing their default behavior.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>\u003ccode>Registry\u003c/code> remains the source of truth. Direct SDK calls and ordinary MCP tools preserve their\nnames, arguments, output schemas and policies. \u003ccode>describe()\u003c/code> still returns the complete catalogue.\nImmutable \u003ccode>catalogue()\u003c/code> and schema-free \u003ccode>summaries()\u003c/code> snapshots are reused until \u003ccode>add\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>replace\u003c/code>\nor \u003ccode>remove\u003c/code> changes the registry; \u003ccode>describe(name)\u003c/code> loads one full definition.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>\u003ccode>ToolGateway\u003c/code> exposes five standard callable tools instead of every definition:\u003c/p>\n\u003ctable>\n\u003cthead>\n\u003ctr>\n\u003cth>Tool\u003c/th>\n\u003cth>Purpose\u003c/th>\n\u003c/tr>\n\u003c/thead>\n\u003ctbody>\u003ctr>\n\u003ctd>\u003ccode>cy_tools_search\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>Search names/descriptions; omit query to browse every command. Follow nextCursor with the same query.\u003c/td>\n\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\n\u003ctd>\u003ccode>cy_tools_describe\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>Retrieve one complete input/output schema.\u003c/td>\n\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\n\u003ctd>\u003ccode>cy_tools_call\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>Invoke the original command with its arguments and the caller&#39;s context.\u003c/td>\n\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\n\u003ctd>\u003ccode>cy_resources_read\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>Read an application resource, manifest or chunk.\u003c/td>\n\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\n\u003ctd>\u003ccode>cy_resources_grep\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>Search registered text resources without loading their entire contents.\u003c/td>\n\u003c/tr>\n\u003c/tbody>\u003c/table>\n\u003cp>Search and describe never execute app commands. Invocation still validates the original schemas\nand applies the original policy, including explicit allow-all. No command is permanently hidden.\nSearch cursors become invalid after registry changes; restart discovery explicitly.\u003c/p>\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block\">\u003cdiv class=\"code-toolbar\">\u003cspan>cpp\u003c/span>\u003cbutton type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy\u003c/button>\u003c/div>\u003cpre>\u003ccode class=\"language-cpp\">\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L1\" data-line=\"1\">\u003cspan class=\"token macro property\">\u003cspan class=\"token directive-hash\">#\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token directive keyword\">include\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token string\">&lt;cymcp/mcp.hpp>\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L2\" data-line=\"2\">\u003cspan class=\"token macro property\">\u003cspan class=\"token directive-hash\">#\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token directive keyword\">include\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token string\">&lt;cymcp/resources.hpp>\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L3\" data-line=\"3\"> \u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L4\" data-line=\"4\">\u003cspan class=\"token keyword\">auto\u003c/span> commands \u003cspan class=\"token operator\">=\u003c/span> std\u003cspan class=\"token double-colon punctuation\">::\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token generic-function\">\u003cspan class=\"token function\">make_shared\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token generic class-name\">\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">&lt;\u003c/span>cymcp\u003cspan class=\"token double-colon punctuation\">::\u003c/span>Registry\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">>\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">(\u003c/span>host_policy\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">)\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L5\" data-line=\"5\">\u003cspan class=\"token comment\">// Register all application operations on commands.\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L6\" data-line=\"6\">cymcp\u003cspan class=\"token double-colon punctuation\">::\u003c/span>ToolGateway \u003cspan class=\"token function\">gateway\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">(\u003c/span>commands\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">)\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L7\" data-line=\"7\">cymcp\u003cspan class=\"token double-colon punctuation\">::\u003c/span>McpServerOptions options\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L8\" data-line=\"8\">options\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">.\u003c/span>resources \u003cspan class=\"token operator\">=\u003c/span> gateway\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">.\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token function\">resources\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">(\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">)\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L9\" data-line=\"9\">cymcp\u003cspan class=\"token double-colon punctuation\">::\u003c/span>McpServer \u003cspan class=\"token function\">server\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">(\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">*\u003c/span>gateway\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">.\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token function\">tools\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">(\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">)\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token string\">\"My application\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span> options\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">)\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L10\" data-line=\"10\">\u003cspan class=\"token comment\">// Keep gateway/commands alive while serving. For an API: config.tools = gateway.tools().\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003c/code>\u003c/pre>\u003c/div>\u003cp>API transports and Codex automatically choose this mode when constructed with more than\n32 tools. \u003ccode>settings.tool_discovery_threshold\u003c/code> changes the threshold; \u003ccode>settings.deferred_tools=false\u003c/code>\nkeeps full definitions. Typed options expose \u003ccode>tool_discovery_threshold\u003c/code> (\u003ccode>size_t\u003c/code> maximum disables it).\nAn explicitly created gateway works with any tool-capable transport. Other native agents retain\ntheir native MCP configuration; the SDK does not invent unsupported CLI tool injection.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"resources\">Read only the data needed\u003ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#/en/optimization/resources\" aria-label=\"Link to Read only the data needed\">#\u003c/a>\u003c/h2>\u003cp>\u003ccode>ResourceRegistry\u003c/code> belongs to \u003ccode>CyMCP::Core\u003c/code>; it also works without MCP or HTTP. Register a\n\u003ccode>Resource\u003c/code> with URI, name, MIME type, byte size and a bounded read callback over an \u003cstrong>immutable\nhost snapshot\u003c/strong>. No filesystem or network is implicitly exposed. Resource reads have their own\npolicy (\u003ccode>resources.read\u003c/code>, arguments containing the requested URI), cancellation and ownership checks.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>MCP advertises \u003ccode>resources/list\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>resources/read\u003c/code> and an empty template catalogue only when\n\u003ccode>McpServerOptions.resources\u003c/code> is supplied. Listing resources does not read their contents.\nSmall contents are returned directly; larger contents return a JSON manifest\n(\u003ccode>type: cymcp.resource.v1\u003c/code>) with \u003ccode>firstUri\u003c/code>, original MIME type, size and chunk size.\nRead firstUri and follow \u003ccode>_meta[&quot;com.cymcp/chunk&quot;].nextUri\u003c/code> until eof. Text chunks preserve UTF-8;\nbinary chunks use standard base64. Never treat an excerpt as a full result.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>Gateway results over 16 KiB become private resource handles; MCP also includes a standard\n\u003ccode>resource_link\u003c/code>. Read with native resources/read or cy_resources_read. Defaults are 32 KiB per\nchunk, 64 MiB retained bytes, 128 results and five-minute retention; all are host-configurable.\nResults are not listed publicly and are bound to \u003ccode>CallContext.principal\u003c/code>. The host must assign\nseparate principals for callers that must be isolated. Replacing a registered snapshot invalidates\nits old chunk URIs. Expiry or LRU eviction returns ResourceNotFound; it never reruns a command.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>A result larger than the retained byte budget remains inline without truncation or re-execution.\nTo keep arbitrarily large datasets bounded, expose them as host-backed snapshot resources or\npaginated application commands from the start. The gateway cannot remove memory already\nallocated by a handler returning a large JSON object. Ordinary unwrapped tools keep their original\nstructured output; the gateway does not violate their outputSchema by substituting a handle.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"cache\">Cache and compatibility\u003ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#/en/optimization/cache\" aria-label=\"Link to Cache and compatibility\">#\u003c/a>\u003c/h2>\u003cp>MCP tools/list and resources/list have revision-bound cursors (64 entries per page by default).\n\u003ccode>McpClient::list_tools()\u003c/code> still aggregates every page; \u003ccode>list_tools_page()\u003c/code> reads just one.\nAn absent nextCursor ends pagination; empty cursors are accepted from other implementations.\n\u003ccode>get_tool(name)\u003c/code> uses advertised \u003ccode>cymcp/tools/get\u003c/code> when supported and falls back to full discovery\nfor older peers. The extension is optional; the five gateway tools use ordinary MCP tool calls.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>Client caches are private per instance and keyed by method plus all parameters. Only discovery,\nschema lookup and resource reads with positive server ttlMs are cached. Defaults: 256 entries,\n16 MiB serialized data and a maximum 30-second TTL. Zero TTL or zero local limits disables caching.\nTools/call and errors are never cached. No background polling occurs. Changes may remain cached\nuntil TTL: use clear_cache() for an immediate refresh after known external changes. Reconnect,\nclose and received catalogue/resource change notifications invalidate the cache. A tool error also\nclears it, without retrying the operation. \u003ccode>cache_stats()\u003c/code> reports hits, misses and retained bytes.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"grep\">Fast text search\u003ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#/en/optimization/grep\" aria-label=\"Link to Fast text search\">#\u003c/a>\u003c/h2>\u003cp>Native cy_resources_grep scans registered text snapshots incrementally, with literal matching,\noptional ASCII ignore-case, line numbers, byte offsets and readUri links. It returns at most 50\nmatching lines per page. Continue with the same text/ignore_case and nextCursor. Binary resources\nand resources denied by policy are excluded. This does not traverse the filesystem.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>For workspace files, \u003ccode>CyMCP::Platform\u003c/code> offers an optional \u003cstrong>ripgrep\u003c/strong> adapter:\u003c/p>\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block\">\u003cdiv class=\"code-toolbar\">\u003cspan>cpp\u003c/span>\u003cbutton type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy\u003c/button>\u003c/div>\u003cpre>\u003ccode class=\"language-cpp\">\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-2-L1\" data-line=\"1\">\u003cspan class=\"token macro property\">\u003cspan class=\"token directive-hash\">#\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token directive keyword\">include\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token string\">&lt;cymcp/search.hpp>\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-2-L2\" data-line=\"2\"> \u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-2-L3\" data-line=\"3\">cymcp\u003cspan class=\"token double-colon punctuation\">::\u003c/span>FileSearchOptions search_options\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-2-L4\" data-line=\"4\">search_options\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">.\u003c/span>root \u003cspan class=\"token operator\">=\u003c/span> host_selected_folder\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token comment\">// Explicit host/user choice.\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-2-L5\" data-line=\"5\">\u003cspan class=\"token comment\">// search_options.ripgrep = trusted_rg_executable; // Otherwise resolves rg from PATH.\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-2-L6\" data-line=\"6\">cymcp\u003cspan class=\"token double-colon punctuation\">::\u003c/span>FileSearch \u003cspan class=\"token function\">search\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">(\u003c/span>search_options\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">)\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-2-L7\" data-line=\"7\">search\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">.\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token function\">add_to\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">(\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">*\u003c/span>commands\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">)\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token comment\">// workspace.grep and workspace.read; also discoverable through gateway.\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003c/code>\u003c/pre>\u003c/div>\u003cp>The host supplies a trusted ripgrep executable separately; the SDK neither bundles nor downloads it.\nRegex uses its default Rust engine. Arguments are passed directly without a shell or rg config.\n\u003ccode>workspace.grep\u003c/code> accepts pattern, regex (default true), ignore_case, glob and include_ignored\n(default false). Hidden files are included; Git metadata and symlinks are excluded. Default ignore\nrules remain active unless include_ignored is enabled or an explicit file glob overrides them.\nThis root scope is not an OS sandbox\nagainst another process changing the filesystem concurrently; use host isolation for untrusted trees.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>Pages contain up to 100 matching lines by default, path/line/byteOffset and bounded UTF-8 excerpts.\n\u003ccode>truncated\u003c/code> and lineBytes identify longer lines; workspace.read retrieves the full text in ranges.\nContinue a search with \u003cstrong>cursor only\u003c/strong>; each returned cursor replaces the previous one. Search\nprocesses are owned, cancellable, limited to eight concurrent searches and expire after 60 idle\nseconds. Non-UTF-8 matches skipped by this text adapter are counted in skippedNonUtf8.\nProcess/line limits fail explicitly instead of silently discarding results.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>\u003ccode>workspace.read\u003c/code> accepts a relative path, offset, length (1–65536 bytes) and optional revision.\nFollow nextOffset with the same revision to detect file changes. Reads preserve UTF-8 boundaries;\nbinary/non-UTF-8 content is rejected. No writes or directories outside the chosen root are exposed.\nThe registry&#39;s host policy still decides whether either command may be invoked.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"example\">Try in Chat Lab\u003ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#/en/optimization/example\" aria-label=\"Link to Try in Chat Lab\">#\u003c/a>\u003c/h2>\u003cp>The default two counter commands stay unchanged. In a private JSON configuration supplied with\n\u003ccode>--config\u003c/code>, enable compact exposure and optionally choose a read-only workspace:\u003c/p>\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block\">\u003cdiv class=\"code-toolbar\">\u003cspan>json\u003c/span>\u003cbutton type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy\u003c/button>\u003c/div>\u003cpre>\u003ccode class=\"language-json\">\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-3-L1\" data-line=\"1\">\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">{\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-3-L2\" data-line=\"2\">  \u003cspan class=\"token property\">\"app_commands\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">:\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">{\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-3-L3\" data-line=\"3\">    \u003cspan class=\"token property\">\"deferred_tools\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">:\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token boolean\">true\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-3-L4\" data-line=\"4\">    \u003cspan class=\"token property\">\"workspace\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">:\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">{\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token property\">\"root\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">:\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token string\">\"./sample-workspace\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">}\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-3-L5\" data-line=\"5\">  \u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">}\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-3-L6\" data-line=\"6\">\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">}\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003c/code>\u003c/pre>\u003c/div>\u003cp>Choose an existing folder. Optional workspace.ripgrep specifies its trusted executable. A workspace\nis never configured automatically. Compact exposure applies to MCP and direct supported AI tools;\nthe JSON SDK endpoint retains original command names. Both paths share the same registry/policy.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"references\">Protocol references\u003ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#/en/optimization/references\" aria-label=\"Link to Protocol references\">#\u003c/a>\u003c/h2>\u003cp>The implementation follows MCP \u003ca href=\"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/server/tools\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">tools\u003c/a>,\n\u003ca href=\"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/server/resources\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">resources\u003c/a>,\n\u003ca href=\"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/server/utilities/caching\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">caching\u003c/a> and\n\u003ca href=\"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/server/utilities/pagination\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">pagination\u003c/a>.\nChunk manifests and targeted lookup are optional CyMCPSDK conventions, not mandatory MCP methods.\u003c/p>\n","text":"Discover without losing capabilities # Optional disk storage, performance logs, change subscriptions and API context windows extend these facilities without changing their default behavior. Registry remains the source of truth. Direct SDK calls and ordinary MCP tools preserve their names, arguments, output schemas and policies. describe() still returns the complete catalogue. Immutable catalogue() and schema-free summaries() snapshots are reused until add , replace or remove changes the registry; describe(name) loads one full definition. ToolGateway exposes five standard callable tools instead of every definition: Tool Purpose cy_tools_search Search names/descriptions; omit query to browse every command. Follow nextCursor with the same query. cy_tools_describe Retrieve one complete input/output schema. cy_tools_call Invoke the original command with its arguments and the caller's context. cy_resources_read Read an application resource, manifest or chunk. cy_resources_grep Search registered text resources without loading their entire contents. Search and describe never execute app commands. Invocation still validates the original schemas and applies the original policy, including explicit allow-all. No command is permanently hidden. Search cursors become invalid after registry changes; restart discovery explicitly. cpp Copy # include \u003ccymcp/mcp.hpp> # include \u003ccymcp/resources.hpp> auto commands = std :: make_shared \u003c cymcp :: Registry > ( host_policy ) ; // Register all application operations on commands. cymcp :: ToolGateway gateway ( commands ) ; cymcp :: McpServerOptions options ; options . resources = gateway . resources ( ) ; cymcp :: McpServer server ( * gateway . tools ( ) , \"My application\" , options ) ; // Keep gateway/commands alive while serving. For an API: config.tools = gateway.tools(). API transports and Codex automatically choose this mode when constructed with more than 32 tools. settings.tool_discovery_threshold changes the threshold; settings.deferred_tools=false keeps full definitions. Typed options expose tool_discovery_threshold ( size_t maximum disables it). An explicitly created gateway works with any tool-capable transport. Other native agents retain their native MCP configuration; the SDK does not invent unsupported CLI tool injection. Read only the data needed # ResourceRegistry belongs to CyMCP::Core ; it also works without MCP or HTTP. Register a Resource with URI, name, MIME type, byte size and a bounded read callback over an immutable host snapshot . No filesystem or network is implicitly exposed. Resource reads have their own policy ( resources.read , arguments containing the requested URI), cancellation and ownership checks. MCP advertises resources/list , resources/read and an empty template catalogue only when McpServerOptions.resources is supplied. Listing resources does not read their contents. Small contents are returned directly; larger contents return a JSON manifest ( type: cymcp.resource.v1 ) with firstUri , original MIME type, size and chunk size. Read firstUri and follow _meta[\"com.cymcp/chunk\"].nextUri until eof. Text chunks preserve UTF-8; binary chunks use standard base64. Never treat an excerpt as a full result. Gateway results over 16 KiB become private resource handles; MCP also includes a standard resource_link . Read with native resources/read or cy_resources_read. Defaults are 32 KiB per chunk, 64 MiB retained bytes, 128 results and five-minute retention; all are host-configurable. Results are not listed publicly and are bound to CallContext.principal . The host must assign separate principals for callers that must be isolated. Replacing a registered snapshot invalidates its old chunk URIs. Expiry or LRU eviction returns ResourceNotFound; it never reruns a command. A result larger than the retained byte budget remains inline without truncation or re-execution. To keep arbitrarily large datasets bounded, expose them as host-backed snapshot resources or paginated application commands from the start. The gateway cannot remove memory already allocated by a handler returning a large JSON object. Ordinary unwrapped tools keep their original structured output; the gateway does not violate their outputSchema by substituting a handle. Cache and compatibility # MCP tools/list and resources/list have revision-bound cursors (64 entries per page by default). McpClient::list_tools() still aggregates every page; list_tools_page() reads just one. An absent nextCursor ends pagination; empty cursors are accepted from other implementations. get_tool(name) uses advertised cymcp/tools/get when supported and falls back to full discovery for older peers. The extension is optional; the five gateway tools use ordinary MCP tool calls. Client caches are private per instance and keyed by method plus all parameters. Only discovery, schema lookup and resource reads with positive server ttlMs are cached. Defaults: 256 entries, 16 MiB serialized data and a maximum 30-second TTL. Zero TTL or zero local limits disables caching. Tools/call and errors are never cached. No background polling occurs. Changes may remain cached until TTL: use clear_cache() for an immediate refresh after known external changes. Reconnect, close and received catalogue/resource change notifications invalidate the cache. A tool error also clears it, without retrying the operation. cache_stats() reports hits, misses and retained bytes. Fast text search # Native cy_resources_grep scans registered text snapshots incrementally, with literal matching, optional ASCII ignore-case, line numbers, byte offsets and readUri links. It returns at most 50 matching lines per page. Continue with the same text/ignore_case and nextCursor. Binary resources and resources denied by policy are excluded. This does not traverse the filesystem. For workspace files, CyMCP::Platform offers an optional ripgrep adapter: cpp Copy # include \u003ccymcp/search.hpp> cymcp :: FileSearchOptions search_options ; search_options . root = host_selected_folder ; // Explicit host/user choice. // search_options.ripgrep = trusted_rg_executable; // Otherwise resolves rg from PATH. cymcp :: FileSearch search ( search_options ) ; search . add_to ( * commands ) ; // workspace.grep and workspace.read; also discoverable through gateway. The host supplies a trusted ripgrep executable separately; the SDK neither bundles nor downloads it. Regex uses its default Rust engine. Arguments are passed directly without a shell or rg config. workspace.grep accepts pattern, regex (default true), ignore_case, glob and include_ignored (default false). Hidden files are included; Git metadata and symlinks are excluded. Default ignore rules remain active unless include_ignored is enabled or an explicit file glob overrides them. This root scope is not an OS sandbox against another process changing the filesystem concurrently; use host isolation for untrusted trees. Pages contain up to 100 matching lines by default, path/line/byteOffset and bounded UTF-8 excerpts. truncated and lineBytes identify longer lines; workspace.read retrieves the full text in ranges. Continue a search with cursor only ; each returned cursor replaces the previous one. Search processes are owned, cancellable, limited to eight concurrent searches and expire after 60 idle seconds. Non-UTF-8 matches skipped by this text adapter are counted in skippedNonUtf8. Process/line limits fail explicitly instead of silently discarding results. workspace.read accepts a relative path, offset, length (1–65536 bytes) and optional revision. Follow nextOffset with the same revision to detect file changes. Reads preserve UTF-8 boundaries; binary/non-UTF-8 content is rejected. No writes or directories outside the chosen root are exposed. The registry's host policy still decides whether either command may be invoked. Try in Chat Lab # The default two counter commands stay unchanged. In a private JSON configuration supplied with --config , enable compact exposure and optionally choose a read-only workspace: json Copy { \"app_commands\" : { \"deferred_tools\" : true , \"workspace\" : { \"root\" : \"./sample-workspace\" } } } Choose an existing folder. Optional workspace.ripgrep specifies its trusted executable. A workspace is never configured automatically. Compact exposure applies to MCP and direct supported AI tools; the JSON SDK endpoint retains original command names. Both paths share the same registry/policy. Protocol references # The implementation follows MCP tools , resources , caching and pagination . Chunk manifests and targeted lookup are optional CyMCPSDK conventions, not mandatory MCP methods. #include \u003ccymcp/mcp.hpp> #include \u003ccymcp/resources.hpp> auto commands = std::make_shared\u003ccymcp::Registry>(host_policy); // Register all application operations on commands. cymcp::ToolGateway gateway(commands); cymcp::McpServerOptions options; options.resources = gateway.resources(); cymcp::McpServer server(*gateway.tools(), \"My application\", options); // Keep gateway/commands alive while serving. For an API: config.tools = gateway.tools(). #include \u003ccymcp/search.hpp> cymcp::FileSearchOptions search_options; search_options.root = host_selected_folder; // Explicit host/user choice. // search_options.ripgrep = trusted_rg_executable; // Otherwise resolves rg from PATH. cymcp::FileSearch search(search_options); search.add_to(*commands); // workspace.grep and workspace.read; also discoverable through gateway. { \"app_commands\": { \"deferred_tools\": true, \"workspace\": {\"root\": \"./sample-workspace\"} } }","headings":[{"id":"tools","text":"Discover without losing capabilities","level":2},{"id":"resources","text":"Read only the data needed","level":2},{"id":"cache","text":"Cache and compatibility","level":2},{"id":"grep","text":"Fast text search","level":2},{"id":"example","text":"Try in Chat Lab","level":2},{"id":"references","text":"Protocol references","level":2}],"anchors":["L1","L2","L3","L4","L5","L6","L7","L8","L9","L10","code-2-L1","code-2-L2","code-2-L3","code-2-L4","code-2-L5","code-2-L6","code-2-L7","code-3-L1","code-3-L2","code-3-L3","code-3-L4","code-3-L5","code-3-L6"],"languages":["cpp","json"],"code":"#include \u003ccymcp/mcp.hpp>\n#include \u003ccymcp/resources.hpp>\n\nauto commands = std::make_shared\u003ccymcp::Registry>(host_policy);\n// Register all application operations on commands.\ncymcp::ToolGateway gateway(commands);\ncymcp::McpServerOptions options;\noptions.resources = gateway.resources();\ncymcp::McpServer server(*gateway.tools(), \"My application\", options);\n// Keep gateway/commands alive while serving. For an API: config.tools = gateway.tools().\n#include \u003ccymcp/search.hpp>\n\ncymcp::FileSearchOptions search_options;\nsearch_options.root = host_selected_folder; // Explicit host/user choice.\n// search_options.ripgrep = trusted_rg_executable; // Otherwise resolves rg from PATH.\ncymcp::FileSearch search(search_options);\nsearch.add_to(*commands); // workspace.grep and workspace.read; also discoverable through gateway.\n{\n  \"app_commands\": {\n    \"deferred_tools\": true,\n    \"workspace\": {\"root\": \"./sample-workspace\"}\n  }\n}","assets":[],"links":["#/en/runtime-options","https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/server/tools","https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/server/resources","https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/server/utilities/caching","https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/server/utilities/pagination"],"kind":"guide"},{"id":"overview","title":"CyMCPSDK","description":"Add AI conversations and application tools to a native C++ application.","section":"Guides","order":0,"revision":"3","locale":"en","html":"\u003ch2 id=\"workflows\">Choose your workflow\u003ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#/en/overview/workflows\" aria-label=\"Link to Choose your workflow\">#\u003c/a>\u003c/h2>\u003cp>CyMCPSDK is an MIT C++20 library for application developers. Register application\noperations once, expose them through a direct SDK or MCP, and connect the application\nto CLI agents, APIs or a local model service. The optional CyUI panel displays conversations.\u003c/p>\n\u003ctable>\n\u003cthead>\n\u003ctr>\n\u003cth>Your task\u003c/th>\n\u003cth>Start here\u003c/th>\n\u003c/tr>\n\u003c/thead>\n\u003ctbody>\u003ctr>\n\u003ctd>Try the Windows application\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>\u003ca href=\"#/en/quickstart\">Quickstart\u003c/a>\u003c/td>\n\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\n\u003ctd>Configure a chat and use its tools\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>\u003ca href=\"#/en/chat-lab\">Chat Lab\u003c/a>\u003c/td>\n\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\n\u003ctd>Add the library to your application\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>\u003ca href=\"#/en/integration\">C++ integration\u003c/a>\u003c/td>\n\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\n\u003ctd>Let an AI or another app call your operations\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>\u003ca href=\"#/en/operations\">Application operations\u003c/a>\u003c/td>\n\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\n\u003ctd>Discover tools on demand, read chunks and search text\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>\u003ca href=\"#/en/optimization\">Optimization and grep\u003c/a>\u003c/td>\n\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\n\u003ctd>Choose access rules\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>\u003ca href=\"#/en/permissions\">Permissions\u003c/a>\u003c/td>\n\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\n\u003ctd>Use an installed local engine\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>\u003ca href=\"#/en/local-engines\">Local engines\u003c/a>\u003c/td>\n\u003c/tr>\n\u003c/tbody>\u003c/table>\n\u003ch2 id=\"modules\">Modules\u003ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#/en/overview/modules\" aria-label=\"Link to Modules\">#\u003c/a>\u003c/h2>\u003ctable>\n\u003cthead>\n\u003ctr>\n\u003cth>CMake target\u003c/th>\n\u003cth>Role\u003c/th>\n\u003c/tr>\n\u003c/thead>\n\u003ctbody>\u003ctr>\n\u003ctd>\u003ccode>CyMCP::Core\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>Operation registry, schemas, policies, cancellation and bounded workers\u003c/td>\n\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\n\u003ctd>\u003ccode>CyMCP::Platform\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>Native child processes and structured arguments\u003c/td>\n\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\n\u003ctd>\u003ccode>CyMCP::Http\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>HTTP(S) client, streaming and authenticated loopback server\u003c/td>\n\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\n\u003ctd>\u003ccode>CyMCP::MCP\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>MCP tool server/client over stdio or local HTTP JSON\u003c/td>\n\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\n\u003ctd>\u003ccode>CyMCP::AI\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>Provider profiles, sessions, conversations and tool exchanges\u003c/td>\n\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\n\u003ctd>\u003ccode>CyMCP::Local\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>Engine supervision and verified dependency downloads\u003c/td>\n\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\n\u003ctd>\u003ccode>CyMCP::ChatUI\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>Optional CyUI controller and Markdown chat panel\u003c/td>\n\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\n\u003ctd>\u003ccode>CyMCP::SDK\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>SDK modules without the graphical dependency\u003c/td>\n\u003c/tr>\n\u003c/tbody>\u003c/table>\n\u003ch2 id=\"scope\">Scope\u003ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#/en/overview/scope\" aria-label=\"Link to Scope\">#\u003c/a>\u003c/h2>\u003cp>The library does not bundle a model, AI CLI, inference engine, CUDA runtime or driver.\nInstall and configure the provider you choose. Native accounts and service terms still apply.\nSee \u003ca href=\"#/en/providers\">provider choices\u003c/a> and \u003ca href=\"#/en/licenses\">licenses\u003c/a>.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>The Windows example uses Win32/DX11. ChatUI uses the host application&#39;s CyUI/ImGui backend.\nLinux/macOS distribution work is still in progress; Android is deferred.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"navigation\">Read this manual\u003ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#/en/overview/navigation\" aria-label=\"Link to Read this manual\">#\u003c/a>\u003c/h2>\u003cp>Use the page tree or search field; \u003cstrong>Ctrl+K\u003c/strong> opens search. Switch between English and\nFrench in the reader. The complete \u003ccode>Documentation\u003c/code> folder opens directly from disk.\nIn Chat Lab, \u003cstrong>F1\u003c/strong> opens Help. Choose \u003cstrong>Open full manual\u003c/strong> for the offline guide in the selected language.\u003c/p>\n","text":"Choose your workflow # CyMCPSDK is an MIT C++20 library for application developers. Register application operations once, expose them through a direct SDK or MCP, and connect the application to CLI agents, APIs or a local model service. The optional CyUI panel displays conversations. Your task Start here Try the Windows application Quickstart Configure a chat and use its tools Chat Lab Add the library to your application C++ integration Let an AI or another app call your operations Application operations Discover tools on demand, read chunks and search text Optimization and grep Choose access rules Permissions Use an installed local engine Local engines Modules # CMake target Role CyMCP::Core Operation registry, schemas, policies, cancellation and bounded workers CyMCP::Platform Native child processes and structured arguments CyMCP::Http HTTP(S) client, streaming and authenticated loopback server CyMCP::MCP MCP tool server/client over stdio or local HTTP JSON CyMCP::AI Provider profiles, sessions, conversations and tool exchanges CyMCP::Local Engine supervision and verified dependency downloads CyMCP::ChatUI Optional CyUI controller and Markdown chat panel CyMCP::SDK SDK modules without the graphical dependency Scope # The library does not bundle a model, AI CLI, inference engine, CUDA runtime or driver. Install and configure the provider you choose. Native accounts and service terms still apply. See provider choices and licenses . The Windows example uses Win32/DX11. ChatUI uses the host application's CyUI/ImGui backend. Linux/macOS distribution work is still in progress; Android is deferred. Read this manual # Use the page tree or search field; Ctrl+K opens search. Switch between English and French in the reader. The complete Documentation folder opens directly from disk. In Chat Lab, F1 opens Help. Choose Open full manual for the offline guide in the selected language.","headings":[{"id":"workflows","text":"Choose your workflow","level":2},{"id":"modules","text":"Modules","level":2},{"id":"scope","text":"Scope","level":2},{"id":"navigation","text":"Read this manual","level":2}],"anchors":[],"languages":[],"code":"","assets":[],"links":["#/en/quickstart","#/en/chat-lab","#/en/integration","#/en/operations","#/en/optimization","#/en/permissions","#/en/local-engines","#/en/providers","#/en/licenses"],"kind":"guide"},{"id":"permissions","title":"Configure permissions","description":"Choose host operation policies and native agent approval behavior independently.","section":"SDK","parent":"integration","order":2,"revision":"1","locale":"en","html":"\u003ch2 id=\"policy\">Choose the host policy\u003ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#/en/permissions/policy\" aria-label=\"Link to Choose the host policy\">#\u003c/a>\u003c/h2>\u003cp>A default \u003ccode>Policy\u003c/code> denies operations. Use a callback to decide from the call context,\noperation name and arguments, or explicitly use \u003ccode>Policy::allow_all()\u003c/code> when the host wants\nunrestricted access to its registered domain. The SDK does not require confirmation dialogs.\u003c/p>\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block\">\u003cdiv class=\"code-toolbar\">\u003cspan>cpp\u003c/span>\u003cbutton type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy\u003c/button>\u003c/div>\u003cpre>\u003ccode class=\"language-cpp\">\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L1\" data-line=\"1\">cymcp\u003cspan class=\"token double-colon punctuation\">::\u003c/span>Policy \u003cspan class=\"token function\">reads_only\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">(\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">[\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">]\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">(\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token keyword\">const\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token keyword\">auto\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">&amp;\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token keyword\">const\u003c/span> std\u003cspan class=\"token double-colon punctuation\">::\u003c/span>string\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">&amp;\u003c/span> name\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token keyword\">const\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token keyword\">auto\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">&amp;\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">)\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">{\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L2\" data-line=\"2\">    \u003cspan class=\"token keyword\">return\u003c/span> name \u003cspan class=\"token operator\">==\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token string\">\"get_counter\"\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token operator\">?\u003c/span> cymcp\u003cspan class=\"token double-colon punctuation\">::\u003c/span>Decision\u003cspan class=\"token double-colon punctuation\">::\u003c/span>allow \u003cspan class=\"token operator\">:\u003c/span> cymcp\u003cspan class=\"token double-colon punctuation\">::\u003c/span>Decision\u003cspan class=\"token double-colon punctuation\">::\u003c/span>deny\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L3\" data-line=\"3\">\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">}\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">)\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003c/code>\u003c/pre>\u003c/div>\u003cp>Permission to call one operation does not create new application capabilities. Keep operation\nhandlers and schemas as narrow as the application needs. Domain validation still applies in an\nallow-all policy. Cancellation and resource budgets are separate from permission decisions.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"agents\">Agent approval and app operations\u003ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#/en/permissions/agents\" aria-label=\"Link to Agent approval and app operations\">#\u003c/a>\u003c/h2>\u003cp>Native agent permissions are separate from the operation registry. In Chat Lab,\n\u003cstrong>Allow all actions\u003c/strong> requests the provider&#39;s unrestricted mode; \u003cstrong>Allow counter changes\u003c/strong>\ncontrols the example operation registry. An enabled switch cannot remove restrictions imposed\nby an external provider or operating system.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>ACP filesystem and terminal client services are not announced by default. An embedding host\nmust declare \u003ccode>settings.client_capabilities\u003c/code>, provide \u003ccode>request_handler\u003c/code> and choose its approval\npolicy. The host implements the file/terminal behavior and cleanup; a capability flag alone\ndoes not create a terminal service.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"network\">Authenticate a local server\u003ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#/en/permissions/network\" aria-label=\"Link to Authenticate a local server\">#\u003c/a>\u003c/h2>\u003cp>The loopback HTTP server requires a token of at least 32 characters and rejects requests carrying\n\u003ccode>Origin\u003c/code>. Pass the token in \u003ccode>Authorization: Bearer ...\u003c/code>. Chat Lab generates a new random token\nwhen its server starts; it displays only the endpoint and offers an explicit token-copy action.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>Authentication identifies an allowed client; it does not replace operation authorization.\nKeep the local server&#39;s lifetime, token distribution and domain policy under the host&#39;s control.\u003c/p>\n","text":"Choose the host policy # A default Policy denies operations. Use a callback to decide from the call context, operation name and arguments, or explicitly use Policy::allow_all() when the host wants unrestricted access to its registered domain. The SDK does not require confirmation dialogs. cpp Copy cymcp :: Policy reads_only ( [ ] ( const auto & , const std :: string & name , const auto & ) { return name == \"get_counter\" ? cymcp :: Decision :: allow : cymcp :: Decision :: deny ; } ) ; Permission to call one operation does not create new application capabilities. Keep operation handlers and schemas as narrow as the application needs. Domain validation still applies in an allow-all policy. Cancellation and resource budgets are separate from permission decisions. Agent approval and app operations # Native agent permissions are separate from the operation registry. In Chat Lab, Allow all actions requests the provider's unrestricted mode; Allow counter changes controls the example operation registry. An enabled switch cannot remove restrictions imposed by an external provider or operating system. ACP filesystem and terminal client services are not announced by default. An embedding host must declare settings.client_capabilities , provide request_handler and choose its approval policy. The host implements the file/terminal behavior and cleanup; a capability flag alone does not create a terminal service. Authenticate a local server # The loopback HTTP server requires a token of at least 32 characters and rejects requests carrying Origin . Pass the token in Authorization: Bearer ... . Chat Lab generates a new random token when its server starts; it displays only the endpoint and offers an explicit token-copy action. Authentication identifies an allowed client; it does not replace operation authorization. Keep the local server's lifetime, token distribution and domain policy under the host's control. cymcp::Policy reads_only([](const auto&, const std::string& name, const auto&) { return name == \"get_counter\" ? cymcp::Decision::allow : cymcp::Decision::deny; });","headings":[{"id":"policy","text":"Choose the host policy","level":2},{"id":"agents","text":"Agent approval and app operations","level":2},{"id":"network","text":"Authenticate a local server","level":2}],"anchors":["L1","L2","L3"],"languages":["cpp"],"code":"cymcp::Policy reads_only([](const auto&, const std::string& name, const auto&) {\n    return name == \"get_counter\" ? cymcp::Decision::allow : cymcp::Decision::deny;\n});","assets":[],"links":[],"kind":"guide"},{"id":"providers","title":"Choose a provider","description":"Select a CLI, native API or local endpoint and supply its real model and credentials.","section":"Guides","parent":"chat-lab","order":1,"revision":"5","locale":"en","html":"\u003ch2 id=\"profiles\">Built-in profiles\u003ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#/en/providers/profiles\" aria-label=\"Link to Built-in profiles\">#\u003c/a>\u003c/h2>\u003ctable>\n\u003cthead>\n\u003ctr>\n\u003cth>Type\u003c/th>\n\u003cth>Registry IDs\u003c/th>\n\u003c/tr>\n\u003c/thead>\n\u003ctbody>\u003ctr>\n\u003ctd>Native agents\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>\u003ccode>codex\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>codex-exec\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>claude-code\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>antigravity\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>command-code\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>codebuddy\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\n\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\n\u003ctd>ACP v1 agents\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>\u003ccode>opencode\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>gemini\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>qwen-code\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>kimi\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>goose\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>devin\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>command-code-acp\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>codebuddy-acp\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>acp\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\n\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\n\u003ctd>Historical OpenCode 1.x\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>\u003ccode>opencode-cli\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\n\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\n\u003ctd>Native APIs\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>\u003ccode>openai\u003c/code> (Responses), \u003ccode>anthropic\u003c/code> (Messages), \u003ccode>openrouter\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>ollama\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\n\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\n\u003ctd>Compatible HTTP servers\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>\u003ccode>openai-compatible\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>llama.cpp\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>lmstudio\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\n\u003c/tr>\n\u003c/tbody>\u003c/table>\n\u003cp>Use \u003ccode>codex\u003c/code> for persistent App Server sessions and host tools. Select \u003ccode>codex-exec\u003c/code> for the\nper-turn CLI transport that reads text from stdin and resumes a saved thread by ID.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>These 23 profiles describe transports and launch recipes. The installed version, server and model\ndetermine actual capabilities. ACP v1 negotiates session loading, models, modes and prompt content.\n\u003ccode>opencode-cli\u003c/code> is the older JSONL transport; current OpenCode uses \u003ccode>opencode\u003c/code> with ACP.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"configure\">Configure a connection\u003ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#/en/providers/configure\" aria-label=\"Link to Configure a connection\">#\u003c/a>\u003c/h2>\u003cp>Use \u003cstrong>Automatic connection\u003c/strong> first: installed CLIs and supported npm packages are resolved\nwithout entering paths or arguments. Native CLIs reuse their existing environment and account.\nDetection covers every named CLI profile above; the generic \u003ccode>acp\u003c/code> profile requires a host recipe.\nAn installation is not proof of successful authentication or generation.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>For an unusual installation, edit the selected provider in the \u003cstrong>Providers\u003c/strong> tab. A host application can add executable\ndirectories, private npm roots and discovery recipes for its own providers. Provider-specific\narguments are structured strings; the SDK never runs them through a shell.\n\u003ccode>process.environment\u003c/code> passes child-only environment values.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>Cloud discovery recognizes \u003ccode>OPENAI_API_KEY\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>ANTHROPIC_API_KEY\u003c/code> and \u003ccode>OPENROUTER_API_KEY\u003c/code>.\nEndpoint overrides use \u003ccode>OPENAI_BASE_URL\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>OPENROUTER_BASE_URL\u003c/code> or\n\u003ccode>OLLAMA_HOST\u003c/code>. Running local servers are queried for their models; a stopped service or an\nempty model catalogue is shown explicitly. Private configuration files are not searched for secrets.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>API credentials come from a named environment variable or Chat Lab&#39;s masked memory field.\nFor example, the CLI and GUI can load this non-secret configuration with \u003ccode>--config\u003c/code>:\u003c/p>\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block\">\u003cdiv class=\"code-toolbar\">\u003cspan>json\u003c/span>\u003cbutton type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy\u003c/button>\u003c/div>\u003cpre>\u003ccode class=\"language-json\">\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L1\" data-line=\"1\">\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">{\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L2\" data-line=\"2\">  \u003cspan class=\"token property\">\"provider\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">:\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token string\">\"openai\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L3\" data-line=\"3\">  \u003cspan class=\"token property\">\"model\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">:\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token string\">\"\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L4\" data-line=\"4\">  \u003cspan class=\"token property\">\"api_key_env\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">:\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token string\">\"OPENAI_API_KEY\"\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L5\" data-line=\"5\">\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">}\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003c/code>\u003c/pre>\u003c/div>\u003cp>In automatic mode, choose a returned model in the dropdown or keep the provider default.\nOnly local services get a model automatically; a remote API shows its catalogue and waits for\nan explicit choice. In manual mode, selecting a provider pre-fills its conventional settings\n(endpoint, key variable, timeouts) and the detected installation.\nManual mode also accepts an exact model ID. Do not put a real key in a JSON file.\nUse \u003ccode>settings.base_url\u003c/code> for an endpoint override. The Ollama profile expects its native\nAPI base, whereas compatible servers commonly use a base ending in \u003ccode>/v1\u003c/code>.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"models\">Discover models and capabilities\u003ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#/en/providers/models\" aria-label=\"Link to Discover models and capabilities\">#\u003c/a>\u003c/h2>\u003cp>The headless example exposes:\u003c/p>\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block\">\u003cdiv class=\"code-toolbar\">\u003cspan>sh\u003c/span>\u003cbutton type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy\u003c/button>\u003c/div>\u003cpre>\u003ccode class=\"language-bash\">\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-2-L1\" data-line=\"1\">cymcp_chat providers\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-2-L2\" data-line=\"2\">cymcp_chat discover\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-2-L3\" data-line=\"3\">cymcp_chat models examples/chat-ollama.json\u003c/span>\u003c/code>\u003c/pre>\u003c/div>\u003cp>\u003ccode>providers\u003c/code> lists configured transport capabilities; \u003ccode>models\u003c/code> contacts the selected provider.\nAn unsupported catalogue is not proof that chat is unavailable: use an exact model ID from the\nnative provider. A chosen model applies to a new connection. The SDK does not silently switch\nmodels or replay failed generations.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"extension\">Add a provider\u003ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#/en/providers/extension\" aria-label=\"Link to Add a provider\">#\u003c/a>\u003c/h2>\u003cp>Implement the public \u003ccode>Provider\u003c/code> interface and register a \u003ccode>ProviderDescriptor\u003c/code> plus factory with\n\u003ccode>ProviderRegistry::add\u003c/code>. Keep \u003ccode>connect\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>start_session\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>send\u003c/code> and \u003ccode>disconnect\u003c/code> consistent with\nthe advertised capabilities. \u003ccode>ProviderConfig\u003c/code> supplies arguments, settings, credentials,\nan optional operation registry and permission callbacks. See \u003ca href=\"#/en/integration/providers\">integration\u003c/a>.\u003c/p>\n","text":"Built-in profiles # Type Registry IDs Native agents codex , codex-exec , claude-code , antigravity , command-code , codebuddy ACP v1 agents opencode , gemini , qwen-code , kimi , goose , devin , command-code-acp , codebuddy-acp , acp Historical OpenCode 1.x opencode-cli Native APIs openai (Responses), anthropic (Messages), openrouter , ollama Compatible HTTP servers openai-compatible , llama.cpp , lmstudio Use codex for persistent App Server sessions and host tools. Select codex-exec for the per-turn CLI transport that reads text from stdin and resumes a saved thread by ID. These 23 profiles describe transports and launch recipes. The installed version, server and model determine actual capabilities. ACP v1 negotiates session loading, models, modes and prompt content. opencode-cli is the older JSONL transport; current OpenCode uses opencode with ACP. Configure a connection # Use Automatic connection first: installed CLIs and supported npm packages are resolved without entering paths or arguments. Native CLIs reuse their existing environment and account. Detection covers every named CLI profile above; the generic acp profile requires a host recipe. An installation is not proof of successful authentication or generation. For an unusual installation, edit the selected provider in the Providers tab. A host application can add executable directories, private npm roots and discovery recipes for its own providers. Provider-specific arguments are structured strings; the SDK never runs them through a shell. process.environment passes child-only environment values. Cloud discovery recognizes OPENAI_API_KEY , ANTHROPIC_API_KEY and OPENROUTER_API_KEY . Endpoint overrides use OPENAI_BASE_URL , ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL , OPENROUTER_BASE_URL or OLLAMA_HOST . Running local servers are queried for their models; a stopped service or an empty model catalogue is shown explicitly. Private configuration files are not searched for secrets. API credentials come from a named environment variable or Chat Lab's masked memory field. For example, the CLI and GUI can load this non-secret configuration with --config : json Copy { \"provider\" : \"openai\" , \"model\" : \"\" , \"api_key_env\" : \"OPENAI_API_KEY\" } In automatic mode, choose a returned model in the dropdown or keep the provider default. Only local services get a model automatically; a remote API shows its catalogue and waits for an explicit choice. In manual mode, selecting a provider pre-fills its conventional settings (endpoint, key variable, timeouts) and the detected installation. Manual mode also accepts an exact model ID. Do not put a real key in a JSON file. Use settings.base_url for an endpoint override. The Ollama profile expects its native API base, whereas compatible servers commonly use a base ending in /v1 . Discover models and capabilities # The headless example exposes: sh Copy cymcp_chat providers cymcp_chat discover cymcp_chat models examples/chat-ollama.json providers lists configured transport capabilities; models contacts the selected provider. An unsupported catalogue is not proof that chat is unavailable: use an exact model ID from the native provider. A chosen model applies to a new connection. The SDK does not silently switch models or replay failed generations. Add a provider # Implement the public Provider interface and register a ProviderDescriptor plus factory with ProviderRegistry::add . Keep connect , start_session , send and disconnect consistent with the advertised capabilities. ProviderConfig supplies arguments, settings, credentials, an optional operation registry and permission callbacks. See integration . { \"provider\": \"openai\", \"model\": \"\", \"api_key_env\": \"OPENAI_API_KEY\" } cymcp_chat providers cymcp_chat discover cymcp_chat models examples/chat-ollama.json","headings":[{"id":"profiles","text":"Built-in profiles","level":2},{"id":"configure","text":"Configure a connection","level":2},{"id":"models","text":"Discover models and capabilities","level":2},{"id":"extension","text":"Add a provider","level":2}],"anchors":["L1","L2","L3","L4","L5","code-2-L1","code-2-L2","code-2-L3"],"languages":["json","bash"],"code":"{\n  \"provider\": \"openai\",\n  \"model\": \"\",\n  \"api_key_env\": \"OPENAI_API_KEY\"\n}\ncymcp_chat providers\ncymcp_chat discover\ncymcp_chat models examples/chat-ollama.json","assets":[],"links":["#/en/integration/providers"],"kind":"guide"},{"id":"quickstart","title":"Start Chat Lab","description":"Build and open the Windows example, then try its local Markdown demonstration.","section":"Guides","parent":"overview","order":1,"revision":"4","locale":"en","html":"\u003ch2 id=\"build\">Build the example\u003ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#/en/quickstart/build\" aria-label=\"Link to Build the example\">#\u003c/a>\u003c/h2>\u003cp>Use Windows 10/11 x64 with Visual Studio 2022&#39;s \u003cstrong>Desktop development with C++\u003c/strong> workload,\nWindows SDK and CMake tools. Obtain a compatible \u003ca href=\"https://github.com/MrMybal/CyUI\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">CyUI checkout\u003c/a>\nbeside the SDK, or pass its actual location to the script.\u003c/p>\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block\">\u003cdiv class=\"code-toolbar\">\u003cspan>powershell\u003c/span>\u003cbutton type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy\u003c/button>\u003c/div>\u003cpre>\u003ccode class=\"language-powershell\">\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L1\" data-line=\"1\">./tools/build-chat.ps1 -CyUISource ../CyUI\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L2\" data-line=\"2\">./out/ChatLab-windows-x64/cymcp_chat_app.exe\u003c/span>\u003c/code>\u003c/pre>\u003c/div>\u003cp>The script compiles and assembles \u003ccode>out/ChatLab-windows-x64\u003c/code>. Keep its executable,\n\u003ccode>Documentation\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>licenses\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>LICENSE\u003c/code> and \u003ccode>THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md\u003c/code> together.\nThe Microsoft Visual C++ 2015–2022 x64 runtime is required. DX11 is used, with a WARP fallback.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"demo\">Try without an account\u003ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#/en/quickstart/demo\" aria-label=\"Link to Try without an account\">#\u003c/a>\u003c/h2>\u003col>\n\u003cli>Start the application. \u003cstrong>English\u003c/strong> is the default language.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Open \u003cstrong>Providers\u003c/strong>, select \u003cstrong>Demo / Markdown (no AI)\u003c/strong> and choose \u003cstrong>Connect / New chat\u003c/strong>.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Type a message and choose \u003cstrong>Send\u003c/strong>, or press \u003cstrong>Ctrl+Enter\u003c/strong>.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Read the streamed Markdown, select text or copy a message.\u003c/li>\n\u003c/ol>\n\u003cfigure data-cydoc-module=\"image\" data-cydoc-id=\"chat-overview\" data-config=\"{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;chat-overview&quot;,&quot;src&quot;:&quot;assets/chat-lab-en.png&quot;,&quot;alt&quot;:&quot;Chat Lab in English showing its local Markdown demonstration&quot;,&quot;controls&quot;:&quot;minimal&quot;}\">\u003cimg src=\"assets/chat-lab-en.png\" alt=\"Chat Lab in English showing its local Markdown demonstration\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\">\u003c/figure>\u003cp>The demonstration generates fixed local text; it does not call a model. Choose a\n\u003ca href=\"#/en/providers\">provider\u003c/a> for an actual conversation. \u003cstrong>Shift+Enter\u003c/strong> adds a line in the composer.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"language\">Language and help\u003ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#/en/quickstart/language\" aria-label=\"Link to Language and help\">#\u003c/a>\u003c/h2>\u003cp>In \u003cstrong>Providers → Appearance\u003c/strong>, choose \u003cstrong>English\u003c/strong> or \u003cstrong>Français\u003c/strong>, and a CyUI theme.\nReconnect the demonstration after changing language to produce new text in that language.\nAI responses follow the selected model and your prompt; changing interface language\ndoes not translate existing messages.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>\u003cstrong>Help (F1)\u003c/strong> opens this manual at \u003ca href=\"#/en/chat-lab\">Chat Lab\u003c/a>. It uses the complete local\nmanual folder beside the executable. The reader does not need an HTTP server.\u003c/p>\n","text":"Build the example # Use Windows 10/11 x64 with Visual Studio 2022's Desktop development with C++ workload, Windows SDK and CMake tools. Obtain a compatible CyUI checkout beside the SDK, or pass its actual location to the script. powershell Copy ./tools/build-chat.ps1 -CyUISource ../CyUI ./out/ChatLab-windows-x64/cymcp_chat_app.exe The script compiles and assembles out/ChatLab-windows-x64 . Keep its executable, Documentation , licenses , LICENSE and THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md together. The Microsoft Visual C++ 2015–2022 x64 runtime is required. DX11 is used, with a WARP fallback. Try without an account # Start the application. English is the default language. Open Providers , select Demo / Markdown (no AI) and choose Connect / New chat . Type a message and choose Send , or press Ctrl+Enter . Read the streamed Markdown, select text or copy a message. The demonstration generates fixed local text; it does not call a model. Choose a provider for an actual conversation. Shift+Enter adds a line in the composer. Language and help # In Providers → Appearance , choose English or Français , and a CyUI theme. Reconnect the demonstration after changing language to produce new text in that language. AI responses follow the selected model and your prompt; changing interface language does not translate existing messages. Help (F1) opens this manual at Chat Lab . It uses the complete local manual folder beside the executable. The reader does not need an HTTP server. ./tools/build-chat.ps1 -CyUISource ../CyUI ./out/ChatLab-windows-x64/cymcp_chat_app.exe","headings":[{"id":"build","text":"Build the example","level":2},{"id":"demo","text":"Try without an account","level":2},{"id":"language","text":"Language and help","level":2}],"anchors":["L1","L2"],"languages":["powershell"],"code":"./tools/build-chat.ps1 -CyUISource ../CyUI\n./out/ChatLab-windows-x64/cymcp_chat_app.exe","assets":["assets/chat-lab-en.png"],"links":["https://github.com/MrMybal/CyUI","#/en/providers","#/en/chat-lab"],"kind":"media"},{"id":"runtime-options","title":"Optional runtime optimizations","description":"Configure disk-backed volumes, metadata-only performance logs, change subscriptions and API context windows.","section":"SDK","parent":"optimization","order":0,"revision":"1","locale":"en","html":"\u003ch2 id=\"options\">Independent options\u003ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#/en/runtime-options/options\" aria-label=\"Link to Independent options\">#\u003c/a>\u003c/h2>\u003cp>All four facilities are opt-in. Core supplies resources, disk spooling, change journals and\nperformance monitoring without graphical or AI dependencies. ContextWindow belongs to AI.\nThere are no added external runtime dependencies. No model is downloaded or launched to summarize\nhistory. Unconfigured applications retain full API history, memory-only retained results and TTL caches.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"disk\">Produce large resources incrementally\u003ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#/en/runtime-options/disk\" aria-label=\"Link to Produce large resources incrementally\">#\u003c/a>\u003c/h2>\u003cdiv class=\"code-block\">\u003cdiv class=\"code-toolbar\">\u003cspan>cpp\u003c/span>\u003cbutton type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy\u003c/button>\u003c/div>\u003cpre>\u003ccode class=\"language-cpp\">\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L1\" data-line=\"1\">\u003cspan class=\"token macro property\">\u003cspan class=\"token directive-hash\">#\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token directive keyword\">include\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token string\">&lt;cymcp/resources.hpp>\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L2\" data-line=\"2\"> \u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L3\" data-line=\"3\">cymcp\u003cspan class=\"token double-colon punctuation\">::\u003c/span>ResourceOptions storage\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L4\" data-line=\"4\">storage\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">.\u003c/span>disk_directory \u003cspan class=\"token operator\">=\u003c/span> host_selected_cache_folder\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L5\" data-line=\"5\">storage\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">.\u003c/span>max_stored_bytes \u003cspan class=\"token operator\">=\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token number\">8\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token operator\">*\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token number\">1024\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token operator\">*\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token number\">1024\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L6\" data-line=\"6\">storage\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">.\u003c/span>spool_threshold \u003cspan class=\"token operator\">=\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token number\">1024\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token operator\">*\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token number\">1024\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L7\" data-line=\"7\">storage\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">.\u003c/span>max_disk_bytes \u003cspan class=\"token operator\">=\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token number\">1024ULL\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token operator\">*\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token number\">1024\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token operator\">*\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token number\">1024\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L8\" data-line=\"8\">\u003cspan class=\"token keyword\">auto\u003c/span> resources \u003cspan class=\"token operator\">=\u003c/span> std\u003cspan class=\"token double-colon punctuation\">::\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token generic-function\">\u003cspan class=\"token function\">make_shared\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token generic class-name\">\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">&lt;\u003c/span>cymcp\u003cspan class=\"token double-colon punctuation\">::\u003c/span>ResourceRegistry\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">>\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">(\u003c/span>host_resource_policy\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span> storage\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">)\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L9\" data-line=\"9\">\u003cspan class=\"token keyword\">auto\u003c/span> handle \u003cspan class=\"token operator\">=\u003c/span> resources\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">->\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token function\">store_stream\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">(\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L10\" data-line=\"10\">    \u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">[\u003c/span>snapshot_blocks\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">]\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">(\u003c/span>std\u003cspan class=\"token double-colon punctuation\">::\u003c/span>ostream\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">&amp;\u003c/span> output\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token keyword\">const\u003c/span> cymcp\u003cspan class=\"token double-colon punctuation\">::\u003c/span>CallContext\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">&amp;\u003c/span> context\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">)\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">{\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L11\" data-line=\"11\">        \u003cspan class=\"token comment\">// Produce bounded blocks from an immutable application snapshot.\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L12\" data-line=\"12\">        \u003cspan class=\"token keyword\">for\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">(\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token keyword\">const\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token keyword\">auto\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">&amp;\u003c/span> block \u003cspan class=\"token operator\">:\u003c/span> snapshot_blocks\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">)\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">{\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L13\" data-line=\"13\">            context\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">.\u003c/span>cancellation\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">.\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token function\">check\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">(\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">)\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L14\" data-line=\"14\">            output\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">.\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token function\">write\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">(\u003c/span>block\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">.\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token function\">data\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">(\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">)\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span> block\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">.\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token function\">size\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">(\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">)\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">)\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L15\" data-line=\"15\">        \u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">}\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L16\" data-line=\"16\">    \u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">}\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token string\">\"text/plain\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span> caller_context\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">)\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003c/code>\u003c/pre>\u003c/div>\u003cp>The host chooses the parent folder. The SDK creates its own random, owner-only child directory\nand private files; it does not change the parent&#39;s permissions. Above the threshold, the producer\nspills to disk. Keep this private cache outside directories exposed through other file tools.\nThe disk quota counts retained files, in-flight writers and pinned readers. Older\nretained disk results can be evicted; occupied active quotas fail explicitly. RAM retention and\ndisk quotas are separate. Concurrent producers run once and publish a handle only after success.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>Read the handle through the existing manifest/chunk APIs. For binary output pass \u003ccode>true\u003c/code> as the\nfourth store_stream argument; chunk contents use base64. UTF-8 text is read at character boundaries.\nFailures, cancellation, expiry and normal destruction release owned files. The optional disk\njanitor checks expiry approximately once per second; an active reader can pin its immutable file.\nAbnormal process termination can leave an orphaned private directory for the host to clean up.\nThe SDK never scans/deletes unrelated directories or automatically resumes an interrupted producer.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>\u003ccode>storage_stats()\u003c/code> reports retained RAM/disk bytes and result count, without local paths.\nToolGateway uses \u003ccode>store_json\u003c/code> to serialize large JSON output directly into this sink, avoiding a\nsecond complete serialized string. The handler still owns its original JSON allocation. For much\nlarger data, return a handle from a streaming producer directly. If a gateway result exceeds all\nconfigured storage budgets, its legacy complete-inline fallback remains; direct stream APIs fail\nResourceTooLarge without truncation. TTL and LRU retention are temporary, not archival storage.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"performance\">Measure without recording contents\u003ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#/en/runtime-options/performance\" aria-label=\"Link to Measure without recording contents\">#\u003c/a>\u003c/h2>\u003cdiv class=\"code-block\">\u003cdiv class=\"code-toolbar\">\u003cspan>cpp\u003c/span>\u003cbutton type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy\u003c/button>\u003c/div>\u003cpre>\u003ccode class=\"language-cpp\">\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-2-L1\" data-line=\"1\">\u003cspan class=\"token macro property\">\u003cspan class=\"token directive-hash\">#\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token directive keyword\">include\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token string\">&lt;cymcp/performance.hpp>\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-2-L2\" data-line=\"2\"> \u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-2-L3\" data-line=\"3\">cymcp\u003cspan class=\"token double-colon punctuation\">::\u003c/span>PerformanceOptions options\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-2-L4\" data-line=\"4\">options\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">.\u003c/span>jsonl_file \u003cspan class=\"token operator\">=\u003c/span> host_selected_private_log_file\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token comment\">// omit for memory only\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-2-L5\" data-line=\"5\">\u003cspan class=\"token keyword\">auto\u003c/span> performance \u003cspan class=\"token operator\">=\u003c/span> std\u003cspan class=\"token double-colon punctuation\">::\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token generic-function\">\u003cspan class=\"token function\">make_shared\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token generic class-name\">\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">&lt;\u003c/span>cymcp\u003cspan class=\"token double-colon punctuation\">::\u003c/span>PerformanceMonitor\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">>\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">(\u003c/span>options\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">)\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-2-L6\" data-line=\"6\">commands\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">->\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token function\">set_performance_monitor\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">(\u003c/span>performance\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">)\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-2-L7\" data-line=\"7\">\u003cspan class=\"token comment\">// Or set CallContext.performance, McpServerOptions.performance,\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-2-L8\" data-line=\"8\">\u003cspan class=\"token comment\">// McpClientOptions.performance or ChatConnection.performance.\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-2-L9\" data-line=\"9\">\u003cspan class=\"token keyword\">auto\u003c/span> totals \u003cspan class=\"token operator\">=\u003c/span> performance\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">->\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token function\">snapshot\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">(\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">)\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-2-L10\" data-line=\"10\">\u003cspan class=\"token keyword\">auto\u003c/span> recent_records \u003cspan class=\"token operator\">=\u003c/span> performance\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">->\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token function\">drain\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">(\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">)\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003c/code>\u003c/pre>\u003c/div>\u003cp>Records contain timestamp, stage/name, status, elapsed_ms, input_bytes, output_bytes and cache_hit.\nThey omit arguments, response contents, error explanations, principals, credentials and request IDs.\nStages distinguish operation, mcp.server, mcp.client and conversation. Conversation output_bytes\ncounts final UTF-8 text; protocol/operation sizes count serialized JSON bytes. These are not token counts.\nByte measurement walks JSON without allocating its serialized copy and is performed only when enabled.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>Snapshots retain aggregate call/error/cache counts, total bytes, mean/max latency and histogram\np50_upper_ms/p95_upper_ms (bucket upper bounds, not exact percentiles). Labels and recent rows\nare bounded; overflowing labels aggregate into other. The asynchronous file queue is bounded;\ndropped_file_records and file_errors expose file delivery failures. Rows drained by an application\nremain included in aggregate statistics. A supplied log destination is a new private output file;\nthe host owns rotation and retention. Instrumentation does not cache/retry operations or alter rights.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"notifications\">Subscribe to changes\u003ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#/en/runtime-options/notifications\" aria-label=\"Link to Subscribe to changes\">#\u003c/a>\u003c/h2>\u003cdiv class=\"code-block\">\u003cdiv class=\"code-toolbar\">\u003cspan>cpp\u003c/span>\u003cbutton type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy\u003c/button>\u003c/div>\u003cpre>\u003ccode class=\"language-cpp\">\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-3-L1\" data-line=\"1\">\u003cspan class=\"token macro property\">\u003cspan class=\"token directive-hash\">#\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token directive keyword\">include\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token string\">&lt;cymcp/changes.hpp>\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-3-L2\" data-line=\"2\">\u003cspan class=\"token macro property\">\u003cspan class=\"token directive-hash\">#\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token directive keyword\">include\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token string\">&lt;cymcp/mcp.hpp>\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-3-L3\" data-line=\"3\"> \u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-3-L4\" data-line=\"4\">\u003cspan class=\"token keyword\">auto\u003c/span> changes \u003cspan class=\"token operator\">=\u003c/span> std\u003cspan class=\"token double-colon punctuation\">::\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token generic-function\">\u003cspan class=\"token function\">make_shared\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token generic class-name\">\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">&lt;\u003c/span>cymcp\u003cspan class=\"token double-colon punctuation\">::\u003c/span>ChangeFeed\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">>\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">(\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">)\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-3-L5\" data-line=\"5\">commands\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">->\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token function\">set_change_feed\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">(\u003c/span>changes\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">)\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-3-L6\" data-line=\"6\">resources\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">->\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token function\">set_change_feed\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">(\u003c/span>changes\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">)\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-3-L7\" data-line=\"7\">cymcp\u003cspan class=\"token double-colon punctuation\">::\u003c/span>McpServerOptions server_options\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-3-L8\" data-line=\"8\">server_options\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">.\u003c/span>resources \u003cspan class=\"token operator\">=\u003c/span> resources\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-3-L9\" data-line=\"9\">server_options\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">.\u003c/span>changes \u003cspan class=\"token operator\">=\u003c/span> changes\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-3-L10\" data-line=\"10\">cymcp\u003cspan class=\"token double-colon punctuation\">::\u003c/span>McpServer \u003cspan class=\"token function\">server\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">(\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">*\u003c/span>commands\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token string\">\"My app\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span> server_options\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">)\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-3-L11\" data-line=\"11\">\u003cspan class=\"token comment\">// Client: after connect(), explicitly opt into its owned notification reader.\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-3-L12\" data-line=\"12\">client\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">.\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token function\">start_notifications\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">(\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">{\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">{\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token string\">\"toolsListChanged\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token boolean\">true\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">}\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-3-L13\" data-line=\"13\">    \u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">{\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token string\">\"resourcesListChanged\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token boolean\">true\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">}\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-3-L14\" data-line=\"14\">    \u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">{\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token string\">\"resourceSubscriptions\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span> cymcp\u003cspan class=\"token double-colon punctuation\">::\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token class-name\">Json\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token double-colon punctuation\">::\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token function\">array\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">(\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">{\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token string\">\"app://state\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">}\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">)\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">}\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">}\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">)\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003c/code>\u003c/pre>\u003c/div>\u003cp>Registry add/replace/remove publishes tool-list changes. Registered resource mutations publish\nresource-list and URI changes. For external host changes, publish \u003ccode>resource\u003c/code> with its URI on the\nsame journal, or replace the immutable snapshot. Notifications never expose resource contents.\nResource URIs are authorized on subscription; subsequent deletion/revocation still invalidates\npreviously authorized URIs, and actual reads always apply current policy. Private generated results\nstay outside public catalogues. A bounded journal reports missed events so subscriptions invalidate\nbroadly instead of silently retaining stale data.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>The server implements MCP 2026 subscriptions/listen, first acknowledgment, per-subscription IDs,\nrequested-type filtering and cancellation. HTTP uses a streamed SSE POST; LocalHttpServer supplies\nthe channel automatically. Custom transports must provide CallContext.notifications (null means\nheartbeat). Stdio uses a separate subscriber worker pool, so one ordinary worker remains usable.\nDefaults accept two active streams and 64 URIs per stream; configure max_subscriptions and\nmax_resource_subscriptions on McpServerOptions to change these bounds. HTTP streams occupy\nHTTP workers: provide more workers than active streams (default is four). Shutdown cancels streams.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>The client owns a reader only after start_notifications. Incoming changes invalidate its caches\nbefore the next access, including changes received while a previous request was in flight.\nUse drain_notifications for host/UI integration and notification_status for the accepted filter,\nrunning flag and terminal error code. No host callbacks run on reader threads. stop_notifications\ncancels/joins the reader; it never retries a command. A failed stream invalidates caches and\nreports failure; reconnection is explicit. Legacy 2025 peers retain TTL/clear_cache behavior and\nreturn Unsupported for this new subscription API. Unenabled servers advertise no subscription support.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"context\">Bound API context while retaining full history\u003ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#/en/runtime-options/context\" aria-label=\"Link to Bound API context while retaining full history\">#\u003c/a>\u003c/h2>\u003cdiv class=\"code-block\">\u003cdiv class=\"code-toolbar\">\u003cspan>cpp\u003c/span>\u003cbutton type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy\u003c/button>\u003c/div>\u003cpre>\u003ccode class=\"language-cpp\">\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-4-L1\" data-line=\"1\">cymcp\u003cspan class=\"token double-colon punctuation\">::\u003c/span>ContextOptions context\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-4-L2\" data-line=\"2\">context\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">.\u003c/span>max_bytes \u003cspan class=\"token operator\">=\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token number\">128\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token operator\">*\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token number\">1024\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token comment\">// serialized messages, not a model token-window claim\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-4-L3\" data-line=\"3\">context\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">.\u003c/span>recent_turns \u003cspan class=\"token operator\">=\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token number\">8\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-4-L4\" data-line=\"4\">conversation\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">.\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token function\">configure_context\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">(\u003c/span>context\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">)\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003c/code>\u003c/pre>\u003c/div>\u003cp>Configure an idle Conversation before use or restore. Default max_bytes=0 disables projection.\nThe sent view retains at most recent_turns complete user turns within its byte budget. System\ninstructions and the active user turn are pinned. Tool calls/results are never split across turns.\nAn assistant reference marker explains omitted history. Full history, transcripts and checkpoints\nremain unchanged; the host can expose bounded history-reading commands if the AI needs older details.\nThis feature bounds the sent view, not the complete host transcript&#39;s RAM usage.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>Optional ContextOptions.summarize is a host callback receiving previous_summary, newly omitted\nmessages and max_bytes. It runs only when necessary, never launches an implicit AI request and\nmust return bounded UTF-8 text. Its summary is assistant reference material, not a replacement for\nsystem instructions. Edits, deletions and restore reset the incremental summary. Context options\nand callbacks are host configuration, not serialized checkpoint data.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>Oversized pinned instructions/current input fail ContextTooLarge before generation. If a live tool\nturn exceeds the budget, its already executed calls/results are retained and never replayed; the\nnext user turn can recover with a new projection. Provider loops enforce this message budget\nbetween tool rounds. Tool schemas and provider framing add overhead outside the message budget.\nNative CLI agents keep their own context behavior; configuring their SDK context window explicitly\nreturns Unsupported. ChatController applies ChatConnection.context only to host-history APIs.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"chat-lab\">Chat Lab configuration\u003ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#/en/runtime-options/chat-lab\" aria-label=\"Link to Chat Lab configuration\">#\u003c/a>\u003c/h2>\u003cdiv class=\"code-block\">\u003cdiv class=\"code-toolbar\">\u003cspan>json\u003c/span>\u003cbutton type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy\u003c/button>\u003c/div>\u003cpre>\u003ccode class=\"language-json\">\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-5-L1\" data-line=\"1\">\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">{\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-5-L2\" data-line=\"2\">  \u003cspan class=\"token property\">\"context\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">:\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">{\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token property\">\"max_bytes\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">:\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token number\">131072\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token property\">\"recent_turns\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">:\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token number\">8\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">}\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-5-L3\" data-line=\"3\">  \u003cspan class=\"token property\">\"performance\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">:\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">{\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token property\">\"enabled\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">:\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token boolean\">true\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">}\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-5-L4\" data-line=\"4\">  \u003cspan class=\"token property\">\"app_commands\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">:\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">{\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-5-L5\" data-line=\"5\">    \u003cspan class=\"token property\">\"notifications\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">:\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token boolean\">true\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-5-L6\" data-line=\"6\">    \u003cspan class=\"token property\">\"storage\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">:\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">{\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token property\">\"directory\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">:\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token string\">\"./private-cache\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token property\">\"disk_bytes\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">:\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token number\">1073741824\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">}\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-5-L7\" data-line=\"7\">  \u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">}\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-5-L8\" data-line=\"8\">\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">}\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003c/code>\u003c/pre>\u003c/div>\u003cp>Merge selected fields into an existing private provider configuration. Each is independent.\nPerformance rows appear in Logs; optional performance.file chooses a separate private JSONL file.\nNotification mode also exposes app://chat-lab/counter, updated by both SDK and MCP counter writes.\nExisting configurations and the original two-command interface continue to work.\u003c/p>\n","text":"Independent options # All four facilities are opt-in. Core supplies resources, disk spooling, change journals and performance monitoring without graphical or AI dependencies. ContextWindow belongs to AI. There are no added external runtime dependencies. No model is downloaded or launched to summarize history. Unconfigured applications retain full API history, memory-only retained results and TTL caches. Produce large resources incrementally # cpp Copy # include \u003ccymcp/resources.hpp> cymcp :: ResourceOptions storage ; storage . disk_directory = host_selected_cache_folder ; storage . max_stored_bytes = 8 * 1024 * 1024 ; storage . spool_threshold = 1024 * 1024 ; storage . max_disk_bytes = 1024ULL * 1024 * 1024 ; auto resources = std :: make_shared \u003c cymcp :: ResourceRegistry > ( host_resource_policy , storage ) ; auto handle = resources -> store_stream ( [ snapshot_blocks ] ( std :: ostream & output , const cymcp :: CallContext & context ) { // Produce bounded blocks from an immutable application snapshot. for ( const auto & block : snapshot_blocks ) { context . cancellation . check ( ) ; output . write ( block . data ( ) , block . size ( ) ) ; } } , \"text/plain\" , caller_context ) ; The host chooses the parent folder. The SDK creates its own random, owner-only child directory and private files; it does not change the parent's permissions. Above the threshold, the producer spills to disk. Keep this private cache outside directories exposed through other file tools. The disk quota counts retained files, in-flight writers and pinned readers. Older retained disk results can be evicted; occupied active quotas fail explicitly. RAM retention and disk quotas are separate. Concurrent producers run once and publish a handle only after success. Read the handle through the existing manifest/chunk APIs. For binary output pass true as the fourth store_stream argument; chunk contents use base64. UTF-8 text is read at character boundaries. Failures, cancellation, expiry and normal destruction release owned files. The optional disk janitor checks expiry approximately once per second; an active reader can pin its immutable file. Abnormal process termination can leave an orphaned private directory for the host to clean up. The SDK never scans/deletes unrelated directories or automatically resumes an interrupted producer. storage_stats() reports retained RAM/disk bytes and result count, without local paths. ToolGateway uses store_json to serialize large JSON output directly into this sink, avoiding a second complete serialized string. The handler still owns its original JSON allocation. For much larger data, return a handle from a streaming producer directly. If a gateway result exceeds all configured storage budgets, its legacy complete-inline fallback remains; direct stream APIs fail ResourceTooLarge without truncation. TTL and LRU retention are temporary, not archival storage. Measure without recording contents # cpp Copy # include \u003ccymcp/performance.hpp> cymcp :: PerformanceOptions options ; options . jsonl_file = host_selected_private_log_file ; // omit for memory only auto performance = std :: make_shared \u003c cymcp :: PerformanceMonitor > ( options ) ; commands -> set_performance_monitor ( performance ) ; // Or set CallContext.performance, McpServerOptions.performance, // McpClientOptions.performance or ChatConnection.performance. auto totals = performance -> snapshot ( ) ; auto recent_records = performance -> drain ( ) ; Records contain timestamp, stage/name, status, elapsed_ms, input_bytes, output_bytes and cache_hit. They omit arguments, response contents, error explanations, principals, credentials and request IDs. Stages distinguish operation, mcp.server, mcp.client and conversation. Conversation output_bytes counts final UTF-8 text; protocol/operation sizes count serialized JSON bytes. These are not token counts. Byte measurement walks JSON without allocating its serialized copy and is performed only when enabled. Snapshots retain aggregate call/error/cache counts, total bytes, mean/max latency and histogram p50_upper_ms/p95_upper_ms (bucket upper bounds, not exact percentiles). Labels and recent rows are bounded; overflowing labels aggregate into other. The asynchronous file queue is bounded; dropped_file_records and file_errors expose file delivery failures. Rows drained by an application remain included in aggregate statistics. A supplied log destination is a new private output file; the host owns rotation and retention. Instrumentation does not cache/retry operations or alter rights. Subscribe to changes # cpp Copy # include \u003ccymcp/changes.hpp> # include \u003ccymcp/mcp.hpp> auto changes = std :: make_shared \u003c cymcp :: ChangeFeed > ( ) ; commands -> set_change_feed ( changes ) ; resources -> set_change_feed ( changes ) ; cymcp :: McpServerOptions server_options ; server_options . resources = resources ; server_options . changes = changes ; cymcp :: McpServer server ( * commands , \"My app\" , server_options ) ; // Client: after connect(), explicitly opt into its owned notification reader. client . start_notifications ( { { \"toolsListChanged\" , true } , { \"resourcesListChanged\" , true } , { \"resourceSubscriptions\" , cymcp :: Json :: array ( { \"app://state\" } ) } } ) ; Registry add/replace/remove publishes tool-list changes. Registered resource mutations publish resource-list and URI changes. For external host changes, publish resource with its URI on the same journal, or replace the immutable snapshot. Notifications never expose resource contents. Resource URIs are authorized on subscription; subsequent deletion/revocation still invalidates previously authorized URIs, and actual reads always apply current policy. Private generated results stay outside public catalogues. A bounded journal reports missed events so subscriptions invalidate broadly instead of silently retaining stale data. The server implements MCP 2026 subscriptions/listen, first acknowledgment, per-subscription IDs, requested-type filtering and cancellation. HTTP uses a streamed SSE POST; LocalHttpServer supplies the channel automatically. Custom transports must provide CallContext.notifications (null means heartbeat). Stdio uses a separate subscriber worker pool, so one ordinary worker remains usable. Defaults accept two active streams and 64 URIs per stream; configure max_subscriptions and max_resource_subscriptions on McpServerOptions to change these bounds. HTTP streams occupy HTTP workers: provide more workers than active streams (default is four). Shutdown cancels streams. The client owns a reader only after start_notifications. Incoming changes invalidate its caches before the next access, including changes received while a previous request was in flight. Use drain_notifications for host/UI integration and notification_status for the accepted filter, running flag and terminal error code. No host callbacks run on reader threads. stop_notifications cancels/joins the reader; it never retries a command. A failed stream invalidates caches and reports failure; reconnection is explicit. Legacy 2025 peers retain TTL/clear_cache behavior and return Unsupported for this new subscription API. Unenabled servers advertise no subscription support. Bound API context while retaining full history # cpp Copy cymcp :: ContextOptions context ; context . max_bytes = 128 * 1024 ; // serialized messages, not a model token-window claim context . recent_turns = 8 ; conversation . configure_context ( context ) ; Configure an idle Conversation before use or restore. Default max_bytes=0 disables projection. The sent view retains at most recent_turns complete user turns within its byte budget. System instructions and the active user turn are pinned. Tool calls/results are never split across turns. An assistant reference marker explains omitted history. Full history, transcripts and checkpoints remain unchanged; the host can expose bounded history-reading commands if the AI needs older details. This feature bounds the sent view, not the complete host transcript's RAM usage. Optional ContextOptions.summarize is a host callback receiving previous_summary, newly omitted messages and max_bytes. It runs only when necessary, never launches an implicit AI request and must return bounded UTF-8 text. Its summary is assistant reference material, not a replacement for system instructions. Edits, deletions and restore reset the incremental summary. Context options and callbacks are host configuration, not serialized checkpoint data. Oversized pinned instructions/current input fail ContextTooLarge before generation. If a live tool turn exceeds the budget, its already executed calls/results are retained and never replayed; the next user turn can recover with a new projection. Provider loops enforce this message budget between tool rounds. Tool schemas and provider framing add overhead outside the message budget. Native CLI agents keep their own context behavior; configuring their SDK context window explicitly returns Unsupported. ChatController applies ChatConnection.context only to host-history APIs. Chat Lab configuration # json Copy { \"context\" : { \"max_bytes\" : 131072 , \"recent_turns\" : 8 } , \"performance\" : { \"enabled\" : true } , \"app_commands\" : { \"notifications\" : true , \"storage\" : { \"directory\" : \"./private-cache\" , \"disk_bytes\" : 1073741824 } } } Merge selected fields into an existing private provider configuration. Each is independent. Performance rows appear in Logs; optional performance.file chooses a separate private JSONL file. Notification mode also exposes app://chat-lab/counter, updated by both SDK and MCP counter writes. Existing configurations and the original two-command interface continue to work. #include \u003ccymcp/resources.hpp> cymcp::ResourceOptions storage; storage.disk_directory = host_selected_cache_folder; storage.max_stored_bytes = 8 * 1024 * 1024; storage.spool_threshold = 1024 * 1024; storage.max_disk_bytes = 1024ULL * 1024 * 1024; auto resources = std::make_shared\u003ccymcp::ResourceRegistry>(host_resource_policy, storage); auto handle = resources->store_stream( [snapshot_blocks](std::ostream& output, const cymcp::CallContext& context) { // Produce bounded blocks from an immutable application snapshot. for (const auto& block : snapshot_blocks) { context.cancellation.check(); output.write(block.data(), block.size()); } }, \"text/plain\", caller_context); #include \u003ccymcp/performance.hpp> cymcp::PerformanceOptions options; options.jsonl_file = host_selected_private_log_file; // omit for memory only auto performance = std::make_shared\u003ccymcp::PerformanceMonitor>(options); commands->set_performance_monitor(performance); // Or set CallContext.performance, McpServerOptions.performance, // McpClientOptions.performance or ChatConnection.performance. auto totals = performance->snapshot(); auto recent_records = performance->drain(); #include \u003ccymcp/changes.hpp> #include \u003ccymcp/mcp.hpp> auto changes = std::make_shared\u003ccymcp::ChangeFeed>(); commands->set_change_feed(changes); resources->set_change_feed(changes); cymcp::McpServerOptions server_options; server_options.resources = resources; server_options.changes = changes; cymcp::McpServer server(*commands, \"My app\", server_options); // Client: after connect(), explicitly opt into its owned notification reader. client.start_notifications({{\"toolsListChanged\", true}, {\"resourcesListChanged\", true}, {\"resourceSubscriptions\", cymcp::Json::array({\"app://state\"})}}); cymcp::ContextOptions context; context.max_bytes = 128 * 1024; // serialized messages, not a model token-window claim context.recent_turns = 8; conversation.configure_context(context); { \"context\": {\"max_bytes\": 131072, \"recent_turns\": 8}, \"performance\": {\"enabled\": true}, \"app_commands\": { \"notifications\": true, \"storage\": {\"directory\": \"./private-cache\", \"disk_bytes\": 1073741824} } }","headings":[{"id":"options","text":"Independent options","level":2},{"id":"disk","text":"Produce large resources incrementally","level":2},{"id":"performance","text":"Measure without recording contents","level":2},{"id":"notifications","text":"Subscribe to changes","level":2},{"id":"context","text":"Bound API context while retaining full history","level":2},{"id":"chat-lab","text":"Chat Lab configuration","level":2}],"anchors":["L1","L2","L3","L4","L5","L6","L7","L8","L9","L10","L11","L12","L13","L14","L15","L16","code-2-L1","code-2-L2","code-2-L3","code-2-L4","code-2-L5","code-2-L6","code-2-L7","code-2-L8","code-2-L9","code-2-L10","code-3-L1","code-3-L2","code-3-L3","code-3-L4","code-3-L5","code-3-L6","code-3-L7","code-3-L8","code-3-L9","code-3-L10","code-3-L11","code-3-L12","code-3-L13","code-3-L14","code-4-L1","code-4-L2","code-4-L3","code-4-L4","code-5-L1","code-5-L2","code-5-L3","code-5-L4","code-5-L5","code-5-L6","code-5-L7","code-5-L8"],"languages":["cpp","json"],"code":"#include \u003ccymcp/resources.hpp>\n\ncymcp::ResourceOptions storage;\nstorage.disk_directory = host_selected_cache_folder;\nstorage.max_stored_bytes = 8 * 1024 * 1024;\nstorage.spool_threshold = 1024 * 1024;\nstorage.max_disk_bytes = 1024ULL * 1024 * 1024;\nauto resources = std::make_shared\u003ccymcp::ResourceRegistry>(host_resource_policy, storage);\nauto handle = resources->store_stream(\n    [snapshot_blocks](std::ostream& output, const cymcp::CallContext& context) {\n        // Produce bounded blocks from an immutable application snapshot.\n        for (const auto& block : snapshot_blocks) {\n            context.cancellation.check();\n            output.write(block.data(), block.size());\n        }\n    }, \"text/plain\", caller_context);\n#include \u003ccymcp/performance.hpp>\n\ncymcp::PerformanceOptions options;\noptions.jsonl_file = host_selected_private_log_file; // omit for memory only\nauto performance = std::make_shared\u003ccymcp::PerformanceMonitor>(options);\ncommands->set_performance_monitor(performance);\n// Or set CallContext.performance, McpServerOptions.performance,\n// McpClientOptions.performance or ChatConnection.performance.\nauto totals = performance->snapshot();\nauto recent_records = performance->drain();\n#include \u003ccymcp/changes.hpp>\n#include \u003ccymcp/mcp.hpp>\n\nauto changes = std::make_shared\u003ccymcp::ChangeFeed>();\ncommands->set_change_feed(changes);\nresources->set_change_feed(changes);\ncymcp::McpServerOptions server_options;\nserver_options.resources = resources;\nserver_options.changes = changes;\ncymcp::McpServer server(*commands, \"My app\", server_options);\n// Client: after connect(), explicitly opt into its owned notification reader.\nclient.start_notifications({{\"toolsListChanged\", true},\n    {\"resourcesListChanged\", true},\n    {\"resourceSubscriptions\", cymcp::Json::array({\"app://state\"})}});\ncymcp::ContextOptions context;\ncontext.max_bytes = 128 * 1024; // serialized messages, not a model token-window claim\ncontext.recent_turns = 8;\nconversation.configure_context(context);\n{\n  \"context\": {\"max_bytes\": 131072, \"recent_turns\": 8},\n  \"performance\": {\"enabled\": true},\n  \"app_commands\": {\n    \"notifications\": true,\n    \"storage\": {\"directory\": \"./private-cache\", \"disk_bytes\": 1073741824}\n  }\n}","assets":[],"links":[],"kind":"guide"},{"id":"troubleshooting","title":"Resolve connection problems","description":"Understand provider errors, interrupted sessions and missing local help.","section":"Guides","parent":"overview","order":4,"revision":"3","locale":"en","html":"\u003ch2 id=\"connection\">Connection errors\u003ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#/en/troubleshooting/connection\" aria-label=\"Link to Connection errors\">#\u003c/a>\u003c/h2>\u003cp>Open \u003cstrong>Logs\u003c/strong> to see which discovery, protocol, account, catalogue or session step failed.\nUse \u003cstrong>Copy log\u003c/strong> or \u003cstrong>Open log file\u003c/strong> for the diagnostic record. See the \u003ca href=\"#/en/chat-lab/logs\">journal controls\u003c/a>.\u003c/p>\n\u003ctable>\n\u003cthead>\n\u003ctr>\n\u003cth>Error or symptom\u003c/th>\n\u003cth>What to do\u003c/th>\n\u003c/tr>\n\u003c/thead>\n\u003ctbody>\u003ctr>\n\u003ctd>\u003ccode>ExecutableMissing\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>Select the native CLI executable; verify it runs in the intended account/environment.\u003c/td>\n\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\n\u003ctd>\u003ccode>AuthenticationRequired\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>For native providers, use \u003cstrong>Sign in\u003c/strong>, complete the native login and reconnect. For APIs, supply the credential through its environment/memory field.\u003c/td>\n\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\n\u003ctd>\u003ccode>ProviderError\u003c/code> after connecting\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>Verify the exact model ID, account entitlement and provider-native error outside the app.\u003c/td>\n\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\n\u003ctd>Catalogue returns \u003ccode>Unsupported\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>Enter a real model ID manually; some transports do not expose discovery.\u003c/td>\n\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\n\u003ctd>Local endpoint unreachable\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>Start the local service and check its base URL/port and API format.\u003c/td>\n\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\n\u003ctd>\u003ccode>UnsupportedContent\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>Choose a model/transport accepting that attachment type, or remove the attachment.\u003c/td>\n\u003c/tr>\n\u003c/tbody>\u003c/table>\n\u003cp>The CLI account used by a launched process can differ from another terminal&#39;s environment.\nUse \u003ccode>process.environment\u003c/code> when the host intentionally needs child-specific values. A successful\nconnection is not a guarantee that the account can perform a generation.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"interrupted\">Interrupted conversations\u003ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#/en/troubleshooting/interrupted\" aria-label=\"Link to Interrupted conversations\">#\u003c/a>\u003c/h2>\u003cp>\u003ccode>Cancelled\u003c/code> is an interruption, not a successful final answer. A truncated stream can report\n\u003ccode>UnexpectedEOF\u003c/code>. Keep the partial text, reconnect explicitly, and decide what to send next.\n\u003ccode>SessionInvalid\u003c/code> means the exact native session could not be resumed; retain its saved history.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>\u003ccode>ContextTooLarge\u003c/code> now means a memory guard (256 MiB per message) or the model&#39;s own context\nwindow was reached: start a new conversation or reduce attachments. A slow or minimised UI no\nlonger fails a turn; very long transcripts only scroll their oldest rows out of the view.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"help\">Missing manual\u003ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#/en/troubleshooting/help\" aria-label=\"Link to Missing manual\">#\u003c/a>\u003c/h2>\u003cp>Keep \u003ccode>Documentation/Documentation.html\u003c/code> and the complete \u003ccode>Documentation/DocData\u003c/code> directory\nbeside Chat Lab. F1 opens that installed copy, not an online fallback. If the folder is absent,\nrestore it from the application package or rebuild the package. Open the HTML directly to check\nits local scripts and images. The reader needs no Node.js or web server.\u003c/p>\n","text":"Connection errors # Open Logs to see which discovery, protocol, account, catalogue or session step failed. Use Copy log or Open log file for the diagnostic record. See the journal controls . Error or symptom What to do ExecutableMissing Select the native CLI executable; verify it runs in the intended account/environment. AuthenticationRequired For native providers, use Sign in , complete the native login and reconnect. For APIs, supply the credential through its environment/memory field. ProviderError after connecting Verify the exact model ID, account entitlement and provider-native error outside the app. Catalogue returns Unsupported Enter a real model ID manually; some transports do not expose discovery. Local endpoint unreachable Start the local service and check its base URL/port and API format. UnsupportedContent Choose a model/transport accepting that attachment type, or remove the attachment. The CLI account used by a launched process can differ from another terminal's environment. Use process.environment when the host intentionally needs child-specific values. A successful connection is not a guarantee that the account can perform a generation. Interrupted conversations # Cancelled is an interruption, not a successful final answer. A truncated stream can report UnexpectedEOF . Keep the partial text, reconnect explicitly, and decide what to send next. SessionInvalid means the exact native session could not be resumed; retain its saved history. ContextTooLarge now means a memory guard (256 MiB per message) or the model's own context window was reached: start a new conversation or reduce attachments. A slow or minimised UI no longer fails a turn; very long transcripts only scroll their oldest rows out of the view. Missing manual # Keep Documentation/Documentation.html and the complete Documentation/DocData directory beside Chat Lab. F1 opens that installed copy, not an online fallback. If the folder is absent, restore it from the application package or rebuild the package. Open the HTML directly to check its local scripts and images. The reader needs no Node.js or web server.","headings":[{"id":"connection","text":"Connection errors","level":2},{"id":"interrupted","text":"Interrupted conversations","level":2},{"id":"help","text":"Missing manual","level":2}],"anchors":[],"languages":[],"code":"","assets":[],"links":["#/en/chat-lab/logs"],"kind":"guide"},{"id":"chat-lab","title":"Commandes de Chat Lab","description":"Connecter un fournisseur, envoyer des messages et exposer les commandes de démonstration.","section":"Guides","parent":"overview","order":2,"sourceRevision":"8","locale":"fr","html":"\u003ch2 id=\"connect\">Se connecter\u003ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#/fr/chat-lab/connect\" aria-label=\"Lien vers Se connecter\">#\u003c/a>\u003c/h2>\u003cp>Le tchat s’ouvre directement. La roue \u003cstrong>Paramètres\u003c/strong> donne accès aux onglets \u003cstrong>Fournisseurs\u003c/strong>,\n\u003cstrong>Journal\u003c/strong> et \u003cstrong>Aide\u003c/strong>. \u003cstrong>Fermer\u003c/strong> revient à la conversation et à son brouillon. \u003cstrong>F1\u003c/strong> ouvre l’aide.\nDans Fournisseurs, rechercher le catalogue, sélectionner une carte et modifier ses propres champs.\nLes réglages des autres fournisseurs restent en mémoire pour cette exécution. \u003cstrong>Connecter / Nouveau tchat\u003c/strong>\nouvre la connexion et revient au tchat ; un double-clic sur une carte connecte directement.\u003c/p>\n\u003cfigure data-cydoc-module=\"image\" data-cydoc-id=\"provider-settings\" data-config=\"{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;provider-settings&quot;,&quot;src&quot;:&quot;assets/providers-fr.png&quot;,&quot;alt&quot;:&quot;Catalogue filtrable et paramètres de connexion et de modèle pour OpenAI API&quot;,&quot;controls&quot;:&quot;minimal&quot;}\">\u003cimg src=\"assets/providers-fr.png\" alt=\"Catalogue filtrable et paramètres de connexion et de modèle pour OpenAI API\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\">\u003c/figure>\u003cp>La \u003cstrong>Connexion automatique\u003c/strong>, dans Fournisseurs, est activée au démarrage. Chat Lab détecte les CLI natifs,\nles installations npm de l&#39;utilisateur, les services Ollama/LM Studio/compatibles démarrés\nà leurs adresses locales connues et les clés API des variables d&#39;environnement. Il prépare\nla première connexion disponible sans envoyer de message. La démonstration initiale ne bloque pas ce choix.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>Les CLI conservent leur compte et leur modèle par défaut. Les services locaux peuvent choisir\nun modèle texte du catalogue réel. Les API distantes affichent leur catalogue et attendent\nvotre choix de modèle. La liste propose les identifiants retournés ; un changement prend effet\nau prochain clic sur \u003cstrong>Connecter\u003c/strong>. La disponibilité dépend toujours du compte et du fournisseur.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>\u003cstrong>Relancer la détection\u003c/strong> recommence la recherche. Les cartes distinguent installation détectée,\nconnexion active et configuration nécessaire. Le panneau du fournisseur sélectionné explique\nles installations, identifiants, adresses ou modèles locaux manquants. La recherche\nn&#39;installe aucun fournisseur et ne connecte aucun compte. Les clés restent en mémoire.\nUne API distante n&#39;est contactée qu&#39;à la sélection de sa connexion.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>Si un fournisseur natif demande une authentification, \u003cstrong>Se connecter\u003c/strong> ouvre son propre parcours\nde connexion dans une console. Terminer cette connexion puis reconnecter ici. Cette action utilise\nl&#39;installation détectée.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>Les champs manuels restent disponibles dans Fournisseurs avec le mode automatique activé.\n\u003cstrong>Actualiser le catalogue\u003c/strong> récupère les vrais modèles. Les modifications s&#39;appliquent\nà la prochaine action \u003cstrong>Connecter / Nouveau tchat\u003c/strong>.\nChoisir un fournisseur préremplit son adresse conventionnelle, sa variable de clé et ses\nparamètres, ainsi que l&#39;installation détectée.\u003c/p>\n\u003cfigure data-cydoc-module=\"image\" data-cydoc-id=\"automatic-connection\" data-config=\"{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;automatic-connection&quot;,&quot;src&quot;:&quot;assets/chat-auto-fr.png&quot;,&quot;alt&quot;:&quot;Capture historique de l’interface après détection et connexion automatiques, sans message envoyé&quot;,&quot;controls&quot;:&quot;minimal&quot;}\">\u003cimg src=\"assets/chat-auto-fr.png\" alt=\"Capture historique de l’interface après détection et connexion automatiques, sans message envoyé\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\">\u003c/figure>\u003cp>\u003cstrong>Installation et connexion\u003c/strong> contient l&#39;exécutable et le dossier de travail ou les champs API.\nDéplier \u003cstrong>Lancement avancé\u003c/strong> pour les arguments JSON et les paramètres particuliers.\nUtiliser le vrai \u003ccode>.exe\u003c/code>, ou \u003ccode>node.exe\u003c/code> accompagné des arguments de son script ;\nles wrappers shell ne sont pas lancés. \u003cstrong>Paramètres avancés (JSON)\u003c/strong> reçoit les réglages du\nfournisseur. \u003cstrong>Consigne système\u003c/strong>, dans \u003cstrong>Conversation et historique\u003c/strong>, fournit les instructions de session.\nConsulter les \u003ca href=\"#/fr/providers/configure\">fournisseurs\u003c/a>.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"messages\">Envoyer et arrêter\u003ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#/fr/chat-lab/messages\" aria-label=\"Lien vers Envoyer et arrêter\">#\u003c/a>\u003c/h2>\u003cp>Écrire dans la zone de saisie. \u003cstrong>Entrée\u003c/strong> envoie ; \u003cstrong>Maj+Entrée\u003c/strong> ajoute une ligne. \u003cstrong>Ctrl+Entrée\u003c/strong> envoie également.\n\u003cstrong>Joindre des fichiers\u003c/strong> sélectionne les pièces jointes locales. Le texte arrive dans le\ntranscript Markdown ; l&#39;activité et la réflexion apparaissent lorsque le fournisseur les émet.\n\u003cstrong>Suivre les réponses\u003c/strong> règle le défilement automatique.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>La saisie grandit avec le brouillon. Sélectionner du texte pour la barre de formatage, ou utiliser\nCtrl+B/I/U/E. Le brouillon reste modifiable pendant une réponse ; un envoi pendant ce temps le conserve.\nDans le menu \u003cstrong>…\u003c/strong> du tchat, activer l’aperçu Markdown du brouillon. \u003cstrong>Ctrl+F\u003c/strong> recherche\ndans les messages. La flèche \u003cstrong>↑\u003c/strong> dans une saisie vide reprend le dernier message utilisateur.\nPour les conversations gérées par le SDK, on peut aussi modifier un message envoyé ou supprimer\nson tour après confirmation. Ces actions attendent un nouvel envoi explicite.\nSurvoler un message ou faire un clic droit pour \u003cstrong>Copier le message\u003c/strong> ou \u003cstrong>Répondre\u003c/strong> : répondre insère\nune citation dans le brouillon et attend l’envoi. L’historique natif reste sous le contrôle du fournisseur.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>Les pièces jointes ont leurs propres cartes. Les images se chargent en arrière-plan et s’agrandissent\ndans l’app. Cliquer sur un texte pour son aperçu, ou \u003cstrong>Enregistrer la pièce jointe\u003c/strong> pour choisir une\ndestination pour les octets embarqués. Pour inclure une image dans un document Markdown,\njoindre les deux fichiers au même message, puis utiliser le nom unique de l’image, par exemple\n\u003ccode>![Résultat](./graphe.png)\u003c/code>. Les définitions de référence fonctionnent aussi.\nCollez une image du presse-papiers ou les fichiers copiés dans l’Explorateur avec \u003cstrong>Ctrl+V\u003c/strong>.\nVérifiez la vignette et retirez au besoin la pièce jointe avant l’envoi.\nLes aperçus ne chargent pas les URL d’images arbitraires du Markdown. Un format sans décodeur conserve\nsa carte et son action d’enregistrement.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>Pendant la génération, \u003cstrong>Arrêter\u003c/strong> apparaît à côté d’\u003cstrong>Envoyer\u003c/strong>. Une annulation conserve la réponse partielle.\nSi le fournisseur refuse le tour, la réponse affiche son explication, le code d’erreur du SDK\net le code du fournisseur lorsqu’il est disponible. Le texte déjà reçu reste visible.\nLe \u003cstrong>Journal\u003c/strong> conserve le même diagnostic après masquage des secrets. Vous pouvez ensuite\nchanger de modèle et envoyer un nouveau message.\n\u003cstrong>Reconnecter\u003c/strong> reprend explicitement la session actuelle, sans renvoyer le message interrompu.\nConsulter les \u003ca href=\"#/fr/conversations\">conversations et l&#39;historique\u003c/a>.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"logs\">Lire le journal\u003ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#/fr/chat-lab/logs\" aria-label=\"Lien vers Lire le journal\">#\u003c/a>\u003c/h2>\u003cp>Ouvrir \u003cstrong>Paramètres → Journal\u003c/strong>. \u003cstrong>JSONL brut\u003c/strong> affiche les mêmes événements que le fichier.\nLa molette permet de lire les entrées précédentes pendant que le journal reçoit de nouvelles lignes.\nLes lignes indiquent l&#39;heure locale,\nle fournisseur, l&#39;opération, le code d&#39;événement ou d&#39;erreur, l&#39;explication et la durée. La connexion native\nprécise l&#39;initialisation du protocole, le contrôle du compte et la création de session. La génération\nindique le début de la réponse et sa fin.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>Utiliser le filtre ou \u003cstrong>Erreurs uniquement\u003c/strong>, \u003cstrong>Suivre le journal\u003c/strong> et \u003cstrong>Copier le journal\u003c/strong> pour les diagnostics.\n\u003cstrong>Ouvrir le fichier journal\u003c/strong> ouvre le fichier privé de session dans \u003ccode>%LOCALAPPDATA%/CyMCPSDK/ChatLab/logs\u003c/code>.\nL&#39;écriture se fait en arrière-plan. Survoler le nom du fichier pour son chemin complet. \u003cstrong>Vider la vue\u003c/strong>\nefface les lignes affichées et conserve le fichier. Messages, identifiants et clés API sont exclus.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>La vue garde les 2 000 dernières lignes. Chaque fichier est limité à 8 Mio ; une notification visible\nsignale sa saturation ou un problème d&#39;écriture. Le journal n&#39;annule jamais une conversation.\u003c/p>\n\u003cfigure data-cydoc-module=\"image\" data-cydoc-id=\"connection-journal\" data-config=\"{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;connection-journal&quot;,&quot;src&quot;:&quot;assets/logs-fr.png&quot;,&quot;alt&quot;:&quot;Journal de Chat Lab affichant le refus de modèle reproduit avec un simulateur de Codex&quot;,&quot;controls&quot;:&quot;minimal&quot;}\">\u003cimg src=\"assets/logs-fr.png\" alt=\"Journal de Chat Lab affichant le refus de modèle reproduit avec un simulateur de Codex\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\">\u003c/figure>\u003ch2 id=\"commands\">Permettre à une IA d&#39;utiliser les commandes\u003ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#/fr/chat-lab/commands\" aria-label=\"Lien vers Permettre à une IA d&#39;utiliser les commandes\">#\u003c/a>\u003c/h2>\u003cp>Dans Fournisseurs, déplier \u003cstrong>Droits et outils de l’app\u003c/strong>. La démonstration expose \u003ccode>get_counter\u003c/code> et \u003ccode>set_counter\u003c/code>,\npour des entiers entre −1 000 000 et 1 000 000. Le panneau affiche la valeur actuelle.\u003c/p>\n\u003col>\n\u003cli>Activer \u003cstrong>Autoriser la modification du compteur\u003c/strong> pour permettre les écritures.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Activer \u003cstrong>L&#39;IA peut appeler les commandes de l&#39;app\u003c/strong>, puis créer une connexion Codex ou API compatible.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Demander à l&#39;IA de modifier le compteur de démonstration, puis de le relire.\u003c/li>\n\u003c/ol>\n\u003cp>L&#39;attachement direct prend en charge Codex, Responses, Messages, Chat Completions/OpenRouter et Ollama.\nLes autres CLI utilisent leur configuration MCP native et renvoient \u003ccode>Unsupported\u003c/code> pour cette option.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"external\">Connecter une autre application\u003ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#/fr/chat-lab/external\" aria-label=\"Lien vers Connecter une autre application\">#\u003c/a>\u003c/h2>\u003cp>\u003cstrong>Activer le MCP local\u003c/strong> crée un serveur loopback authentifié sur un port libre.\nCopier l&#39;adresse affichée et utiliser \u003cstrong>Copier le jeton MCP\u003c/strong> pour configurer le client.\nUtiliser \u003ccode>/mcp\u003c/code> pour les outils MCP ou \u003ccode>/v1\u003c/code> sur le même port pour le SDK JSON direct.\u003c/p>\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block\">\u003cdiv class=\"code-toolbar\">\u003cspan>json\u003c/span>\u003cbutton type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copier\u003c/button>\u003c/div>\u003cpre>\u003ccode class=\"language-json\">\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L1\" data-line=\"1\">\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">{\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token property\">\"method\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">:\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token string\">\"invoke\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token property\">\"name\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">:\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token string\">\"get_counter\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token property\">\"arguments\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">:\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">{\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">}\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">}\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003c/code>\u003c/pre>\u003c/div>\u003cp>Les deux routes partagent le compteur et la politique d&#39;écriture active. Interdire les écritures\nne déconnecte pas le client. Désactiver le serveur ferme l&#39;adresse ; le réactiver crée un nouveau\njeton. Consulter les \u003ca href=\"#/fr/operations\">opérations\u003c/a> et les \u003ca href=\"#/fr/permissions\">droits\u003c/a>.\u003c/p>\n","text":"Se connecter # Le tchat s’ouvre directement. La roue Paramètres donne accès aux onglets Fournisseurs , Journal et Aide . Fermer revient à la conversation et à son brouillon. F1 ouvre l’aide. Dans Fournisseurs, rechercher le catalogue, sélectionner une carte et modifier ses propres champs. Les réglages des autres fournisseurs restent en mémoire pour cette exécution. Connecter / Nouveau tchat ouvre la connexion et revient au tchat ; un double-clic sur une carte connecte directement. La Connexion automatique , dans Fournisseurs, est activée au démarrage. Chat Lab détecte les CLI natifs, les installations npm de l'utilisateur, les services Ollama/LM Studio/compatibles démarrés à leurs adresses locales connues et les clés API des variables d'environnement. Il prépare la première connexion disponible sans envoyer de message. La démonstration initiale ne bloque pas ce choix. Les CLI conservent leur compte et leur modèle par défaut. Les services locaux peuvent choisir un modèle texte du catalogue réel. Les API distantes affichent leur catalogue et attendent votre choix de modèle. La liste propose les identifiants retournés ; un changement prend effet au prochain clic sur Connecter . La disponibilité dépend toujours du compte et du fournisseur. Relancer la détection recommence la recherche. Les cartes distinguent installation détectée, connexion active et configuration nécessaire. Le panneau du fournisseur sélectionné explique les installations, identifiants, adresses ou modèles locaux manquants. La recherche n'installe aucun fournisseur et ne connecte aucun compte. Les clés restent en mémoire. Une API distante n'est contactée qu'à la sélection de sa connexion. Si un fournisseur natif demande une authentification, Se connecter ouvre son propre parcours de connexion dans une console. Terminer cette connexion puis reconnecter ici. Cette action utilise l'installation détectée. Les champs manuels restent disponibles dans Fournisseurs avec le mode automatique activé. Actualiser le catalogue récupère les vrais modèles. Les modifications s'appliquent à la prochaine action Connecter / Nouveau tchat . Choisir un fournisseur préremplit son adresse conventionnelle, sa variable de clé et ses paramètres, ainsi que l'installation détectée. Installation et connexion contient l'exécutable et le dossier de travail ou les champs API. Déplier Lancement avancé pour les arguments JSON et les paramètres particuliers. Utiliser le vrai .exe , ou node.exe accompagné des arguments de son script ; les wrappers shell ne sont pas lancés. Paramètres avancés (JSON) reçoit les réglages du fournisseur. Consigne système , dans Conversation et historique , fournit les instructions de session. Consulter les fournisseurs . Envoyer et arrêter # Écrire dans la zone de saisie. Entrée envoie ; Maj+Entrée ajoute une ligne. Ctrl+Entrée envoie également. Joindre des fichiers sélectionne les pièces jointes locales. Le texte arrive dans le transcript Markdown ; l'activité et la réflexion apparaissent lorsque le fournisseur les émet. Suivre les réponses règle le défilement automatique. La saisie grandit avec le brouillon. Sélectionner du texte pour la barre de formatage, ou utiliser Ctrl+B/I/U/E. Le brouillon reste modifiable pendant une réponse ; un envoi pendant ce temps le conserve. Dans le menu … du tchat, activer l’aperçu Markdown du brouillon. Ctrl+F recherche dans les messages. La flèche ↑ dans une saisie vide reprend le dernier message utilisateur. Pour les conversations gérées par le SDK, on peut aussi modifier un message envoyé ou supprimer son tour après confirmation. Ces actions attendent un nouvel envoi explicite. Survoler un message ou faire un clic droit pour Copier le message ou Répondre : répondre insère une citation dans le brouillon et attend l’envoi. L’historique natif reste sous le contrôle du fournisseur. Les pièces jointes ont leurs propres cartes. Les images se chargent en arrière-plan et s’agrandissent dans l’app. Cliquer sur un texte pour son aperçu, ou Enregistrer la pièce jointe pour choisir une destination pour les octets embarqués. Pour inclure une image dans un document Markdown, joindre les deux fichiers au même message, puis utiliser le nom unique de l’image, par exemple ![Résultat](./graphe.png) . Les définitions de référence fonctionnent aussi. Collez une image du presse-papiers ou les fichiers copiés dans l’Explorateur avec Ctrl+V . Vérifiez la vignette et retirez au besoin la pièce jointe avant l’envoi. Les aperçus ne chargent pas les URL d’images arbitraires du Markdown. Un format sans décodeur conserve sa carte et son action d’enregistrement. Pendant la génération, Arrêter apparaît à côté d’ Envoyer . Une annulation conserve la réponse partielle. Si le fournisseur refuse le tour, la réponse affiche son explication, le code d’erreur du SDK et le code du fournisseur lorsqu’il est disponible. Le texte déjà reçu reste visible. Le Journal conserve le même diagnostic après masquage des secrets. Vous pouvez ensuite changer de modèle et envoyer un nouveau message. Reconnecter reprend explicitement la session actuelle, sans renvoyer le message interrompu. Consulter les conversations et l'historique . Lire le journal # Ouvrir Paramètres → Journal . JSONL brut affiche les mêmes événements que le fichier. La molette permet de lire les entrées précédentes pendant que le journal reçoit de nouvelles lignes. Les lignes indiquent l'heure locale, le fournisseur, l'opération, le code d'événement ou d'erreur, l'explication et la durée. La connexion native précise l'initialisation du protocole, le contrôle du compte et la création de session. La génération indique le début de la réponse et sa fin. Utiliser le filtre ou Erreurs uniquement , Suivre le journal et Copier le journal pour les diagnostics. Ouvrir le fichier journal ouvre le fichier privé de session dans %LOCALAPPDATA%/CyMCPSDK/ChatLab/logs . L'écriture se fait en arrière-plan. Survoler le nom du fichier pour son chemin complet. Vider la vue efface les lignes affichées et conserve le fichier. Messages, identifiants et clés API sont exclus. La vue garde les 2 000 dernières lignes. Chaque fichier est limité à 8 Mio ; une notification visible signale sa saturation ou un problème d'écriture. Le journal n'annule jamais une conversation. Permettre à une IA d'utiliser les commandes # Dans Fournisseurs, déplier Droits et outils de l’app . La démonstration expose get_counter et set_counter , pour des entiers entre −1 000 000 et 1 000 000. Le panneau affiche la valeur actuelle. Activer Autoriser la modification du compteur pour permettre les écritures. Activer L'IA peut appeler les commandes de l'app , puis créer une connexion Codex ou API compatible. Demander à l'IA de modifier le compteur de démonstration, puis de le relire. L'attachement direct prend en charge Codex, Responses, Messages, Chat Completions/OpenRouter et Ollama. Les autres CLI utilisent leur configuration MCP native et renvoient Unsupported pour cette option. Connecter une autre application # Activer le MCP local crée un serveur loopback authentifié sur un port libre. Copier l'adresse affichée et utiliser Copier le jeton MCP pour configurer le client. Utiliser /mcp pour les outils MCP ou /v1 sur le même port pour le SDK JSON direct. json Copier { \"method\" : \"invoke\" , \"name\" : \"get_counter\" , \"arguments\" : { } } Les deux routes partagent le compteur et la politique d'écriture active. Interdire les écritures ne déconnecte pas le client. Désactiver le serveur ferme l'adresse ; le réactiver crée un nouveau jeton. Consulter les opérations et les droits . {\"method\":\"invoke\",\"name\":\"get_counter\",\"arguments\":{}}","headings":[{"id":"connect","text":"Se connecter","level":2},{"id":"messages","text":"Envoyer et arrêter","level":2},{"id":"logs","text":"Lire le journal","level":2},{"id":"commands","text":"Permettre à une IA d'utiliser les commandes","level":2},{"id":"external","text":"Connecter une autre application","level":2}],"anchors":["L1"],"languages":["json"],"code":"{\"method\":\"invoke\",\"name\":\"get_counter\",\"arguments\":{}}","assets":["assets/providers-fr.png","assets/chat-auto-fr.png","assets/logs-fr.png"],"links":["#/fr/providers/configure","#/fr/conversations","#/fr/operations","#/fr/permissions"],"kind":"media","revision":"923de8c59496"},{"id":"conversations","title":"Conversations et historique","description":"Joindre des fichiers, annuler un tour et reprendre exactement une conversation sans la rejouer.","section":"Guides","parent":"chat-lab","order":2,"sourceRevision":"2","locale":"fr","html":"\u003ch2 id=\"attachments\">Pièces jointes\u003ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#/fr/conversations/attachments\" aria-label=\"Lien vers Pièces jointes\">#\u003c/a>\u003c/h2>\u003cp>\u003cstrong>Joindre des fichiers\u003c/strong> capture les fichiers locaux sélectionnés sur le worker. Images, audio et\nressources texte/PDF sont acceptés selon le transport et le modèle. Le panneau affiche les noms ;\nun aperçu multimédia enrichi nécessite les services de ressources fournis par l&#39;application hôte.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>La saisie s&#39;agrandit avec le texte et accepte jusqu&#39;à 256 fichiers. Des budgets de fichiers/contenus et la\nvalidation MIME/base64 s&#39;appliquent aussi. Un contenu incompatible est refusé explicitement.\nUn modèle qui reçoit une image ne prend pas forcément en charge l&#39;audio ou les documents.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"history\">Conserver une conversation\u003ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#/fr/conversations/history\" aria-label=\"Lien vers Conserver une conversation\">#\u003c/a>\u003c/h2>\u003col>\n\u003cli>Activer \u003cstrong>Enregistrer l&#39;historique\u003c/strong> avant la connexion.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Choisir un dossier privé et un identifiant d&#39;historique simple.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Envoyer les messages normalement ; chaque tour terminé ou interrompu est sauvegardé automatiquement.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Choisir les mêmes fournisseur/modèle, dossier et ID, puis \u003cstrong>Reprendre le tchat enregistré\u003c/strong>.\u003c/li>\n\u003c/ol>\n\u003cp>L&#39;historique est optionnel. Il contient messages, résultats d&#39;outils et pièces jointes intégrées : ce sont\ndes données utilisateur. Les clés et réglages de connexion n&#39;y sont pas inclus. Une erreur de stockage\ns&#39;affiche séparément d&#39;une génération réussie. Restaurer ne renvoie aucune consigne et ne répète aucune commande.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"resume\">Reprise et annulation\u003ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#/fr/conversations/resume\" aria-label=\"Lien vers Reprise et annulation\">#\u003c/a>\u003c/h2>\u003cp>Les fournisseurs natifs reprennent leur session exacte lorsqu&#39;ils le permettent ; les API sans état\nutilisent l&#39;historique conservé par l&#39;hôte. Si la session native ne peut pas être chargée, \u003ccode>SessionInvalid\u003c/code>\npréserve l&#39;historique au lieu de créer une conversation de remplacement. La reprise ACP dépend des\ncapacités négociées avec l&#39;agent.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>\u003cstrong>Arrêter\u003c/strong> annule l&#39;opération active. \u003cstrong>Reconnecter\u003c/strong> rouvre explicitement la connexion si nécessaire.\nAprès interruption, choisir d&#39;envoyer ou non un nouveau message ; aucune génération n&#39;est retentée automatiquement.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"api\">API C++ publique\u003ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#/fr/conversations/api\" aria-label=\"Lien vers API C++ publique\">#\u003c/a>\u003c/h2>\u003cp>\u003ccode>Conversation::checkpoint()\u003c/code> retourne un instantané restaurable. \u003ccode>ConversationStore::save(id, conversation)\u003c/code>\nl&#39;écrit de façon privée et atomique ; \u003ccode>load(id)\u003c/code> le lit pour \u003ccode>Conversation::restore(snapshot)\u003c/code>.\nLe fournisseur/modèle doit correspondre. Garder les instances de fournisseur et l&#39;executor en vie jusqu&#39;à\nla fin des opérations asynchrones. Les callbacks s&#39;exécutent sur le worker appelant, pas sur le thread UI.\u003c/p>\n","text":"Pièces jointes # Joindre des fichiers capture les fichiers locaux sélectionnés sur le worker. Images, audio et ressources texte/PDF sont acceptés selon le transport et le modèle. Le panneau affiche les noms ; un aperçu multimédia enrichi nécessite les services de ressources fournis par l'application hôte. La saisie s'agrandit avec le texte et accepte jusqu'à 256 fichiers. Des budgets de fichiers/contenus et la validation MIME/base64 s'appliquent aussi. Un contenu incompatible est refusé explicitement. Un modèle qui reçoit une image ne prend pas forcément en charge l'audio ou les documents. Conserver une conversation # Activer Enregistrer l'historique avant la connexion. Choisir un dossier privé et un identifiant d'historique simple. Envoyer les messages normalement ; chaque tour terminé ou interrompu est sauvegardé automatiquement. Choisir les mêmes fournisseur/modèle, dossier et ID, puis Reprendre le tchat enregistré . L'historique est optionnel. Il contient messages, résultats d'outils et pièces jointes intégrées : ce sont des données utilisateur. Les clés et réglages de connexion n'y sont pas inclus. Une erreur de stockage s'affiche séparément d'une génération réussie. Restaurer ne renvoie aucune consigne et ne répète aucune commande. Reprise et annulation # Les fournisseurs natifs reprennent leur session exacte lorsqu'ils le permettent ; les API sans état utilisent l'historique conservé par l'hôte. Si la session native ne peut pas être chargée, SessionInvalid préserve l'historique au lieu de créer une conversation de remplacement. La reprise ACP dépend des capacités négociées avec l'agent. Arrêter annule l'opération active. Reconnecter rouvre explicitement la connexion si nécessaire. Après interruption, choisir d'envoyer ou non un nouveau message ; aucune génération n'est retentée automatiquement. API C++ publique # Conversation::checkpoint() retourne un instantané restaurable. ConversationStore::save(id, conversation) l'écrit de façon privée et atomique ; load(id) le lit pour Conversation::restore(snapshot) . Le fournisseur/modèle doit correspondre. Garder les instances de fournisseur et l'executor en vie jusqu'à la fin des opérations asynchrones. Les callbacks s'exécutent sur le worker appelant, pas sur le thread UI.","headings":[{"id":"attachments","text":"Pièces jointes","level":2},{"id":"history","text":"Conserver une conversation","level":2},{"id":"resume","text":"Reprise et annulation","level":2},{"id":"api","text":"API C++ publique","level":2}],"anchors":[],"languages":[],"code":"","assets":[],"links":[],"kind":"guide","revision":"90cde8eec2e7"},{"id":"integration","title":"Intégrer la bibliothèque C++","description":"Lier uniquement les modules nécessaires et déporter les fournisseurs hors du thread UI.","section":"SDK","order":0,"sourceRevision":"1","locale":"fr","html":"\u003ch2 id=\"build\">Prérequis de compilation\u003ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#/fr/integration/build\" aria-label=\"Lien vers Prérequis de compilation\">#\u003c/a>\u003c/h2>\u003cp>Utiliser CMake 3.24+, C++20 et les threads système. Windows utilise Visual Studio 2022 C++,\nWindows SDK, WinHTTP et BCrypt. Linux/macOS utilisent les API POSIX et les fichiers de\ndéveloppement libcurl pour HTTP(S). Les limites de distribution multiplateforme actuelles\nfigurent dans les notes de version des sources.\u003c/p>\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block\">\u003cdiv class=\"code-toolbar\">\u003cspan>sh\u003c/span>\u003cbutton type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copier\u003c/button>\u003c/div>\u003cpre>\u003ccode class=\"language-bash\">\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L1\" data-line=\"1\">cmake \u003cspan class=\"token parameter variable\">-S\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token builtin class-name\">.\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token parameter variable\">-B\u003c/span> build \u003cspan class=\"token parameter variable\">-DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">=\u003c/span>Release\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L2\" data-line=\"2\">cmake \u003cspan class=\"token parameter variable\">--build\u003c/span> build \u003cspan class=\"token parameter variable\">--config\u003c/span> Release \u003cspan class=\"token parameter variable\">--parallel\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token number\">4\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L3\" data-line=\"3\">cmake \u003cspan class=\"token parameter variable\">--install\u003c/span> build \u003cspan class=\"token parameter variable\">--config\u003c/span> Release \u003cspan class=\"token parameter variable\">--prefix\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token function\">install\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003c/code>\u003c/pre>\u003c/div>\u003cp>Un hôte qui consomme l&#39;installation utilise les cibles exportées :\u003c/p>\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block\">\u003cdiv class=\"code-toolbar\">\u003cspan>cmake\u003c/span>\u003cbutton type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copier\u003c/button>\u003c/div>\u003cpre>\u003ccode class=\"language-cmake\">\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-2-L1\" data-line=\"1\">\u003cspan class=\"token keyword\">find_package\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">(\u003c/span>CyMCPSDK \u003cspan class=\"token number\">0.5\u003c/span> CONFIG REQUIRED\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">)\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-2-L2\" data-line=\"2\">\u003cspan class=\"token keyword\">target_link_libraries\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">(\u003c/span>my_app \u003cspan class=\"token namespace\">PRIVATE\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token inserted class-name\">CyMCP::Core\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token inserted class-name\">CyMCP::MCP\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token inserted class-name\">CyMCP::AI\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">)\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003c/code>\u003c/pre>\u003c/div>\u003cp>Autre possibilité : \u003ccode>add_subdirectory(external/CyMCPSDK)\u003c/code>. Désactiver les modules inutiles\navec \u003ccode>CYMCP_BUILD_HTTP\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>CYMCP_BUILD_PLATFORM\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>CYMCP_BUILD_MCP\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>CYMCP_BUILD_AI\u003c/code> et\n\u003ccode>CYMCP_BUILD_LOCAL\u003c/code> ; CMake vérifie leurs dépendances. \u003ccode>core-only\u003c/code> compile le cœur des opérations.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"providers\">Créer une conversation\u003ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#/fr/integration/providers\" aria-label=\"Lien vers Créer une conversation\">#\u003c/a>\u003c/h2>\u003cdiv class=\"code-block\">\u003cdiv class=\"code-toolbar\">\u003cspan>cpp\u003c/span>\u003cbutton type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copier\u003c/button>\u003c/div>\u003cpre>\u003ccode class=\"language-cpp\">\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-3-L1\" data-line=\"1\">\u003cspan class=\"token macro property\">\u003cspan class=\"token directive-hash\">#\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token directive keyword\">include\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token string\">&lt;cymcp/ai.hpp>\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-3-L2\" data-line=\"2\"> \u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-3-L3\" data-line=\"3\">cymcp\u003cspan class=\"token double-colon punctuation\">::\u003c/span>ProviderRegistry providers\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-3-L4\" data-line=\"4\">cymcp\u003cspan class=\"token double-colon punctuation\">::\u003c/span>ProviderConfig config\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-3-L5\" data-line=\"5\">config\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">.\u003c/span>settings\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">[\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token string\">\"base_url\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">]\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token operator\">=\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token string\">\"http://127.0.0.1:11434\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-3-L6\" data-line=\"6\">\u003cspan class=\"token keyword\">auto\u003c/span> provider \u003cspan class=\"token operator\">=\u003c/span> providers\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">.\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token function\">create\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">(\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token string\">\"ollama\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span> config\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">)\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003c/code>\u003c/pre>\u003c/div>\u003cp>Construire \u003ccode>Conversation(provider, model_id)\u003c/code> avec l&#39;ID réel d&#39;un modèle installé, puis appeler\n\u003ccode>connect()\u003c/code> et \u003ccode>send(text_block(prompt))\u003c/code>. Ces appels synchrones s&#39;exécutent sur un worker.\n\u003ccode>send_async(executor, content, context)\u003c/code> retourne un futur ; garder executor et fournisseur en vie.\n\u003ccode>CallContext.events\u003c/code> reçoit les deltas et l&#39;activité. Les transférer par \u003ccode>EventQueue\u003c/code> vers\nl&#39;interface. \u003ccode>cancel()\u003c/code> demande l&#39;annulation ; \u003ccode>reconnect()\u003c/code> reste explicite.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"chat-ui\">Intégrer le panneau CyUI\u003ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#/fr/integration/chat-ui\" aria-label=\"Lien vers Intégrer le panneau CyUI\">#\u003c/a>\u003c/h2>\u003cp>\u003ccode>CYMCP_BUILD_CHAT_UI\u003c/code> et \u003ccode>CYMCP_BUILD_CHAT_APP\u003c/code> sont désactivés par défaut. L&#39;hôte fournit\n\u003ccode>CyUI::DocumentViews\u003c/code>, ou renseigne \u003ccode>CYMCP_CYUI_SOURCE_DIR\u003c/code> avec une copie compatible de CyUI.\nUn consommateur installé crée sa cible CyUI avant de demander \u003ccode>COMPONENTS ChatUI\u003c/code>.\u003c/p>\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block\">\u003cdiv class=\"code-toolbar\">\u003cspan>cpp\u003c/span>\u003cbutton type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copier\u003c/button>\u003c/div>\u003cpre>\u003ccode class=\"language-cpp\">\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-4-L1\" data-line=\"1\">\u003cspan class=\"token macro property\">\u003cspan class=\"token directive-hash\">#\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token directive keyword\">include\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token string\">&lt;cymcp/chat_ui.hpp>\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-4-L2\" data-line=\"2\"> \u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-4-L3\" data-line=\"3\">\u003cspan class=\"token comment\">// Après la création du contexte ImGui et l'initialisation de CyUI par l'hôte :\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-4-L4\" data-line=\"4\">cymcp\u003cspan class=\"token double-colon punctuation\">::\u003c/span>ChatController controller\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-4-L5\" data-line=\"5\">cymcp\u003cspan class=\"token double-colon punctuation\">::\u003c/span>ChatPanel \u003cspan class=\"token function\">panel\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">(\u003c/span>controller\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">)\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-4-L6\" data-line=\"6\"> \u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-4-L7\" data-line=\"7\">\u003cspan class=\"token comment\">// Dans la fenêtre hôte, entre NewFrame et Render :\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-4-L8\" data-line=\"8\">panel\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">.\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token function\">draw\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">(\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">)\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003c/code>\u003c/pre>\u003c/div>\u003cp>\u003ccode>ChatController::open(ChatConnection)\u003c/code> programme la connexion. \u003ccode>send\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>refresh_models\u003c/code>,\n\u003ccode>save\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>disconnect\u003c/code> et \u003ccode>reconnect\u003c/code> programment aussi des opérations sur le worker ; \u003ccode>poll\u003c/code>\ntransfère leurs résultats. Utiliser le contrôleur et son état depuis un seul thread UI hôte.\nLe détruire avant le contexte ImGui et les modules fournisseurs. Son destructeur annule et attend le worker.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>\u003ccode>ChatPanelOptions\u003c/code> fournit la sélection des fichiers, l&#39;ouverture des liens et les ressources\nde documents en cache. Sans callback de lien, le panneau propose le lien à copier.\nInitialiser la locale CyUI de l&#39;hôte à \u003ccode>en\u003c/code> pour l&#39;anglais ; c&#39;est le défaut de l&#39;exemple Windows.\u003c/p>\n","text":"Prérequis de compilation # Utiliser CMake 3.24+, C++20 et les threads système. Windows utilise Visual Studio 2022 C++, Windows SDK, WinHTTP et BCrypt. Linux/macOS utilisent les API POSIX et les fichiers de développement libcurl pour HTTP(S). Les limites de distribution multiplateforme actuelles figurent dans les notes de version des sources. sh Copier cmake -S . -B build -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE = Release cmake --build build --config Release --parallel 4 cmake --install build --config Release --prefix install Un hôte qui consomme l'installation utilise les cibles exportées : cmake Copier find_package ( CyMCPSDK 0.5 CONFIG REQUIRED ) target_link_libraries ( my_app PRIVATE CyMCP::Core CyMCP::MCP CyMCP::AI ) Autre possibilité : add_subdirectory(external/CyMCPSDK) . Désactiver les modules inutiles avec CYMCP_BUILD_HTTP , CYMCP_BUILD_PLATFORM , CYMCP_BUILD_MCP , CYMCP_BUILD_AI et CYMCP_BUILD_LOCAL ; CMake vérifie leurs dépendances. core-only compile le cœur des opérations. Créer une conversation # cpp Copier # include \u003ccymcp/ai.hpp> cymcp :: ProviderRegistry providers ; cymcp :: ProviderConfig config ; config . settings [ \"base_url\" ] = \"http://127.0.0.1:11434\" ; auto provider = providers . create ( \"ollama\" , config ) ; Construire Conversation(provider, model_id) avec l'ID réel d'un modèle installé, puis appeler connect() et send(text_block(prompt)) . Ces appels synchrones s'exécutent sur un worker. send_async(executor, content, context) retourne un futur ; garder executor et fournisseur en vie. CallContext.events reçoit les deltas et l'activité. Les transférer par EventQueue vers l'interface. cancel() demande l'annulation ; reconnect() reste explicite. Intégrer le panneau CyUI # CYMCP_BUILD_CHAT_UI et CYMCP_BUILD_CHAT_APP sont désactivés par défaut. L'hôte fournit CyUI::DocumentViews , ou renseigne CYMCP_CYUI_SOURCE_DIR avec une copie compatible de CyUI. Un consommateur installé crée sa cible CyUI avant de demander COMPONENTS ChatUI . cpp Copier # include \u003ccymcp/chat_ui.hpp> // Après la création du contexte ImGui et l'initialisation de CyUI par l'hôte : cymcp :: ChatController controller ; cymcp :: ChatPanel panel ( controller ) ; // Dans la fenêtre hôte, entre NewFrame et Render : panel . draw ( ) ; ChatController::open(ChatConnection) programme la connexion. send , refresh_models , save , disconnect et reconnect programment aussi des opérations sur le worker ; poll transfère leurs résultats. Utiliser le contrôleur et son état depuis un seul thread UI hôte. Le détruire avant le contexte ImGui et les modules fournisseurs. Son destructeur annule et attend le worker. ChatPanelOptions fournit la sélection des fichiers, l'ouverture des liens et les ressources de documents en cache. Sans callback de lien, le panneau propose le lien à copier. Initialiser la locale CyUI de l'hôte à en pour l'anglais ; c'est le défaut de l'exemple Windows. cmake -S . -B build -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release cmake --build build --config Release --parallel 4 cmake --install build --config Release --prefix install find_package(CyMCPSDK 0.5 CONFIG REQUIRED) target_link_libraries(my_app PRIVATE CyMCP::Core CyMCP::MCP CyMCP::AI) #include \u003ccymcp/ai.hpp> cymcp::ProviderRegistry providers; cymcp::ProviderConfig config; config.settings[\"base_url\"] = \"http://127.0.0.1:11434\"; auto provider = providers.create(\"ollama\", config); #include \u003ccymcp/chat_ui.hpp> // Après la création du contexte ImGui et l'initialisation de CyUI par l'hôte : cymcp::ChatController controller; cymcp::ChatPanel panel(controller); // Dans la fenêtre hôte, entre NewFrame et Render : panel.draw();","headings":[{"id":"build","text":"Prérequis de compilation","level":2},{"id":"providers","text":"Créer une conversation","level":2},{"id":"chat-ui","text":"Intégrer le panneau CyUI","level":2}],"anchors":["L1","L2","L3","code-2-L1","code-2-L2","code-3-L1","code-3-L2","code-3-L3","code-3-L4","code-3-L5","code-3-L6","code-4-L1","code-4-L2","code-4-L3","code-4-L4","code-4-L5","code-4-L6","code-4-L7","code-4-L8"],"languages":["bash","cmake","cpp"],"code":"cmake -S . -B build -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release\ncmake --build build --config Release --parallel 4\ncmake --install build --config Release --prefix install\nfind_package(CyMCPSDK 0.5 CONFIG REQUIRED)\ntarget_link_libraries(my_app PRIVATE CyMCP::Core CyMCP::MCP CyMCP::AI)\n#include \u003ccymcp/ai.hpp>\n\ncymcp::ProviderRegistry providers;\ncymcp::ProviderConfig config;\nconfig.settings[\"base_url\"] = \"http://127.0.0.1:11434\";\nauto provider = providers.create(\"ollama\", config);\n#include \u003ccymcp/chat_ui.hpp>\n\n// Après la création du contexte ImGui et l'initialisation de CyUI par l'hôte :\ncymcp::ChatController controller;\ncymcp::ChatPanel panel(controller);\n\n// Dans la fenêtre hôte, entre NewFrame et Render :\npanel.draw();","assets":[],"links":[],"kind":"guide","revision":"1ec77eb96cec"},{"id":"licenses","title":"Licences et composants","description":"Comprendre la licence MIT du SDK et les conditions des composants optionnels.","section":"Guides","parent":"overview","order":5,"sourceRevision":"1","locale":"fr","html":"\u003ch2 id=\"sdk\">CyMCPSDK\u003ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#/fr/licenses/sdk\" aria-label=\"Lien vers CyMCPSDK\">#\u003c/a>\u003c/h2>\u003cp>Copyright © 2026 Cyberalien. Les sources CyMCPSDK sont distribuées sous licence MIT.\nConserver copyright et autorisation dans les copies redistribuées. \u003ccode>LICENSE\u003c/code> et\n\u003ccode>THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md\u003c/code> à la racine des sources contiennent les conditions et notices des composants.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"components\">Composants\u003ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#/fr/licenses/components\" aria-label=\"Lien vers Composants\">#\u003c/a>\u003c/h2>\u003ctable>\n\u003cthead>\n\u003ctr>\n\u003cth>Composant\u003c/th>\n\u003cth>Licence\u003c/th>\n\u003cth>Périmètre\u003c/th>\n\u003c/tr>\n\u003c/thead>\n\u003ctbody>\u003ctr>\n\u003ctd>nlohmann/json 3.12.0\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>MIT\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>Représentation JSON et validation du SDK\u003c/td>\n\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\n\u003ctd>cpp-httplib 0.66.0\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>MIT\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>Serveur HTTP local et transports de test\u003c/td>\n\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\n\u003ctd>PicoSHA2\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>MIT\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>Vérification des artefacts\u003c/td>\n\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\n\u003ctd>libcurl système\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>Licence curl et conditions TLS de l&#39;hôte\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>HTTP(S) Linux/macOS\u003c/td>\n\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\n\u003ctd>CyUI, Dear ImGui, MD4C\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>MIT\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>Rendu du tchat natif optionnel\u003c/td>\n\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\n\u003ctd>Lexers Lexilla/Scintilla\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>Leurs notices permissives\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>Coloration du code optionnelle via CyUI\u003c/td>\n\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\n\u003ctd>JetBrains Mono\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>SIL Open Font License 1.1\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>Police embarquée par CyUI\u003c/td>\n\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\n\u003ctd>Lecteur CyDoc\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>MIT\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>Ce lecteur de documentation statique\u003c/td>\n\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\n\u003ctd>marked, PrismJS, esbuild\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>MIT\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>Outils de génération de documentation uniquement\u003c/td>\n\u003c/tr>\n\u003c/tbody>\u003c/table>\n\u003cp>Le paquet Windows contient les notices complètes de l&#39;UI optionnelle dans \u003ccode>licenses/\u003c/code>.\nCe manuel inclut les textes MIT du SDK et de CyDoc dans \u003ccode>DocData/\u003c/code>.\nLes moteurs d&#39;inférence, modèles et runtimes GPU ne prennent pas la licence MIT du SDK :\nles composants installés séparément et les services fournisseurs gardent leurs propres conditions.\u003c/p>\n","text":"CyMCPSDK # Copyright © 2026 Cyberalien. Les sources CyMCPSDK sont distribuées sous licence MIT. Conserver copyright et autorisation dans les copies redistribuées. LICENSE et THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md à la racine des sources contiennent les conditions et notices des composants. Composants # Composant Licence Périmètre nlohmann/json 3.12.0 MIT Représentation JSON et validation du SDK cpp-httplib 0.66.0 MIT Serveur HTTP local et transports de test PicoSHA2 MIT Vérification des artefacts libcurl système Licence curl et conditions TLS de l'hôte HTTP(S) Linux/macOS CyUI, Dear ImGui, MD4C MIT Rendu du tchat natif optionnel Lexers Lexilla/Scintilla Leurs notices permissives Coloration du code optionnelle via CyUI JetBrains Mono SIL Open Font License 1.1 Police embarquée par CyUI Lecteur CyDoc MIT Ce lecteur de documentation statique marked, PrismJS, esbuild MIT Outils de génération de documentation uniquement Le paquet Windows contient les notices complètes de l'UI optionnelle dans licenses/ . Ce manuel inclut les textes MIT du SDK et de CyDoc dans DocData/ . Les moteurs d'inférence, modèles et runtimes GPU ne prennent pas la licence MIT du SDK : les composants installés séparément et les services fournisseurs gardent leurs propres conditions.","headings":[{"id":"sdk","text":"CyMCPSDK","level":2},{"id":"components","text":"Composants","level":2}],"anchors":[],"languages":[],"code":"","assets":[],"links":[],"kind":"guide","revision":"06003b5b41cd"},{"id":"local-engines","title":"Moteurs locaux et dépendances","description":"Connecter un service existant ou superviser un moteur compatible llama.cpp installé.","section":"SDK","parent":"integration","order":3,"sourceRevision":"2","locale":"fr","html":"\u003ch2 id=\"service\">Utiliser un service existant\u003ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#/fr/local-engines/service\" aria-label=\"Lien vers Utiliser un service existant\">#\u003c/a>\u003c/h2>\u003cp>Choisir \u003ccode>ollama\u003c/code> pour l&#39;API native Ollama, \u003ccode>lmstudio\u003c/code> pour son serveur compatible, ou \u003ccode>llama.cpp\u003c/code>\npour une adresse compatible déjà active. Renseigner l&#39;URL réelle du service et un modèle qu&#39;il propose.\nChoisir un profil fournisseur n&#39;installe ni ne lance ce produit.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>Chat Lab se connecte aux services locaux. Il ne propose pas encore d&#39;installateur de modèles ou de\npaquets GPU. L&#39;application qui intègre le SDK peut fournir son propre parcours d&#39;installation.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"supervise\">Superviser un moteur natif\u003ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#/fr/local-engines/supervise\" aria-label=\"Lien vers Superviser un moteur natif\">#\u003c/a>\u003c/h2>\u003cp>\u003ccode>LocalEngine\u003c/code> possède un processus enfant compatible llama.cpp. Ses options comprennent le chemin\nde l&#39;exécutable, le modèle, un dossier de travail privé, le contexte en tokens, les couches GPU et le\ndélai de démarrage. Exécutable et modèle doivent déjà exister et être compatibles.\u003c/p>\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block\">\u003cdiv class=\"code-toolbar\">\u003cspan>cpp\u003c/span>\u003cbutton type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copier\u003c/button>\u003c/div>\u003cpre>\u003ccode class=\"language-cpp\">\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L1\" data-line=\"1\">\u003cspan class=\"token macro property\">\u003cspan class=\"token directive-hash\">#\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token directive keyword\">include\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token string\">&lt;cymcp/local.hpp>\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L2\" data-line=\"2\"> \u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L3\" data-line=\"3\">\u003cspan class=\"token keyword\">void\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token function\">start_local\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">(\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token keyword\">const\u003c/span> std\u003cspan class=\"token double-colon punctuation\">::\u003c/span>filesystem\u003cspan class=\"token double-colon punctuation\">::\u003c/span>path\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">&amp;\u003c/span> server_executable\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L4\" data-line=\"4\">                 \u003cspan class=\"token keyword\">const\u003c/span> std\u003cspan class=\"token double-colon punctuation\">::\u003c/span>filesystem\u003cspan class=\"token double-colon punctuation\">::\u003c/span>path\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">&amp;\u003c/span> model\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L5\" data-line=\"5\">                 \u003cspan class=\"token keyword\">const\u003c/span> std\u003cspan class=\"token double-colon punctuation\">::\u003c/span>filesystem\u003cspan class=\"token double-colon punctuation\">::\u003c/span>path\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">&amp;\u003c/span> private_work_directory\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">)\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">{\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L6\" data-line=\"6\">    cymcp\u003cspan class=\"token double-colon punctuation\">::\u003c/span>LocalEngineOptions options\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L7\" data-line=\"7\">    options\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">.\u003c/span>process\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">.\u003c/span>executable \u003cspan class=\"token operator\">=\u003c/span> server_executable\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L8\" data-line=\"8\">    options\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">.\u003c/span>model \u003cspan class=\"token operator\">=\u003c/span> model\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L9\" data-line=\"9\">    options\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">.\u003c/span>private_work_directory \u003cspan class=\"token operator\">=\u003c/span> private_work_directory\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L10\" data-line=\"10\">    cymcp\u003cspan class=\"token double-colon punctuation\">::\u003c/span>LocalEngine \u003cspan class=\"token function\">engine\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">(\u003c/span>options\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">)\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L11\" data-line=\"11\">    engine\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">.\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token function\">start\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">(\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">)\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L12\" data-line=\"12\">    \u003cspan class=\"token comment\">// Pendant la vie de engine, configurer un fournisseur API avec\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L13\" data-line=\"13\">    \u003cspan class=\"token comment\">// engine.base_url() et engine.token(), puis exécuter la conversation hôte.\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L14\" data-line=\"14\">    engine\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">.\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token function\">stop\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">(\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">)\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L15\" data-line=\"15\">\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">}\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003c/code>\u003c/pre>\u003c/div>\u003cp>Garder le moteur en vie jusqu&#39;à la fin des conversations. Le superviseur vérifie sa disponibilité,\nfournit un fichier d&#39;authentification privé et arrête l&#39;arbre de processus qu&#39;il possède. Il ne gère pas\nun service utilisateur indépendant. Choisir les paramètres GPU selon le moteur et le runtime installés ;\naucun composant GPU n&#39;est embarqué.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"dependencies\">Télécharger des composants vérifiés\u003ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#/fr/local-engines/dependencies\" aria-label=\"Lien vers Télécharger des composants vérifiés\">#\u003c/a>\u003c/h2>\u003cp>\u003ccode>DependencyManager\u003c/code> reçoit un manifeste \u003ccode>Package\u003c/code> de confiance fourni par l&#39;hôte : URL des artefacts,\nchemins relatifs, tailles, empreintes SHA-256 et arguments d&#39;installation éventuels. Il propose\n\u003ccode>install\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>verify\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>run_installer\u003c/code> et \u003ccode>uninstall\u003c/code>. La politique hôte décide des actions permises ;\nun callback d&#39;élévation gère les installateurs qui en ont besoin.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>L&#39;application contrôle les manifestes, jamais la sortie d&#39;un modèle. Les chemins restent dans le cache\nconfiguré ; HTTPS et les hôtes de redirection déclarés encadrent les téléchargements. Les paquets\nexternes gardent leurs licences. L’hôte peut déclarer des fichiers ordinaires dans une archive avec\nleur destination, leur taille et leur SHA-256. Le lecteur tar du système les extrait dans un dossier\nprivé avant publication.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>Sous Windows x64, sélectionner un service local dans \u003cstrong>Fournisseurs\u003c/strong> de Chat Lab, ouvrir\n\u003cstrong>Installation et connexion\u003c/strong> puis choisir \u003cstrong>Installer le runtime NVIDIA CUDA 12\u003c/strong>. Chat Lab\ntélécharge NVIDIA CUDART 12.8.90 et sa licence dans le cache privé de l’utilisateur. Il affiche le\ndossier du runtime après vérification. Un pilote NVIDIA compatible et les éventuelles autres\nbibliothèques exigées par le moteur choisi sont des prérequis distincts.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>Les applications Windows et Linux x64 peuvent exécuter la même installation sur un worker et\nfournir le dossier à un moteur supervisé. Le superviseur applique le chemin de recherche des\nbibliothèques au processus enfant.\u003c/p>\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block\">\u003cdiv class=\"code-toolbar\">\u003cspan>cpp\u003c/span>\u003cbutton type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copier\u003c/button>\u003c/div>\u003cpre>\u003ccode class=\"language-cpp\">\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-2-L1\" data-line=\"1\">cymcp\u003cspan class=\"token double-colon punctuation\">::\u003c/span>DependencyManager \u003cspan class=\"token function\">dependencies\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">(\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">{\u003c/span>cache_prive\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span> politique_hote\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">}\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">)\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-2-L2\" data-line=\"2\">\u003cspan class=\"token keyword\">auto\u003c/span> installation \u003cspan class=\"token operator\">=\u003c/span> dependencies\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">.\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token function\">install\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">(\u003c/span>cymcp\u003cspan class=\"token double-colon punctuation\">::\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token function\">cuda_runtime_package\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">(\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">)\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span> contexte\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">)\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-2-L3\" data-line=\"3\">options\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">.\u003c/span>cuda_runtime_directory \u003cspan class=\"token operator\">=\u003c/span> installation \u003cspan class=\"token operator\">/\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token string\">\"runtime\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token comment\">// LocalEngineOptions\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003c/code>\u003c/pre>\u003c/div>\u003cp>Les empreintes proviennent du \u003ca href=\"https://developer.download.nvidia.com/compute/cuda/redist/redistrib_12.8.1.json\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">manifeste de redistribution NVIDIA CUDA 12.8.1\u003c/a>.\nLe paquet installé contient la licence NVIDIA. La reprise HTTP Range et la sélection automatique du GPU restent à réaliser.\u003c/p>\n","text":"Utiliser un service existant # Choisir ollama pour l'API native Ollama, lmstudio pour son serveur compatible, ou llama.cpp pour une adresse compatible déjà active. Renseigner l'URL réelle du service et un modèle qu'il propose. Choisir un profil fournisseur n'installe ni ne lance ce produit. Chat Lab se connecte aux services locaux. Il ne propose pas encore d'installateur de modèles ou de paquets GPU. L'application qui intègre le SDK peut fournir son propre parcours d'installation. Superviser un moteur natif # LocalEngine possède un processus enfant compatible llama.cpp. Ses options comprennent le chemin de l'exécutable, le modèle, un dossier de travail privé, le contexte en tokens, les couches GPU et le délai de démarrage. Exécutable et modèle doivent déjà exister et être compatibles. cpp Copier # include \u003ccymcp/local.hpp> void start_local ( const std :: filesystem :: path & server_executable , const std :: filesystem :: path & model , const std :: filesystem :: path & private_work_directory ) { cymcp :: LocalEngineOptions options ; options . process . executable = server_executable ; options . model = model ; options . private_work_directory = private_work_directory ; cymcp :: LocalEngine engine ( options ) ; engine . start ( ) ; // Pendant la vie de engine, configurer un fournisseur API avec // engine.base_url() et engine.token(), puis exécuter la conversation hôte. engine . stop ( ) ; } Garder le moteur en vie jusqu'à la fin des conversations. Le superviseur vérifie sa disponibilité, fournit un fichier d'authentification privé et arrête l'arbre de processus qu'il possède. Il ne gère pas un service utilisateur indépendant. Choisir les paramètres GPU selon le moteur et le runtime installés ; aucun composant GPU n'est embarqué. Télécharger des composants vérifiés # DependencyManager reçoit un manifeste Package de confiance fourni par l'hôte : URL des artefacts, chemins relatifs, tailles, empreintes SHA-256 et arguments d'installation éventuels. Il propose install , verify , run_installer et uninstall . La politique hôte décide des actions permises ; un callback d'élévation gère les installateurs qui en ont besoin. L'application contrôle les manifestes, jamais la sortie d'un modèle. Les chemins restent dans le cache configuré ; HTTPS et les hôtes de redirection déclarés encadrent les téléchargements. Les paquets externes gardent leurs licences. L’hôte peut déclarer des fichiers ordinaires dans une archive avec leur destination, leur taille et leur SHA-256. Le lecteur tar du système les extrait dans un dossier privé avant publication. Sous Windows x64, sélectionner un service local dans Fournisseurs de Chat Lab, ouvrir Installation et connexion puis choisir Installer le runtime NVIDIA CUDA 12 . Chat Lab télécharge NVIDIA CUDART 12.8.90 et sa licence dans le cache privé de l’utilisateur. Il affiche le dossier du runtime après vérification. Un pilote NVIDIA compatible et les éventuelles autres bibliothèques exigées par le moteur choisi sont des prérequis distincts. Les applications Windows et Linux x64 peuvent exécuter la même installation sur un worker et fournir le dossier à un moteur supervisé. Le superviseur applique le chemin de recherche des bibliothèques au processus enfant. cpp Copier cymcp :: DependencyManager dependencies ( { cache_prive , politique_hote } ) ; auto installation = dependencies . install ( cymcp :: cuda_runtime_package ( ) , contexte ) ; options . cuda_runtime_directory = installation / \"runtime\" ; // LocalEngineOptions Les empreintes proviennent du manifeste de redistribution NVIDIA CUDA 12.8.1 . Le paquet installé contient la licence NVIDIA. La reprise HTTP Range et la sélection automatique du GPU restent à réaliser. #include \u003ccymcp/local.hpp> void start_local(const std::filesystem::path& server_executable, const std::filesystem::path& model, const std::filesystem::path& private_work_directory) { cymcp::LocalEngineOptions options; options.process.executable = server_executable; options.model = model; options.private_work_directory = private_work_directory; cymcp::LocalEngine engine(options); engine.start(); // Pendant la vie de engine, configurer un fournisseur API avec // engine.base_url() et engine.token(), puis exécuter la conversation hôte. engine.stop(); } cymcp::DependencyManager dependencies({cache_prive, politique_hote}); auto installation = dependencies.install(cymcp::cuda_runtime_package(), contexte); options.cuda_runtime_directory = installation / \"runtime\"; // LocalEngineOptions","headings":[{"id":"service","text":"Utiliser un service existant","level":2},{"id":"supervise","text":"Superviser un moteur natif","level":2},{"id":"dependencies","text":"Télécharger des composants vérifiés","level":2}],"anchors":["L1","L2","L3","L4","L5","L6","L7","L8","L9","L10","L11","L12","L13","L14","L15","code-2-L1","code-2-L2","code-2-L3"],"languages":["cpp"],"code":"#include \u003ccymcp/local.hpp>\n\nvoid start_local(const std::filesystem::path& server_executable,\n                 const std::filesystem::path& model,\n                 const std::filesystem::path& private_work_directory) {\n    cymcp::LocalEngineOptions options;\n    options.process.executable = server_executable;\n    options.model = model;\n    options.private_work_directory = private_work_directory;\n    cymcp::LocalEngine engine(options);\n    engine.start();\n    // Pendant la vie de engine, configurer un fournisseur API avec\n    // engine.base_url() et engine.token(), puis exécuter la conversation hôte.\n    engine.stop();\n}\ncymcp::DependencyManager dependencies({cache_prive, politique_hote});\nauto installation = dependencies.install(cymcp::cuda_runtime_package(), contexte);\noptions.cuda_runtime_directory = installation / \"runtime\"; // LocalEngineOptions","assets":[],"links":["https://developer.download.nvidia.com/compute/cuda/redist/redistrib_12.8.1.json"],"kind":"guide","revision":"1afbf55b97bf"},{"id":"operations","title":"Exposer les opérations de l'app","description":"Partager un registre typé entre appels natifs, SDK JSON, MCP et outils IA compatibles.","section":"SDK","parent":"integration","order":1,"sourceRevision":"2","locale":"fr","html":"\u003ch2 id=\"registry\">Définir un registre\u003ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#/fr/operations/registry\" aria-label=\"Lien vers Définir un registre\">#\u003c/a>\u003c/h2>\u003cp>Une \u003ccode>Operation\u003c/code> contient un nom portable, une description, des schémas objet d&#39;entrée/sortie,\nun indicateur de lecture seule et un handler. \u003ccode>Registry\u003c/code> valide les entrées, applique sa politique\net vérifie les sorties déclarées. L&#39;indicateur de lecture seule ne remplace pas une politique de refus.\u003c/p>\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block\">\u003cdiv class=\"code-toolbar\">\u003cspan>cpp\u003c/span>\u003cbutton type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copier\u003c/button>\u003c/div>\u003cpre>\u003ccode class=\"language-cpp\">\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L1\" data-line=\"1\">\u003cspan class=\"token macro property\">\u003cspan class=\"token directive-hash\">#\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token directive keyword\">include\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token string\">&lt;cymcp/core.hpp>\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L2\" data-line=\"2\"> \u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L3\" data-line=\"3\">cymcp\u003cspan class=\"token double-colon punctuation\">::\u003c/span>Registry \u003cspan class=\"token function\">commands\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">(\u003c/span>cymcp\u003cspan class=\"token double-colon punctuation\">::\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token class-name\">Policy\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token double-colon punctuation\">::\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token function\">allow_all\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">(\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">)\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">)\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L4\" data-line=\"4\">commands\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">.\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token function\">add\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">(\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">{\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token string\">\"get_counter\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token string\">\"Lire le compteur de démonstration.\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L5\" data-line=\"5\">    \u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">{\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">{\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token string\">\"type\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token string\">\"object\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">}\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">{\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token string\">\"additionalProperties\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token boolean\">false\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">}\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">}\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L6\" data-line=\"6\">    \u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">{\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">{\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token string\">\"type\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token string\">\"object\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">}\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L7\" data-line=\"7\">     \u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">{\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token string\">\"properties\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">{\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">{\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token string\">\"value\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">{\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">{\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token string\">\"type\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token string\">\"integer\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">}\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">}\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">}\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">}\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">}\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L8\" data-line=\"8\">     \u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">{\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token string\">\"required\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">{\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token string\">\"value\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">}\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">}\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">{\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token string\">\"additionalProperties\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token boolean\">false\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">}\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">}\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L9\" data-line=\"9\">    \u003cspan class=\"token boolean\">true\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L10\" data-line=\"10\">    \u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">[\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">]\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">(\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token keyword\">const\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token keyword\">auto\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">&amp;\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token keyword\">const\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token keyword\">auto\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">&amp;\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">)\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">{\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token keyword\">return\u003c/span> cymcp\u003cspan class=\"token double-colon punctuation\">::\u003c/span>Json\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">{\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">{\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token string\">\"value\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token number\">42\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">}\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">}\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">}\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">}\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">)\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L11\" data-line=\"11\">\u003cspan class=\"token keyword\">auto\u003c/span> result \u003cspan class=\"token operator\">=\u003c/span> commands\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">.\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token function\">invoke\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">(\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token string\">\"get_counter\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span> cymcp\u003cspan class=\"token double-colon punctuation\">::\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token class-name\">Json\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token double-colon punctuation\">::\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token function\">object\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">(\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">)\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">)\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003c/code>\u003c/pre>\u003c/div>\u003cp>Cet exemple autorise explicitement sa lecture sans effet de bord. Pour un domaine modifiable,\nutiliser la politique de l&#39;hôte et synchroniser ses objets. Les handlers MCP peuvent être concurrents ;\ntransférer les mutations liées à l&#39;UI vers la boucle d&#39;événements et garder les données capturées en vie.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"sdk\">SDK JSON direct\u003ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#/fr/operations/sdk\" aria-label=\"Lien vers SDK JSON direct\">#\u003c/a>\u003c/h2>\u003cp>\u003ccode>dispatch_app(registry, request, context)\u003c/code> accepte ces messages applicatifs :\u003c/p>\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block\">\u003cdiv class=\"code-toolbar\">\u003cspan>json\u003c/span>\u003cbutton type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copier\u003c/button>\u003c/div>\u003cpre>\u003ccode class=\"language-json\">\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-2-L1\" data-line=\"1\">\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">{\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token property\">\"method\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">:\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token string\">\"describe\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">}\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003c/code>\u003c/pre>\u003c/div>\u003cdiv class=\"code-block\">\u003cdiv class=\"code-toolbar\">\u003cspan>json\u003c/span>\u003cbutton type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copier\u003c/button>\u003c/div>\u003cpre>\u003ccode class=\"language-json\">\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-3-L1\" data-line=\"1\">\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">{\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token property\">\"method\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">:\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token string\">\"invoke\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token property\">\"name\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">:\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token string\">\"get_counter\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token property\">\"arguments\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">:\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">{\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">}\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">}\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003c/code>\u003c/pre>\u003c/div>\u003cp>Le CLI d&#39;exemple propose \u003ccode>describe\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>invoke\u003c/code> et le JSONL applicatif sur stdin. JSONL applicatif et\nJSON-RPC MCP sont deux protocoles distincts. Dans Chat Lab, ces mêmes requêtes vont vers \u003ccode>/v1\u003c/code>\nsur le serveur local activé, avec \u003ccode>Content-Type: application/json\u003c/code> et le jeton Bearer.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"mcp\">Serveur et client MCP\u003ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#/fr/operations/mcp\" aria-label=\"Lien vers Serveur et client MCP\">#\u003c/a>\u003c/h2>\u003cp>\u003ccode>McpServer(registry)\u003c/code> expose les opérations comme outils MCP. \u003ccode>serve_stdio(input, output)\u003c/code> sert\nune connexion CLI ; \u003ccode>handle(request, context)\u003c/code> s&#39;intègre à un endpoint HTTP. Garder registre et\nserveur en vie pendant toute la connexion.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>\u003ccode>McpClient(ProcessOptions)\u003c/code> se connecte par stdio ; \u003ccode>McpClient(url, token)\u003c/code> utilise HTTP local\nlorsque ce support est compilé. Appeler \u003ccode>connect\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>list_tools\u003c/code> et \u003ccode>call_tool(name, arguments)\u003c/code>.\nVérifier \u003ccode>isError\u003c/code> dans le résultat MCP avant de traiter \u003ccode>structuredContent\u003c/code> comme une sortie réussie.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>Pour qu&#39;une IA dans l&#39;app A utilise l&#39;app B, connecter un client à B, enregistrer des opérations\nde transfert explicites dans A et attacher ce registre à un fournisseur compatible. Conserver le\nschéma de B et appliquer la politique de A avant le transfert. Une réponse de modèle ne doit pas\npouvoir enregistrer librement de nouvelles opérations.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"tools\">Attacher les outils à une conversation\u003ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#/fr/operations/tools\" aria-label=\"Lien vers Attacher les outils à une conversation\">#\u003c/a>\u003c/h2>\u003cp>Fournir un registre partagé dans \u003ccode>ProviderConfig.tools\u003c/code> pour les API compatibles ou les outils\ndynamiques Codex. Ce registre porte la politique des opérations réelles de l&#39;app. Pour les autres\nCLI, exposer MCP et passer leur configuration MCP native. ACP utilise \u003ccode>settings.mcp_servers\u003c/code>\nsous forme de tableau au format ACP. Consulter les \u003ca href=\"#/fr/permissions\">droits\u003c/a> avant d&#39;exposer des mutations.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>Voir \u003ca href=\"#/fr/optimization\">les outils à la demande, ressources et grep\u003c/a> pour réduire les échanges\ntout en conservant toutes les commandes et leur politique d&#39;accès.\u003c/p>\n","text":"Définir un registre # Une Operation contient un nom portable, une description, des schémas objet d'entrée/sortie, un indicateur de lecture seule et un handler. Registry valide les entrées, applique sa politique et vérifie les sorties déclarées. L'indicateur de lecture seule ne remplace pas une politique de refus. cpp Copier # include \u003ccymcp/core.hpp> cymcp :: Registry commands ( cymcp :: Policy :: allow_all ( ) ) ; commands . add ( { \"get_counter\" , \"Lire le compteur de démonstration.\" , { { \"type\" , \"object\" } , { \"additionalProperties\" , false } } , { { \"type\" , \"object\" } , { \"properties\" , { { \"value\" , { { \"type\" , \"integer\" } } } } } , { \"required\" , { \"value\" } } , { \"additionalProperties\" , false } } , true , [ ] ( const auto & , const auto & ) { return cymcp :: Json { { \"value\" , 42 } } ; } } ) ; auto result = commands . invoke ( \"get_counter\" , cymcp :: Json :: object ( ) ) ; Cet exemple autorise explicitement sa lecture sans effet de bord. Pour un domaine modifiable, utiliser la politique de l'hôte et synchroniser ses objets. Les handlers MCP peuvent être concurrents ; transférer les mutations liées à l'UI vers la boucle d'événements et garder les données capturées en vie. SDK JSON direct # dispatch_app(registry, request, context) accepte ces messages applicatifs : json Copier { \"method\" : \"describe\" } json Copier { \"method\" : \"invoke\" , \"name\" : \"get_counter\" , \"arguments\" : { } } Le CLI d'exemple propose describe , invoke et le JSONL applicatif sur stdin. JSONL applicatif et JSON-RPC MCP sont deux protocoles distincts. Dans Chat Lab, ces mêmes requêtes vont vers /v1 sur le serveur local activé, avec Content-Type: application/json et le jeton Bearer. Serveur et client MCP # McpServer(registry) expose les opérations comme outils MCP. serve_stdio(input, output) sert une connexion CLI ; handle(request, context) s'intègre à un endpoint HTTP. Garder registre et serveur en vie pendant toute la connexion. McpClient(ProcessOptions) se connecte par stdio ; McpClient(url, token) utilise HTTP local lorsque ce support est compilé. Appeler connect , list_tools et call_tool(name, arguments) . Vérifier isError dans le résultat MCP avant de traiter structuredContent comme une sortie réussie. Pour qu'une IA dans l'app A utilise l'app B, connecter un client à B, enregistrer des opérations de transfert explicites dans A et attacher ce registre à un fournisseur compatible. Conserver le schéma de B et appliquer la politique de A avant le transfert. Une réponse de modèle ne doit pas pouvoir enregistrer librement de nouvelles opérations. Attacher les outils à une conversation # Fournir un registre partagé dans ProviderConfig.tools pour les API compatibles ou les outils dynamiques Codex. Ce registre porte la politique des opérations réelles de l'app. Pour les autres CLI, exposer MCP et passer leur configuration MCP native. ACP utilise settings.mcp_servers sous forme de tableau au format ACP. Consulter les droits avant d'exposer des mutations. Voir les outils à la demande, ressources et grep pour réduire les échanges tout en conservant toutes les commandes et leur politique d'accès. #include \u003ccymcp/core.hpp> cymcp::Registry commands(cymcp::Policy::allow_all()); commands.add({\"get_counter\", \"Lire le compteur de démonstration.\", {{\"type\", \"object\"}, {\"additionalProperties\", false}}, {{\"type\", \"object\"}, {\"properties\", {{\"value\", {{\"type\", \"integer\"}}}}}, {\"required\", {\"value\"}}, {\"additionalProperties\", false}}, true, [](const auto&, const auto&) { return cymcp::Json{{\"value\", 42}}; }}); auto result = commands.invoke(\"get_counter\", cymcp::Json::object()); {\"method\":\"describe\"} {\"method\":\"invoke\",\"name\":\"get_counter\",\"arguments\":{}}","headings":[{"id":"registry","text":"Définir un registre","level":2},{"id":"sdk","text":"SDK JSON direct","level":2},{"id":"mcp","text":"Serveur et client MCP","level":2},{"id":"tools","text":"Attacher les outils à une conversation","level":2}],"anchors":["L1","L2","L3","L4","L5","L6","L7","L8","L9","L10","L11","code-2-L1","code-3-L1"],"languages":["cpp","json"],"code":"#include \u003ccymcp/core.hpp>\n\ncymcp::Registry commands(cymcp::Policy::allow_all());\ncommands.add({\"get_counter\", \"Lire le compteur de démonstration.\",\n    {{\"type\", \"object\"}, {\"additionalProperties\", false}},\n    {{\"type\", \"object\"},\n     {\"properties\", {{\"value\", {{\"type\", \"integer\"}}}}},\n     {\"required\", {\"value\"}}, {\"additionalProperties\", false}},\n    true,\n    [](const auto&, const auto&) { return cymcp::Json{{\"value\", 42}}; }});\nauto result = commands.invoke(\"get_counter\", cymcp::Json::object());\n{\"method\":\"describe\"}\n{\"method\":\"invoke\",\"name\":\"get_counter\",\"arguments\":{}}","assets":[],"links":["#/fr/permissions","#/fr/optimization"],"kind":"guide","revision":"698f192b1d02"},{"id":"optimization","title":"Outils à la demande, ressources et grep","description":"Garder toutes les commandes accessibles en réduisant les catalogues et les résultats transmis.","section":"SDK","parent":"integration","order":2,"sourceRevision":"2","locale":"fr","html":"\u003ch2 id=\"tools\">Découvrir sans perdre de fonctions\u003ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#/fr/optimization/tools\" aria-label=\"Lien vers Découvrir sans perdre de fonctions\">#\u003c/a>\u003c/h2>\u003cp>Le \u003ca href=\"#/fr/runtime-options\">stockage disque, les mesures, les abonnements et les fenêtres de contexte API\u003c/a>\ncomplètent ces fonctions par des options indépendantes, désactivées par défaut.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>\u003ccode>Registry\u003c/code> reste la référence. Les appels SDK directs et les outils MCP classiques gardent leurs\nnoms, arguments, schémas de sortie et droits. \u003ccode>describe()\u003c/code> renvoie toujours le catalogue complet.\nLes instantanés immuables \u003ccode>catalogue()\u003c/code> et \u003ccode>summaries()\u003c/code> (sans schémas) sont réutilisés jusqu&#39;à un\n\u003ccode>add\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>replace\u003c/code> ou \u003ccode>remove\u003c/code> ; \u003ccode>describe(name)\u003c/code> charge une définition complète précise.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>\u003ccode>ToolGateway\u003c/code> expose cinq outils standard à la place de toutes les définitions :\u003c/p>\n\u003ctable>\n\u003cthead>\n\u003ctr>\n\u003cth>Outil\u003c/th>\n\u003cth>Fonction\u003c/th>\n\u003c/tr>\n\u003c/thead>\n\u003ctbody>\u003ctr>\n\u003ctd>\u003ccode>cy_tools_search\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>Rechercher noms/descriptions ; sans query, parcourir toutes les commandes. Suivre nextCursor avec la même query.\u003c/td>\n\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\n\u003ctd>\u003ccode>cy_tools_describe\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>Obtenir un schéma d&#39;entrée/sortie complet.\u003c/td>\n\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\n\u003ctd>\u003ccode>cy_tools_call\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>Appeler la commande d&#39;origine avec ses arguments et le contexte de l&#39;appelant.\u003c/td>\n\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\n\u003ctd>\u003ccode>cy_resources_read\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>Lire une ressource, un manifeste ou un morceau.\u003c/td>\n\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\n\u003ctd>\u003ccode>cy_resources_grep\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>Rechercher dans les ressources texte sans charger tout leur contenu.\u003c/td>\n\u003c/tr>\n\u003c/tbody>\u003c/table>\n\u003cp>Recherche et description n&#39;exécutent aucune commande. L&#39;appel valide les schémas d&#39;origine\net applique leur politique, y compris l&#39;autorisation totale explicite. Aucune commande n&#39;est\ndéfinitivement masquée. Un changement de registre invalide les curseurs de recherche.\u003c/p>\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block\">\u003cdiv class=\"code-toolbar\">\u003cspan>cpp\u003c/span>\u003cbutton type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copier\u003c/button>\u003c/div>\u003cpre>\u003ccode class=\"language-cpp\">\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L1\" data-line=\"1\">\u003cspan class=\"token macro property\">\u003cspan class=\"token directive-hash\">#\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token directive keyword\">include\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token string\">&lt;cymcp/mcp.hpp>\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L2\" data-line=\"2\">\u003cspan class=\"token macro property\">\u003cspan class=\"token directive-hash\">#\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token directive keyword\">include\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token string\">&lt;cymcp/resources.hpp>\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L3\" data-line=\"3\"> \u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L4\" data-line=\"4\">\u003cspan class=\"token keyword\">auto\u003c/span> commands \u003cspan class=\"token operator\">=\u003c/span> std\u003cspan class=\"token double-colon punctuation\">::\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token generic-function\">\u003cspan class=\"token function\">make_shared\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token generic class-name\">\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">&lt;\u003c/span>cymcp\u003cspan class=\"token double-colon punctuation\">::\u003c/span>Registry\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">>\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">(\u003c/span>host_policy\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">)\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L5\" data-line=\"5\">\u003cspan class=\"token comment\">// Enregistrer toutes les opérations de l'application dans commands.\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L6\" data-line=\"6\">cymcp\u003cspan class=\"token double-colon punctuation\">::\u003c/span>ToolGateway \u003cspan class=\"token function\">gateway\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">(\u003c/span>commands\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">)\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L7\" data-line=\"7\">cymcp\u003cspan class=\"token double-colon punctuation\">::\u003c/span>McpServerOptions options\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L8\" data-line=\"8\">options\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">.\u003c/span>resources \u003cspan class=\"token operator\">=\u003c/span> gateway\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">.\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token function\">resources\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">(\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">)\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L9\" data-line=\"9\">cymcp\u003cspan class=\"token double-colon punctuation\">::\u003c/span>McpServer \u003cspan class=\"token function\">server\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">(\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">*\u003c/span>gateway\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">.\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token function\">tools\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">(\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">)\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token string\">\"My application\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span> options\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">)\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L10\" data-line=\"10\">\u003cspan class=\"token comment\">// Garder gateway/commands vivants pendant le service. Pour une API : config.tools = gateway.tools().\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003c/code>\u003c/pre>\u003c/div>\u003cp>Les transports API et Codex choisissent ce mode à leur construction au-delà de 32 outils.\n\u003ccode>settings.tool_discovery_threshold\u003c/code> règle le seuil ; \u003ccode>settings.deferred_tools=false\u003c/code> conserve les\ndéfinitions complètes. Les options C++ exposent tool_discovery_threshold (maximum de size_t\npour désactiver). Une passerelle explicite fonctionne avec tout transport acceptant les outils.\nLes autres agents natifs gardent leur configuration MCP ; aucune injection CLI non supportée\nn&#39;est simulée.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"resources\">Lire uniquement les données nécessaires\u003ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#/fr/optimization/resources\" aria-label=\"Lien vers Lire uniquement les données nécessaires\">#\u003c/a>\u003c/h2>\u003cp>\u003ccode>ResourceRegistry\u003c/code> appartient à \u003ccode>CyMCP::Core\u003c/code> et fonctionne sans MCP ni HTTP. Une \u003ccode>Resource\u003c/code>\ndéclare URI, nom, MIME, taille en octets et callback de lecture bornée sur un \u003cstrong>instantané immuable\nfourni par l&#39;hôte\u003c/strong>. Aucun fichier ni réseau n&#39;est exposé implicitement. Les lectures appliquent leur\npolitique (\u003ccode>resources.read\u003c/code>, argument uri demandé), l&#39;annulation et l&#39;identité de l&#39;appelant.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>MCP annonce resources/list, resources/read et un catalogue de modèles vide seulement si\nMcpServerOptions.resources est fourni. Lister ne lit aucun contenu. Les petites ressources sont\nrenvoyées directement ; les grandes donnent un manifeste JSON (type cymcp.resource.v1), avec\nfirstUri, MIME d&#39;origine, taille et taille des morceaux. Lire firstUri puis suivre\n\u003ccode>_meta[&quot;com.cymcp/chunk&quot;].nextUri\u003c/code> jusqu&#39;à eof. Le texte préserve l&#39;UTF-8 ; le binaire utilise base64.\nUn extrait ne représente jamais le résultat complet.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>Les résultats de passerelle au-delà de 16 Kio deviennent des références privées ; MCP ajoute un\nresource_link standard. Les lire avec resources/read ou cy_resources_read. Valeurs par défaut :\nmorceaux de 32 Kio, 64 Mio conservés, 128 résultats et cinq minutes de rétention, tous réglables.\nLes résultats privés ne sont pas listés et sont liés à CallContext.principal. L&#39;hôte doit distinguer\nles identités à isoler. Remplacer un instantané invalide ses anciens URI de morceaux. Expiration\nou éviction LRU renvoie ResourceNotFound sans réexécuter la commande.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>Un résultat dépassant le budget de rétention reste en ligne, sans troncature ni nouvel appel.\nPour les jeux de données arbitrairement grands, fournir dès le départ une ressource sur instantané\nou une commande paginée. La passerelle ne supprime pas la mémoire déjà allouée par un handler\nqui renvoie un gros objet JSON. Les outils classiques gardent leur sortie structurée : leur\noutputSchema n&#39;est pas remplacé par une référence incompatible.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"cache\">Cache et compatibilité\u003ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#/fr/optimization/cache\" aria-label=\"Lien vers Cache et compatibilité\">#\u003c/a>\u003c/h2>\u003cp>tools/list et resources/list ont des curseurs liés à leur révision (64 entrées par page par défaut).\nMcpClient::list_tools() agrège toujours toutes les pages ; list_tools_page() en lit une seule.\nL&#39;absence de nextCursor termine la liste ; un curseur vide reçu d&#39;un autre serveur reste accepté.\nget_tool(name) utilise cymcp/tools/get si annoncé, sinon le catalogue complet d&#39;un ancien serveur.\nL&#39;extension est facultative ; les cinq outils compacts utilisent des appels MCP ordinaires.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>Le cache est privé à chaque client, indexé par méthode et ensemble des paramètres. Seules les\ndécouvertes, descriptions et lectures avec ttlMs positif sont conservées. Par défaut : 256 entrées,\n16 Mio sérialisés et TTL maximal de 30 secondes. TTL nul ou limites locales nulles désactivent\nle cache. tools/call et les erreurs ne sont jamais mis en cache. Aucun sondage périodique.\nUne modification peut rester invisible jusqu&#39;au TTL : clear_cache() force un rafraîchissement\naprès un changement connu. Reconnexion, fermeture et notifications de changement reçues\ninvalident le cache. Une erreur d&#39;outil le vide sans réessayer l&#39;opération. cache_stats() indique\nles accès, défauts de cache et octets conservés.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"grep\">Recherche texte rapide\u003ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#/fr/optimization/grep\" aria-label=\"Lien vers Recherche texte rapide\">#\u003c/a>\u003c/h2>\u003cp>cy_resources_grep parcourt les instantanés texte par morceaux : recherche littérale, ignore_case\nASCII facultatif, numéros de ligne, positions en octets et liens readUri. Une page contient au plus\n50 lignes correspondantes. Continuer avec les mêmes text/ignore_case et nextCursor. Le binaire\net les ressources refusées par la politique sont exclus. Aucun parcours du système de fichiers.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>Pour les fichiers, CyMCP::Platform propose un adaptateur \u003cstrong>ripgrep\u003c/strong> optionnel :\u003c/p>\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block\">\u003cdiv class=\"code-toolbar\">\u003cspan>cpp\u003c/span>\u003cbutton type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copier\u003c/button>\u003c/div>\u003cpre>\u003ccode class=\"language-cpp\">\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-2-L1\" data-line=\"1\">\u003cspan class=\"token macro property\">\u003cspan class=\"token directive-hash\">#\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token directive keyword\">include\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token string\">&lt;cymcp/search.hpp>\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-2-L2\" data-line=\"2\"> \u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-2-L3\" data-line=\"3\">cymcp\u003cspan class=\"token double-colon punctuation\">::\u003c/span>FileSearchOptions search_options\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-2-L4\" data-line=\"4\">search_options\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">.\u003c/span>root \u003cspan class=\"token operator\">=\u003c/span> host_selected_folder\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token comment\">// Choix explicite de l'hôte/utilisateur.\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-2-L5\" data-line=\"5\">\u003cspan class=\"token comment\">// search_options.ripgrep = trusted_rg_executable; // Sinon rg est résolu dans PATH.\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-2-L6\" data-line=\"6\">cymcp\u003cspan class=\"token double-colon punctuation\">::\u003c/span>FileSearch \u003cspan class=\"token function\">search\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">(\u003c/span>search_options\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">)\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-2-L7\" data-line=\"7\">search\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">.\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token function\">add_to\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">(\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">*\u003c/span>commands\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">)\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token comment\">// workspace.grep et workspace.read, découvrables via la passerelle.\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003c/code>\u003c/pre>\u003c/div>\u003cp>L&#39;hôte fournit séparément un exécutable ripgrep de confiance ; le SDK ne l&#39;embarque ni ne le\ntélécharge. Les regex utilisent le moteur Rust par défaut. Arguments directs, sans shell ni config rg.\nworkspace.grep accepte pattern, regex (true par défaut), ignore_case, glob et include_ignored\n(false par défaut). Les fichiers cachés sont inclus ; métadonnées Git et liens symboliques exclus.\nLes exclusions restent actives sauf include_ignored ou sélection explicite par un glob de fichier. Ce périmètre\nn&#39;est pas une sandbox système contre un autre processus modifiant simultanément les fichiers ;\nl&#39;hôte doit isoler les arborescences non fiables.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>Les pages contiennent par défaut au plus 100 lignes, path/line/byteOffset et des extraits UTF-8\nbornés. truncated et lineBytes signalent les longues lignes ; workspace.read permet de lire tout\nle texte par plages. Continuer avec \u003cstrong>cursor seul\u003c/strong> ; chaque curseur remplace le précédent.\nLes processus sont possédés, annulables, limités à huit recherches simultanées et expirent après\n60 secondes d&#39;inactivité. skippedNonUtf8 compte les correspondances non UTF-8 ignorées par\ncet adaptateur texte. Les limites de processus/ligne déclenchent une erreur explicite.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>workspace.read accepte un chemin relatif, offset, length (1–65536 octets) et revision facultative.\nSuivre nextOffset avec la même revision détecte un changement de fichier. Les frontières UTF-8\nsont préservées ; les contenus binaires/non UTF-8 sont refusés. Aucune écriture ni dossier hors\npérimètre n&#39;est exposé. La politique du registre décide toujours des appels autorisés.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"example\">Essayer dans Chat Lab\u003ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#/fr/optimization/example\" aria-label=\"Lien vers Essayer dans Chat Lab\">#\u003c/a>\u003c/h2>\u003cp>Les deux commandes du compteur restent inchangées par défaut. Dans une configuration JSON\nprivée passée à --config, activer le mode compact et choisir éventuellement un dossier en lecture seule :\u003c/p>\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block\">\u003cdiv class=\"code-toolbar\">\u003cspan>json\u003c/span>\u003cbutton type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copier\u003c/button>\u003c/div>\u003cpre>\u003ccode class=\"language-json\">\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-3-L1\" data-line=\"1\">\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">{\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-3-L2\" data-line=\"2\">  \u003cspan class=\"token property\">\"app_commands\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">:\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">{\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-3-L3\" data-line=\"3\">    \u003cspan class=\"token property\">\"deferred_tools\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">:\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token boolean\">true\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-3-L4\" data-line=\"4\">    \u003cspan class=\"token property\">\"workspace\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">:\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">{\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token property\">\"root\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">:\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token string\">\"./sample-workspace\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">}\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-3-L5\" data-line=\"5\">  \u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">}\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-3-L6\" data-line=\"6\">\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">}\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003c/code>\u003c/pre>\u003c/div>\u003cp>Choisir un dossier existant. workspace.ripgrep peut indiquer l&#39;exécutable de confiance. Aucun\ndossier n&#39;est configuré automatiquement. Le mode compact s&#39;applique à MCP et aux outils IA\ndirects supportés ; le SDK JSON garde les noms d&#39;origine. Registre et droits sont partagés.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"references\">Références du protocole\u003ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#/fr/optimization/references\" aria-label=\"Lien vers Références du protocole\">#\u003c/a>\u003c/h2>\u003cp>L&#39;implémentation suit les sections MCP \u003ca href=\"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/server/tools\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">outils\u003c/a>,\n\u003ca href=\"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/server/resources\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">ressources\u003c/a>,\n\u003ca href=\"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/server/utilities/caching\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">cache\u003c/a> et\n\u003ca href=\"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/server/utilities/pagination\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">pagination\u003c/a>.\nLes manifestes et la description ciblée sont des conventions CyMCPSDK facultatives, pas des\nméthodes MCP imposées.\u003c/p>\n","text":"Découvrir sans perdre de fonctions # Le stockage disque, les mesures, les abonnements et les fenêtres de contexte API complètent ces fonctions par des options indépendantes, désactivées par défaut. Registry reste la référence. Les appels SDK directs et les outils MCP classiques gardent leurs noms, arguments, schémas de sortie et droits. describe() renvoie toujours le catalogue complet. Les instantanés immuables catalogue() et summaries() (sans schémas) sont réutilisés jusqu'à un add , replace ou remove ; describe(name) charge une définition complète précise. ToolGateway expose cinq outils standard à la place de toutes les définitions : Outil Fonction cy_tools_search Rechercher noms/descriptions ; sans query, parcourir toutes les commandes. Suivre nextCursor avec la même query. cy_tools_describe Obtenir un schéma d'entrée/sortie complet. cy_tools_call Appeler la commande d'origine avec ses arguments et le contexte de l'appelant. cy_resources_read Lire une ressource, un manifeste ou un morceau. cy_resources_grep Rechercher dans les ressources texte sans charger tout leur contenu. Recherche et description n'exécutent aucune commande. L'appel valide les schémas d'origine et applique leur politique, y compris l'autorisation totale explicite. Aucune commande n'est définitivement masquée. Un changement de registre invalide les curseurs de recherche. cpp Copier # include \u003ccymcp/mcp.hpp> # include \u003ccymcp/resources.hpp> auto commands = std :: make_shared \u003c cymcp :: Registry > ( host_policy ) ; // Enregistrer toutes les opérations de l'application dans commands. cymcp :: ToolGateway gateway ( commands ) ; cymcp :: McpServerOptions options ; options . resources = gateway . resources ( ) ; cymcp :: McpServer server ( * gateway . tools ( ) , \"My application\" , options ) ; // Garder gateway/commands vivants pendant le service. Pour une API : config.tools = gateway.tools(). Les transports API et Codex choisissent ce mode à leur construction au-delà de 32 outils. settings.tool_discovery_threshold règle le seuil ; settings.deferred_tools=false conserve les définitions complètes. Les options C++ exposent tool_discovery_threshold (maximum de size_t pour désactiver). Une passerelle explicite fonctionne avec tout transport acceptant les outils. Les autres agents natifs gardent leur configuration MCP ; aucune injection CLI non supportée n'est simulée. Lire uniquement les données nécessaires # ResourceRegistry appartient à CyMCP::Core et fonctionne sans MCP ni HTTP. Une Resource déclare URI, nom, MIME, taille en octets et callback de lecture bornée sur un instantané immuable fourni par l'hôte . Aucun fichier ni réseau n'est exposé implicitement. Les lectures appliquent leur politique ( resources.read , argument uri demandé), l'annulation et l'identité de l'appelant. MCP annonce resources/list, resources/read et un catalogue de modèles vide seulement si McpServerOptions.resources est fourni. Lister ne lit aucun contenu. Les petites ressources sont renvoyées directement ; les grandes donnent un manifeste JSON (type cymcp.resource.v1), avec firstUri, MIME d'origine, taille et taille des morceaux. Lire firstUri puis suivre _meta[\"com.cymcp/chunk\"].nextUri jusqu'à eof. Le texte préserve l'UTF-8 ; le binaire utilise base64. Un extrait ne représente jamais le résultat complet. Les résultats de passerelle au-delà de 16 Kio deviennent des références privées ; MCP ajoute un resource_link standard. Les lire avec resources/read ou cy_resources_read. Valeurs par défaut : morceaux de 32 Kio, 64 Mio conservés, 128 résultats et cinq minutes de rétention, tous réglables. Les résultats privés ne sont pas listés et sont liés à CallContext.principal. L'hôte doit distinguer les identités à isoler. Remplacer un instantané invalide ses anciens URI de morceaux. Expiration ou éviction LRU renvoie ResourceNotFound sans réexécuter la commande. Un résultat dépassant le budget de rétention reste en ligne, sans troncature ni nouvel appel. Pour les jeux de données arbitrairement grands, fournir dès le départ une ressource sur instantané ou une commande paginée. La passerelle ne supprime pas la mémoire déjà allouée par un handler qui renvoie un gros objet JSON. Les outils classiques gardent leur sortie structurée : leur outputSchema n'est pas remplacé par une référence incompatible. Cache et compatibilité # tools/list et resources/list ont des curseurs liés à leur révision (64 entrées par page par défaut). McpClient::list_tools() agrège toujours toutes les pages ; list_tools_page() en lit une seule. L'absence de nextCursor termine la liste ; un curseur vide reçu d'un autre serveur reste accepté. get_tool(name) utilise cymcp/tools/get si annoncé, sinon le catalogue complet d'un ancien serveur. L'extension est facultative ; les cinq outils compacts utilisent des appels MCP ordinaires. Le cache est privé à chaque client, indexé par méthode et ensemble des paramètres. Seules les découvertes, descriptions et lectures avec ttlMs positif sont conservées. Par défaut : 256 entrées, 16 Mio sérialisés et TTL maximal de 30 secondes. TTL nul ou limites locales nulles désactivent le cache. tools/call et les erreurs ne sont jamais mis en cache. Aucun sondage périodique. Une modification peut rester invisible jusqu'au TTL : clear_cache() force un rafraîchissement après un changement connu. Reconnexion, fermeture et notifications de changement reçues invalident le cache. Une erreur d'outil le vide sans réessayer l'opération. cache_stats() indique les accès, défauts de cache et octets conservés. Recherche texte rapide # cy_resources_grep parcourt les instantanés texte par morceaux : recherche littérale, ignore_case ASCII facultatif, numéros de ligne, positions en octets et liens readUri. Une page contient au plus 50 lignes correspondantes. Continuer avec les mêmes text/ignore_case et nextCursor. Le binaire et les ressources refusées par la politique sont exclus. Aucun parcours du système de fichiers. Pour les fichiers, CyMCP::Platform propose un adaptateur ripgrep optionnel : cpp Copier # include \u003ccymcp/search.hpp> cymcp :: FileSearchOptions search_options ; search_options . root = host_selected_folder ; // Choix explicite de l'hôte/utilisateur. // search_options.ripgrep = trusted_rg_executable; // Sinon rg est résolu dans PATH. cymcp :: FileSearch search ( search_options ) ; search . add_to ( * commands ) ; // workspace.grep et workspace.read, découvrables via la passerelle. L'hôte fournit séparément un exécutable ripgrep de confiance ; le SDK ne l'embarque ni ne le télécharge. Les regex utilisent le moteur Rust par défaut. Arguments directs, sans shell ni config rg. workspace.grep accepte pattern, regex (true par défaut), ignore_case, glob et include_ignored (false par défaut). Les fichiers cachés sont inclus ; métadonnées Git et liens symboliques exclus. Les exclusions restent actives sauf include_ignored ou sélection explicite par un glob de fichier. Ce périmètre n'est pas une sandbox système contre un autre processus modifiant simultanément les fichiers ; l'hôte doit isoler les arborescences non fiables. Les pages contiennent par défaut au plus 100 lignes, path/line/byteOffset et des extraits UTF-8 bornés. truncated et lineBytes signalent les longues lignes ; workspace.read permet de lire tout le texte par plages. Continuer avec cursor seul ; chaque curseur remplace le précédent. Les processus sont possédés, annulables, limités à huit recherches simultanées et expirent après 60 secondes d'inactivité. skippedNonUtf8 compte les correspondances non UTF-8 ignorées par cet adaptateur texte. Les limites de processus/ligne déclenchent une erreur explicite. workspace.read accepte un chemin relatif, offset, length (1–65536 octets) et revision facultative. Suivre nextOffset avec la même revision détecte un changement de fichier. Les frontières UTF-8 sont préservées ; les contenus binaires/non UTF-8 sont refusés. Aucune écriture ni dossier hors périmètre n'est exposé. La politique du registre décide toujours des appels autorisés. Essayer dans Chat Lab # Les deux commandes du compteur restent inchangées par défaut. Dans une configuration JSON privée passée à --config, activer le mode compact et choisir éventuellement un dossier en lecture seule : json Copier { \"app_commands\" : { \"deferred_tools\" : true , \"workspace\" : { \"root\" : \"./sample-workspace\" } } } Choisir un dossier existant. workspace.ripgrep peut indiquer l'exécutable de confiance. Aucun dossier n'est configuré automatiquement. Le mode compact s'applique à MCP et aux outils IA directs supportés ; le SDK JSON garde les noms d'origine. Registre et droits sont partagés. Références du protocole # L'implémentation suit les sections MCP outils , ressources , cache et pagination . Les manifestes et la description ciblée sont des conventions CyMCPSDK facultatives, pas des méthodes MCP imposées. #include \u003ccymcp/mcp.hpp> #include \u003ccymcp/resources.hpp> auto commands = std::make_shared\u003ccymcp::Registry>(host_policy); // Enregistrer toutes les opérations de l'application dans commands. cymcp::ToolGateway gateway(commands); cymcp::McpServerOptions options; options.resources = gateway.resources(); cymcp::McpServer server(*gateway.tools(), \"My application\", options); // Garder gateway/commands vivants pendant le service. Pour une API : config.tools = gateway.tools(). #include \u003ccymcp/search.hpp> cymcp::FileSearchOptions search_options; search_options.root = host_selected_folder; // Choix explicite de l'hôte/utilisateur. // search_options.ripgrep = trusted_rg_executable; // Sinon rg est résolu dans PATH. cymcp::FileSearch search(search_options); search.add_to(*commands); // workspace.grep et workspace.read, découvrables via la passerelle. { \"app_commands\": { \"deferred_tools\": true, \"workspace\": {\"root\": \"./sample-workspace\"} } }","headings":[{"id":"tools","text":"Découvrir sans perdre de fonctions","level":2},{"id":"resources","text":"Lire uniquement les données nécessaires","level":2},{"id":"cache","text":"Cache et compatibilité","level":2},{"id":"grep","text":"Recherche texte rapide","level":2},{"id":"example","text":"Essayer dans Chat Lab","level":2},{"id":"references","text":"Références du protocole","level":2}],"anchors":["L1","L2","L3","L4","L5","L6","L7","L8","L9","L10","code-2-L1","code-2-L2","code-2-L3","code-2-L4","code-2-L5","code-2-L6","code-2-L7","code-3-L1","code-3-L2","code-3-L3","code-3-L4","code-3-L5","code-3-L6"],"languages":["cpp","json"],"code":"#include \u003ccymcp/mcp.hpp>\n#include \u003ccymcp/resources.hpp>\n\nauto commands = std::make_shared\u003ccymcp::Registry>(host_policy);\n// Enregistrer toutes les opérations de l'application dans commands.\ncymcp::ToolGateway gateway(commands);\ncymcp::McpServerOptions options;\noptions.resources = gateway.resources();\ncymcp::McpServer server(*gateway.tools(), \"My application\", options);\n// Garder gateway/commands vivants pendant le service. Pour une API : config.tools = gateway.tools().\n#include \u003ccymcp/search.hpp>\n\ncymcp::FileSearchOptions search_options;\nsearch_options.root = host_selected_folder; // Choix explicite de l'hôte/utilisateur.\n// search_options.ripgrep = trusted_rg_executable; // Sinon rg est résolu dans PATH.\ncymcp::FileSearch search(search_options);\nsearch.add_to(*commands); // workspace.grep et workspace.read, découvrables via la passerelle.\n{\n  \"app_commands\": {\n    \"deferred_tools\": true,\n    \"workspace\": {\"root\": \"./sample-workspace\"}\n  }\n}","assets":[],"links":["#/fr/runtime-options","https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/server/tools","https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/server/resources","https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/server/utilities/caching","https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/server/utilities/pagination"],"kind":"guide","revision":"f8630257d13f"},{"id":"overview","title":"CyMCPSDK","description":"Ajouter conversations IA et outils applicatifs à une application C++ native.","section":"Guides","order":0,"sourceRevision":"3","locale":"fr","html":"\u003ch2 id=\"workflows\">Choisir un parcours\u003ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#/fr/overview/workflows\" aria-label=\"Lien vers Choisir un parcours\">#\u003c/a>\u003c/h2>\u003cp>CyMCPSDK est une bibliothèque C++20 sous MIT pour les développeurs d&#39;applications.\nEnregistrer les opérations une fois, les exposer par SDK direct ou MCP, puis connecter\nl&#39;application à des agents CLI, des API ou un service de modèle local. Le panneau CyUI\noptionnel affiche les conversations.\u003c/p>\n\u003ctable>\n\u003cthead>\n\u003ctr>\n\u003cth>Votre besoin\u003c/th>\n\u003cth>Point de départ\u003c/th>\n\u003c/tr>\n\u003c/thead>\n\u003ctbody>\u003ctr>\n\u003ctd>Essayer l&#39;application Windows\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>\u003ca href=\"#/fr/quickstart\">Démarrage\u003c/a>\u003c/td>\n\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\n\u003ctd>Configurer un tchat et ses outils\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>\u003ca href=\"#/fr/chat-lab\">Chat Lab\u003c/a>\u003c/td>\n\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\n\u003ctd>Ajouter la bibliothèque à votre application\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>\u003ca href=\"#/fr/integration\">Intégration C++\u003c/a>\u003c/td>\n\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\n\u003ctd>Permettre à une IA ou une autre app d&#39;appeler vos opérations\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>\u003ca href=\"#/fr/operations\">Opérations applicatives\u003c/a>\u003c/td>\n\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\n\u003ctd>Charger les outils à la demande et rechercher du texte\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>\u003ca href=\"#/fr/optimization\">Optimisation et grep\u003c/a>\u003c/td>\n\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\n\u003ctd>Choisir les règles d&#39;accès\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>\u003ca href=\"#/fr/permissions\">Droits\u003c/a>\u003c/td>\n\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\n\u003ctd>Utiliser un moteur local installé\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>\u003ca href=\"#/fr/local-engines\">Moteurs locaux\u003c/a>\u003c/td>\n\u003c/tr>\n\u003c/tbody>\u003c/table>\n\u003ch2 id=\"modules\">Modules\u003ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#/fr/overview/modules\" aria-label=\"Lien vers Modules\">#\u003c/a>\u003c/h2>\u003ctable>\n\u003cthead>\n\u003ctr>\n\u003cth>Cible CMake\u003c/th>\n\u003cth>Rôle\u003c/th>\n\u003c/tr>\n\u003c/thead>\n\u003ctbody>\u003ctr>\n\u003ctd>\u003ccode>CyMCP::Core\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>Registre d&#39;opérations, schémas, politiques, annulation et workers bornés\u003c/td>\n\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\n\u003ctd>\u003ccode>CyMCP::Platform\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>Processus enfants natifs et arguments structurés\u003c/td>\n\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\n\u003ctd>\u003ccode>CyMCP::Http\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>Client HTTP(S), streaming et serveur loopback authentifié\u003c/td>\n\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\n\u003ctd>\u003ccode>CyMCP::MCP\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>Serveur/client d&#39;outils MCP par stdio ou HTTP JSON local\u003c/td>\n\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\n\u003ctd>\u003ccode>CyMCP::AI\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>Profils fournisseurs, sessions, conversations et échanges d&#39;outils\u003c/td>\n\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\n\u003ctd>\u003ccode>CyMCP::Local\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>Supervision des moteurs et téléchargements vérifiés\u003c/td>\n\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\n\u003ctd>\u003ccode>CyMCP::ChatUI\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>Contrôleur CyUI et panneau de tchat Markdown optionnels\u003c/td>\n\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\n\u003ctd>\u003ccode>CyMCP::SDK\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>Modules du SDK sans dépendance graphique\u003c/td>\n\u003c/tr>\n\u003c/tbody>\u003c/table>\n\u003ch2 id=\"scope\">Périmètre\u003ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#/fr/overview/scope\" aria-label=\"Lien vers Périmètre\">#\u003c/a>\u003c/h2>\u003cp>La bibliothèque n&#39;embarque ni modèle, CLI IA, moteur d&#39;inférence, runtime CUDA ou pilote.\nInstaller et configurer le fournisseur choisi. Ses comptes natifs et conditions restent\napplicables. Consulter les \u003ca href=\"#/fr/providers\">fournisseurs\u003c/a> et les \u003ca href=\"#/fr/licenses\">licences\u003c/a>.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>L&#39;exemple Windows utilise Win32/DX11. ChatUI utilise le backend CyUI/ImGui de l&#39;application\nhôte. La distribution Linux/macOS reste en cours de réalisation ; Android est reporté.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"navigation\">Lire ce manuel\u003ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#/fr/overview/navigation\" aria-label=\"Lien vers Lire ce manuel\">#\u003c/a>\u003c/h2>\u003cp>Utiliser l&#39;arbre des pages ou le champ de recherche ; \u003cstrong>Ctrl+K\u003c/strong> ouvre la recherche.\nBasculer entre anglais et français dans le lecteur. Le dossier \u003ccode>Documentation\u003c/code> complet\ns&#39;ouvre directement depuis le disque. Dans Chat Lab, \u003cstrong>F1\u003c/strong> ouvre l’aide. \u003cstrong>Ouvrir le manuel complet\u003c/strong>\naffiche le guide local dans la langue sélectionnée.\u003c/p>\n","text":"Choisir un parcours # CyMCPSDK est une bibliothèque C++20 sous MIT pour les développeurs d'applications. Enregistrer les opérations une fois, les exposer par SDK direct ou MCP, puis connecter l'application à des agents CLI, des API ou un service de modèle local. Le panneau CyUI optionnel affiche les conversations. Votre besoin Point de départ Essayer l'application Windows Démarrage Configurer un tchat et ses outils Chat Lab Ajouter la bibliothèque à votre application Intégration C++ Permettre à une IA ou une autre app d'appeler vos opérations Opérations applicatives Charger les outils à la demande et rechercher du texte Optimisation et grep Choisir les règles d'accès Droits Utiliser un moteur local installé Moteurs locaux Modules # Cible CMake Rôle CyMCP::Core Registre d'opérations, schémas, politiques, annulation et workers bornés CyMCP::Platform Processus enfants natifs et arguments structurés CyMCP::Http Client HTTP(S), streaming et serveur loopback authentifié CyMCP::MCP Serveur/client d'outils MCP par stdio ou HTTP JSON local CyMCP::AI Profils fournisseurs, sessions, conversations et échanges d'outils CyMCP::Local Supervision des moteurs et téléchargements vérifiés CyMCP::ChatUI Contrôleur CyUI et panneau de tchat Markdown optionnels CyMCP::SDK Modules du SDK sans dépendance graphique Périmètre # La bibliothèque n'embarque ni modèle, CLI IA, moteur d'inférence, runtime CUDA ou pilote. Installer et configurer le fournisseur choisi. Ses comptes natifs et conditions restent applicables. Consulter les fournisseurs et les licences . L'exemple Windows utilise Win32/DX11. ChatUI utilise le backend CyUI/ImGui de l'application hôte. La distribution Linux/macOS reste en cours de réalisation ; Android est reporté. Lire ce manuel # Utiliser l'arbre des pages ou le champ de recherche ; Ctrl+K ouvre la recherche. Basculer entre anglais et français dans le lecteur. Le dossier Documentation complet s'ouvre directement depuis le disque. Dans Chat Lab, F1 ouvre l’aide. Ouvrir le manuel complet affiche le guide local dans la langue sélectionnée.","headings":[{"id":"workflows","text":"Choisir un parcours","level":2},{"id":"modules","text":"Modules","level":2},{"id":"scope","text":"Périmètre","level":2},{"id":"navigation","text":"Lire ce manuel","level":2}],"anchors":[],"languages":[],"code":"","assets":[],"links":["#/fr/quickstart","#/fr/chat-lab","#/fr/integration","#/fr/operations","#/fr/optimization","#/fr/permissions","#/fr/local-engines","#/fr/providers","#/fr/licenses"],"kind":"guide","revision":"1dd4b2b10684"},{"id":"permissions","title":"Configurer les droits","description":"Choisir séparément la politique des opérations hôtes et les autorisations de l'agent natif.","section":"SDK","parent":"integration","order":2,"sourceRevision":"1","locale":"fr","html":"\u003ch2 id=\"policy\">Choisir la politique hôte\u003ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#/fr/permissions/policy\" aria-label=\"Lien vers Choisir la politique hôte\">#\u003c/a>\u003c/h2>\u003cp>Une \u003ccode>Policy\u003c/code> par défaut refuse les opérations. Utiliser un callback pour décider à partir du\ncontexte, du nom de l&#39;opération et des arguments, ou choisir explicitement \u003ccode>Policy::allow_all()\u003c/code>\nlorsque l&#39;hôte veut un accès libre à son domaine enregistré. Le SDK n&#39;impose pas de boîtes de confirmation.\u003c/p>\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block\">\u003cdiv class=\"code-toolbar\">\u003cspan>cpp\u003c/span>\u003cbutton type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copier\u003c/button>\u003c/div>\u003cpre>\u003ccode class=\"language-cpp\">\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L1\" data-line=\"1\">cymcp\u003cspan class=\"token double-colon punctuation\">::\u003c/span>Policy \u003cspan class=\"token function\">reads_only\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">(\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">[\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">]\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">(\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token keyword\">const\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token keyword\">auto\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">&amp;\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token keyword\">const\u003c/span> std\u003cspan class=\"token double-colon punctuation\">::\u003c/span>string\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">&amp;\u003c/span> name\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token keyword\">const\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token keyword\">auto\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">&amp;\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">)\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">{\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L2\" data-line=\"2\">    \u003cspan class=\"token keyword\">return\u003c/span> name \u003cspan class=\"token operator\">==\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token string\">\"get_counter\"\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token operator\">?\u003c/span> cymcp\u003cspan class=\"token double-colon punctuation\">::\u003c/span>Decision\u003cspan class=\"token double-colon punctuation\">::\u003c/span>allow \u003cspan class=\"token operator\">:\u003c/span> cymcp\u003cspan class=\"token double-colon punctuation\">::\u003c/span>Decision\u003cspan class=\"token double-colon punctuation\">::\u003c/span>deny\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L3\" data-line=\"3\">\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">}\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">)\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003c/code>\u003c/pre>\u003c/div>\u003cp>Autoriser une opération ne crée pas de capacités supplémentaires. Limiter les handlers et leurs\nschémas au besoin de l&#39;application. La validation du domaine s&#39;applique même avec une politique\npermissive. L&#39;annulation et les budgets de ressources sont distincts des décisions de droits.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"agents\">Autorisations de l&#39;agent et opérations\u003ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#/fr/permissions/agents\" aria-label=\"Lien vers Autorisations de l&#39;agent et opérations\">#\u003c/a>\u003c/h2>\u003cp>Les droits natifs de l&#39;agent sont distincts du registre d&#39;opérations. Dans Chat Lab,\n\u003cstrong>Autoriser toutes les actions\u003c/strong> demande le mode permissif du fournisseur ; \u003cstrong>Autoriser la\nmodification du compteur\u003c/strong> contrôle le registre de démonstration. Une option activée ne retire\npas les restrictions imposées par un fournisseur externe ou le système d&#39;exploitation.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>Les services client ACP de fichiers et terminal ne sont pas annoncés par défaut. L&#39;hôte doit\ndéclarer \u003ccode>settings.client_capabilities\u003c/code>, fournir \u003ccode>request_handler\u003c/code> et choisir sa politique\nd&#39;autorisation. Il implémente le comportement et le nettoyage des fichiers/terminaux ; une simple\ncapacité déclarée ne crée aucun service de terminal.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"network\">Authentifier un serveur local\u003ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#/fr/permissions/network\" aria-label=\"Lien vers Authentifier un serveur local\">#\u003c/a>\u003c/h2>\u003cp>Le serveur HTTP loopback exige un jeton d&#39;au moins 32 caractères et refuse les requêtes portant\n\u003ccode>Origin\u003c/code>. Passer le jeton dans \u003ccode>Authorization: Bearer ...\u003c/code>. Chat Lab crée un nouveau jeton aléatoire\nau démarrage du serveur ; il affiche uniquement l&#39;adresse et propose une copie explicite du jeton.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>L&#39;authentification identifie un client autorisé ; elle ne remplace pas les droits des opérations.\nLa durée de vie du serveur, la distribution du jeton et la politique du domaine restent contrôlées par l&#39;hôte.\u003c/p>\n","text":"Choisir la politique hôte # Une Policy par défaut refuse les opérations. Utiliser un callback pour décider à partir du contexte, du nom de l'opération et des arguments, ou choisir explicitement Policy::allow_all() lorsque l'hôte veut un accès libre à son domaine enregistré. Le SDK n'impose pas de boîtes de confirmation. cpp Copier cymcp :: Policy reads_only ( [ ] ( const auto & , const std :: string & name , const auto & ) { return name == \"get_counter\" ? cymcp :: Decision :: allow : cymcp :: Decision :: deny ; } ) ; Autoriser une opération ne crée pas de capacités supplémentaires. Limiter les handlers et leurs schémas au besoin de l'application. La validation du domaine s'applique même avec une politique permissive. L'annulation et les budgets de ressources sont distincts des décisions de droits. Autorisations de l'agent et opérations # Les droits natifs de l'agent sont distincts du registre d'opérations. Dans Chat Lab, Autoriser toutes les actions demande le mode permissif du fournisseur ; Autoriser la modification du compteur contrôle le registre de démonstration. Une option activée ne retire pas les restrictions imposées par un fournisseur externe ou le système d'exploitation. Les services client ACP de fichiers et terminal ne sont pas annoncés par défaut. L'hôte doit déclarer settings.client_capabilities , fournir request_handler et choisir sa politique d'autorisation. Il implémente le comportement et le nettoyage des fichiers/terminaux ; une simple capacité déclarée ne crée aucun service de terminal. Authentifier un serveur local # Le serveur HTTP loopback exige un jeton d'au moins 32 caractères et refuse les requêtes portant Origin . Passer le jeton dans Authorization: Bearer ... . Chat Lab crée un nouveau jeton aléatoire au démarrage du serveur ; il affiche uniquement l'adresse et propose une copie explicite du jeton. L'authentification identifie un client autorisé ; elle ne remplace pas les droits des opérations. La durée de vie du serveur, la distribution du jeton et la politique du domaine restent contrôlées par l'hôte. cymcp::Policy reads_only([](const auto&, const std::string& name, const auto&) { return name == \"get_counter\" ? cymcp::Decision::allow : cymcp::Decision::deny; });","headings":[{"id":"policy","text":"Choisir la politique hôte","level":2},{"id":"agents","text":"Autorisations de l'agent et opérations","level":2},{"id":"network","text":"Authentifier un serveur local","level":2}],"anchors":["L1","L2","L3"],"languages":["cpp"],"code":"cymcp::Policy reads_only([](const auto&, const std::string& name, const auto&) {\n    return name == \"get_counter\" ? cymcp::Decision::allow : cymcp::Decision::deny;\n});","assets":[],"links":[],"kind":"guide","revision":"13569a6b2d2d"},{"id":"providers","title":"Choisir un fournisseur","description":"Sélectionner CLI, API native ou service local avec ses vrais modèles et identifiants.","section":"Guides","parent":"chat-lab","order":1,"sourceRevision":"5","locale":"fr","html":"\u003ch2 id=\"profiles\">Profils intégrés\u003ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#/fr/providers/profiles\" aria-label=\"Lien vers Profils intégrés\">#\u003c/a>\u003c/h2>\u003ctable>\n\u003cthead>\n\u003ctr>\n\u003cth>Type\u003c/th>\n\u003cth>Identifiants du registre\u003c/th>\n\u003c/tr>\n\u003c/thead>\n\u003ctbody>\u003ctr>\n\u003ctd>Agents natifs\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>\u003ccode>codex\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>codex-exec\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>claude-code\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>antigravity\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>command-code\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>codebuddy\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\n\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\n\u003ctd>Agents ACP v1\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>\u003ccode>opencode\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>gemini\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>qwen-code\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>kimi\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>goose\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>devin\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>command-code-acp\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>codebuddy-acp\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>acp\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\n\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\n\u003ctd>OpenCode historique 1.x\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>\u003ccode>opencode-cli\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\n\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\n\u003ctd>API natives\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>\u003ccode>openai\u003c/code> (Responses), \u003ccode>anthropic\u003c/code> (Messages), \u003ccode>openrouter\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>ollama\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\n\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\n\u003ctd>Serveurs HTTP compatibles\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>\u003ccode>openai-compatible\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>llama.cpp\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>lmstudio\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\n\u003c/tr>\n\u003c/tbody>\u003c/table>\n\u003cp>Choisir \u003ccode>codex\u003c/code> pour une session App Server persistante et les outils de l’hôte. Le\nprofil \u003ccode>codex-exec\u003c/code> lit le texte sur stdin et peut reprendre un thread par son identifiant.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>Ces 23 profils décrivent des transports et des recettes de lancement. La version installée, le\nserveur et le modèle déterminent les capacités réelles. ACP v1 négocie le chargement des sessions,\nles modèles, modes et contenus acceptés. \u003ccode>opencode-cli\u003c/code> est l&#39;ancien transport JSONL ; OpenCode\nactuel utilise \u003ccode>opencode\u003c/code> avec ACP.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"configure\">Configurer une connexion\u003ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#/fr/providers/configure\" aria-label=\"Lien vers Configurer une connexion\">#\u003c/a>\u003c/h2>\u003cp>Utiliser d&#39;abord \u003cstrong>Connexion automatique\u003c/strong> : les CLI installés et les paquets npm pris en\ncharge sont résolus sans saisir de chemins ni d&#39;arguments. Les CLI réutilisent leur compte\net leur environnement. La détection couvre chaque profil CLI nommé ci-dessus ; le profil\ngénérique \u003ccode>acp\u003c/code> nécessite une recette fournie par l&#39;hôte. Une installation ne prouve pas\nque l&#39;authentification ou la génération réussira.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>Pour une installation particulière, modifier les champs dans l&#39;onglet \u003cstrong>Fournisseurs\u003c/strong>. L&#39;application hôte peut\najouter ses dossiers d&#39;exécutables, ses racines npm privées et ses recettes de détection.\nLes arguments sont des chaînes structurées ; le SDK ne les passe jamais à un shell.\n\u003ccode>process.environment\u003c/code> transmet des variables uniquement au processus enfant.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>La détection reconnaît \u003ccode>OPENAI_API_KEY\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>ANTHROPIC_API_KEY\u003c/code> et \u003ccode>OPENROUTER_API_KEY\u003c/code>.\nLes adresses peuvent venir de \u003ccode>OPENAI_BASE_URL\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL\u003c/code>,\n\u003ccode>OPENROUTER_BASE_URL\u003c/code> ou \u003ccode>OLLAMA_HOST\u003c/code>. Les services locaux démarrés sont interrogés\npour leurs modèles ; un service arrêté ou sans modèles est signalé explicitement.\nLa recherche n&#39;inspecte pas les fichiers privés pour y chercher des secrets.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>Les identifiants API viennent d&#39;une variable d&#39;environnement nommée ou du champ masqué en mémoire\nde Chat Lab. Le CLI et l&#39;interface peuvent charger cette configuration sans secret avec \u003ccode>--config\u003c/code> :\u003c/p>\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block\">\u003cdiv class=\"code-toolbar\">\u003cspan>json\u003c/span>\u003cbutton type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copier\u003c/button>\u003c/div>\u003cpre>\u003ccode class=\"language-json\">\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L1\" data-line=\"1\">\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">{\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L2\" data-line=\"2\">  \u003cspan class=\"token property\">\"provider\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">:\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token string\">\"openai\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L3\" data-line=\"3\">  \u003cspan class=\"token property\">\"model\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">:\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token string\">\"\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L4\" data-line=\"4\">  \u003cspan class=\"token property\">\"api_key_env\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">:\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token string\">\"OPENAI_API_KEY\"\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L5\" data-line=\"5\">\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">}\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003c/code>\u003c/pre>\u003c/div>\u003cp>En mode automatique, choisir un modèle retourné dans la liste ou conserver le réglage natif.\nSeuls les services locaux reçoivent un modèle automatiquement ; une API distante affiche son\ncatalogue et attend un choix explicite. En mode manuel, choisir un fournisseur préremplit ses\nparamètres conventionnels (adresse, variable de clé, délais) et l&#39;installation détectée.\nLe mode manuel accepte aussi un identifiant exact. Ne pas mettre de vraie\nclé dans un fichier JSON. \u003ccode>settings.base_url\u003c/code> remplace l&#39;adresse du service. Le profil Ollama\nattend la base de son API native ; les serveurs compatibles utilisent généralement une base \u003ccode>/v1\u003c/code>.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"models\">Découvrir modèles et capacités\u003ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#/fr/providers/models\" aria-label=\"Lien vers Découvrir modèles et capacités\">#\u003c/a>\u003c/h2>\u003cp>L&#39;exemple sans interface propose :\u003c/p>\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block\">\u003cdiv class=\"code-toolbar\">\u003cspan>sh\u003c/span>\u003cbutton type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copier\u003c/button>\u003c/div>\u003cpre>\u003ccode class=\"language-bash\">\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-2-L1\" data-line=\"1\">cymcp_chat providers\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-2-L2\" data-line=\"2\">cymcp_chat discover\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-2-L3\" data-line=\"3\">cymcp_chat models examples/chat-ollama.json\u003c/span>\u003c/code>\u003c/pre>\u003c/div>\u003cp>\u003ccode>providers\u003c/code> liste les capacités des transports configurés ; \u003ccode>models\u003c/code> contacte le fournisseur choisi.\nUn catalogue non pris en charge ne signifie pas que le tchat est indisponible : utiliser un ID exact\nfourni par l&#39;outil natif. Le modèle choisi s&#39;applique à une nouvelle connexion. Le SDK ne change pas\nsilencieusement de modèle et ne rejoue pas les générations échouées.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"extension\">Ajouter un fournisseur\u003ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#/fr/providers/extension\" aria-label=\"Lien vers Ajouter un fournisseur\">#\u003c/a>\u003c/h2>\u003cp>Implémenter l&#39;interface publique \u003ccode>Provider\u003c/code>, puis enregistrer un \u003ccode>ProviderDescriptor\u003c/code> et sa factory\navec \u003ccode>ProviderRegistry::add\u003c/code>. Les méthodes \u003ccode>connect\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>start_session\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>send\u003c/code> et \u003ccode>disconnect\u003c/code>\ndoivent respecter les capacités annoncées. \u003ccode>ProviderConfig\u003c/code> fournit arguments, réglages,\nidentifiants, registre d&#39;opérations optionnel et callbacks de droits.\nConsulter l&#39;\u003ca href=\"#/fr/integration/providers\">intégration\u003c/a>.\u003c/p>\n","text":"Profils intégrés # Type Identifiants du registre Agents natifs codex , codex-exec , claude-code , antigravity , command-code , codebuddy Agents ACP v1 opencode , gemini , qwen-code , kimi , goose , devin , command-code-acp , codebuddy-acp , acp OpenCode historique 1.x opencode-cli API natives openai (Responses), anthropic (Messages), openrouter , ollama Serveurs HTTP compatibles openai-compatible , llama.cpp , lmstudio Choisir codex pour une session App Server persistante et les outils de l’hôte. Le profil codex-exec lit le texte sur stdin et peut reprendre un thread par son identifiant. Ces 23 profils décrivent des transports et des recettes de lancement. La version installée, le serveur et le modèle déterminent les capacités réelles. ACP v1 négocie le chargement des sessions, les modèles, modes et contenus acceptés. opencode-cli est l'ancien transport JSONL ; OpenCode actuel utilise opencode avec ACP. Configurer une connexion # Utiliser d'abord Connexion automatique : les CLI installés et les paquets npm pris en charge sont résolus sans saisir de chemins ni d'arguments. Les CLI réutilisent leur compte et leur environnement. La détection couvre chaque profil CLI nommé ci-dessus ; le profil générique acp nécessite une recette fournie par l'hôte. Une installation ne prouve pas que l'authentification ou la génération réussira. Pour une installation particulière, modifier les champs dans l'onglet Fournisseurs . L'application hôte peut ajouter ses dossiers d'exécutables, ses racines npm privées et ses recettes de détection. Les arguments sont des chaînes structurées ; le SDK ne les passe jamais à un shell. process.environment transmet des variables uniquement au processus enfant. La détection reconnaît OPENAI_API_KEY , ANTHROPIC_API_KEY et OPENROUTER_API_KEY . Les adresses peuvent venir de OPENAI_BASE_URL , ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL , OPENROUTER_BASE_URL ou OLLAMA_HOST . Les services locaux démarrés sont interrogés pour leurs modèles ; un service arrêté ou sans modèles est signalé explicitement. La recherche n'inspecte pas les fichiers privés pour y chercher des secrets. Les identifiants API viennent d'une variable d'environnement nommée ou du champ masqué en mémoire de Chat Lab. Le CLI et l'interface peuvent charger cette configuration sans secret avec --config : json Copier { \"provider\" : \"openai\" , \"model\" : \"\" , \"api_key_env\" : \"OPENAI_API_KEY\" } En mode automatique, choisir un modèle retourné dans la liste ou conserver le réglage natif. Seuls les services locaux reçoivent un modèle automatiquement ; une API distante affiche son catalogue et attend un choix explicite. En mode manuel, choisir un fournisseur préremplit ses paramètres conventionnels (adresse, variable de clé, délais) et l'installation détectée. Le mode manuel accepte aussi un identifiant exact. Ne pas mettre de vraie clé dans un fichier JSON. settings.base_url remplace l'adresse du service. Le profil Ollama attend la base de son API native ; les serveurs compatibles utilisent généralement une base /v1 . Découvrir modèles et capacités # L'exemple sans interface propose : sh Copier cymcp_chat providers cymcp_chat discover cymcp_chat models examples/chat-ollama.json providers liste les capacités des transports configurés ; models contacte le fournisseur choisi. Un catalogue non pris en charge ne signifie pas que le tchat est indisponible : utiliser un ID exact fourni par l'outil natif. Le modèle choisi s'applique à une nouvelle connexion. Le SDK ne change pas silencieusement de modèle et ne rejoue pas les générations échouées. Ajouter un fournisseur # Implémenter l'interface publique Provider , puis enregistrer un ProviderDescriptor et sa factory avec ProviderRegistry::add . Les méthodes connect , start_session , send et disconnect doivent respecter les capacités annoncées. ProviderConfig fournit arguments, réglages, identifiants, registre d'opérations optionnel et callbacks de droits. Consulter l' intégration . { \"provider\": \"openai\", \"model\": \"\", \"api_key_env\": \"OPENAI_API_KEY\" } cymcp_chat providers cymcp_chat discover cymcp_chat models examples/chat-ollama.json","headings":[{"id":"profiles","text":"Profils intégrés","level":2},{"id":"configure","text":"Configurer une connexion","level":2},{"id":"models","text":"Découvrir modèles et capacités","level":2},{"id":"extension","text":"Ajouter un fournisseur","level":2}],"anchors":["L1","L2","L3","L4","L5","code-2-L1","code-2-L2","code-2-L3"],"languages":["json","bash"],"code":"{\n  \"provider\": \"openai\",\n  \"model\": \"\",\n  \"api_key_env\": \"OPENAI_API_KEY\"\n}\ncymcp_chat providers\ncymcp_chat discover\ncymcp_chat models examples/chat-ollama.json","assets":[],"links":["#/fr/integration/providers"],"kind":"guide","revision":"77d1f32ddb77"},{"id":"quickstart","title":"Démarrer Chat Lab","description":"Compiler et ouvrir l'exemple Windows, puis essayer la démonstration Markdown locale.","section":"Guides","parent":"overview","order":1,"sourceRevision":"4","locale":"fr","html":"\u003ch2 id=\"build\">Compiler l&#39;exemple\u003ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#/fr/quickstart/build\" aria-label=\"Lien vers Compiler l&#39;exemple\">#\u003c/a>\u003c/h2>\u003cp>Utiliser Windows 10/11 x64 avec la charge \u003cstrong>Développement Desktop en C++\u003c/strong> de Visual\nStudio 2022, le Windows SDK et les outils CMake. Placer une copie compatible de\n\u003ca href=\"https://github.com/MrMybal/CyUI\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">CyUI\u003c/a> à côté du SDK, ou passer son emplacement réel au script.\u003c/p>\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block\">\u003cdiv class=\"code-toolbar\">\u003cspan>powershell\u003c/span>\u003cbutton type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copier\u003c/button>\u003c/div>\u003cpre>\u003ccode class=\"language-powershell\">\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L1\" data-line=\"1\">./tools/build-chat.ps1 -CyUISource ../CyUI\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L2\" data-line=\"2\">./out/ChatLab-windows-x64/cymcp_chat_app.exe\u003c/span>\u003c/code>\u003c/pre>\u003c/div>\u003cp>Le script compile et prépare \u003ccode>out/ChatLab-windows-x64\u003c/code>. Conserver ensemble l&#39;exécutable,\n\u003ccode>Documentation\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>licenses\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>LICENSE\u003c/code> et \u003ccode>THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md\u003c/code>.\nLe runtime Microsoft Visual C++ 2015–2022 x64 est nécessaire. Le rendu utilise DX11,\navec repli WARP.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"demo\">Essayer sans compte\u003ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#/fr/quickstart/demo\" aria-label=\"Lien vers Essayer sans compte\">#\u003c/a>\u003c/h2>\u003col>\n\u003cli>Lancer l&#39;application. \u003cstrong>L&#39;anglais\u003c/strong> est la langue par défaut.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Ouvrir \u003cstrong>Providers\u003c/strong>, choisir \u003cstrong>Demo / Markdown (no AI)\u003c/strong> puis \u003cstrong>Connect / New chat\u003c/strong>.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Saisir un message et choisir \u003cstrong>Send\u003c/strong>, ou appuyer sur \u003cstrong>Ctrl+Entrée\u003c/strong>.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Lire le Markdown pendant son affichage progressif, sélectionner du texte ou copier un message.\u003c/li>\n\u003c/ol>\n\u003cfigure data-cydoc-module=\"image\" data-cydoc-id=\"chat-overview\" data-config=\"{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;chat-overview&quot;,&quot;src&quot;:&quot;assets/chat-lab-fr.png&quot;,&quot;alt&quot;:&quot;Chat Lab en français avec sa démonstration Markdown locale&quot;,&quot;controls&quot;:&quot;minimal&quot;}\">\u003cimg src=\"assets/chat-lab-fr.png\" alt=\"Chat Lab en français avec sa démonstration Markdown locale\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\">\u003c/figure>\u003cp>La démonstration produit un texte local fixe ; elle n&#39;appelle aucun modèle. Choisir un\n\u003ca href=\"#/fr/providers\">fournisseur\u003c/a> pour une vraie conversation. \u003cstrong>Maj+Entrée\u003c/strong> ajoute une ligne dans la saisie.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"language\">Langue et aide\u003ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#/fr/quickstart/language\" aria-label=\"Lien vers Langue et aide\">#\u003c/a>\u003c/h2>\u003cp>Dans \u003cstrong>Fournisseurs → Apparence\u003c/strong>, sélectionner \u003cstrong>Français\u003c/strong> ou \u003cstrong>English\u003c/strong>, puis un thème CyUI.\nReconnecter la démonstration après un changement de langue pour produire le nouveau texte\ndans cette langue. Les réponses IA suivent le modèle et la consigne ; changer la langue\nde l&#39;interface ne traduit pas les messages existants.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>\u003cstrong>Aide (F1)\u003c/strong> ouvre ce manuel sur \u003ca href=\"#/fr/chat-lab\">Chat Lab\u003c/a>. Le dossier local complet doit\naccompagner l&#39;exécutable. Le lecteur n&#39;a pas besoin de serveur HTTP.\u003c/p>\n","text":"Compiler l'exemple # Utiliser Windows 10/11 x64 avec la charge Développement Desktop en C++ de Visual Studio 2022, le Windows SDK et les outils CMake. Placer une copie compatible de CyUI à côté du SDK, ou passer son emplacement réel au script. powershell Copier ./tools/build-chat.ps1 -CyUISource ../CyUI ./out/ChatLab-windows-x64/cymcp_chat_app.exe Le script compile et prépare out/ChatLab-windows-x64 . Conserver ensemble l'exécutable, Documentation , licenses , LICENSE et THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md . Le runtime Microsoft Visual C++ 2015–2022 x64 est nécessaire. Le rendu utilise DX11, avec repli WARP. Essayer sans compte # Lancer l'application. L'anglais est la langue par défaut. Ouvrir Providers , choisir Demo / Markdown (no AI) puis Connect / New chat . Saisir un message et choisir Send , ou appuyer sur Ctrl+Entrée . Lire le Markdown pendant son affichage progressif, sélectionner du texte ou copier un message. La démonstration produit un texte local fixe ; elle n'appelle aucun modèle. Choisir un fournisseur pour une vraie conversation. Maj+Entrée ajoute une ligne dans la saisie. Langue et aide # Dans Fournisseurs → Apparence , sélectionner Français ou English , puis un thème CyUI. Reconnecter la démonstration après un changement de langue pour produire le nouveau texte dans cette langue. Les réponses IA suivent le modèle et la consigne ; changer la langue de l'interface ne traduit pas les messages existants. Aide (F1) ouvre ce manuel sur Chat Lab . Le dossier local complet doit accompagner l'exécutable. Le lecteur n'a pas besoin de serveur HTTP. ./tools/build-chat.ps1 -CyUISource ../CyUI ./out/ChatLab-windows-x64/cymcp_chat_app.exe","headings":[{"id":"build","text":"Compiler l'exemple","level":2},{"id":"demo","text":"Essayer sans compte","level":2},{"id":"language","text":"Langue et aide","level":2}],"anchors":["L1","L2"],"languages":["powershell"],"code":"./tools/build-chat.ps1 -CyUISource ../CyUI\n./out/ChatLab-windows-x64/cymcp_chat_app.exe","assets":["assets/chat-lab-fr.png"],"links":["https://github.com/MrMybal/CyUI","#/fr/providers","#/fr/chat-lab"],"kind":"media","revision":"9ba9276bc68e"},{"id":"runtime-options","title":"Optimisations d'exécution optionnelles","description":"Configurer les gros volumes sur disque, les mesures, les notifications et le contexte API.","section":"SDK","parent":"optimization","order":0,"sourceRevision":"1","locale":"fr","html":"\u003ch2 id=\"options\">Options indépendantes\u003ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#/fr/runtime-options/options\" aria-label=\"Lien vers Options indépendantes\">#\u003c/a>\u003c/h2>\u003cp>Les quatre fonctions sont facultatives. Core fournit ressources, stockage temporaire, journal de\nchangements et mesures sans dépendance graphique ni IA. ContextWindow appartient à AI. Aucune\ndépendance externe supplémentaire ni modèle de résumé n&#39;est installé. Sans configuration, les\napps gardent l&#39;historique API complet, les résultats conservés en RAM et les caches par TTL.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"disk\">Produire les gros volumes progressivement\u003ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#/fr/runtime-options/disk\" aria-label=\"Lien vers Produire les gros volumes progressivement\">#\u003c/a>\u003c/h2>\u003cdiv class=\"code-block\">\u003cdiv class=\"code-toolbar\">\u003cspan>cpp\u003c/span>\u003cbutton type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copier\u003c/button>\u003c/div>\u003cpre>\u003ccode class=\"language-cpp\">\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L1\" data-line=\"1\">\u003cspan class=\"token macro property\">\u003cspan class=\"token directive-hash\">#\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token directive keyword\">include\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token string\">&lt;cymcp/resources.hpp>\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L2\" data-line=\"2\"> \u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L3\" data-line=\"3\">cymcp\u003cspan class=\"token double-colon punctuation\">::\u003c/span>ResourceOptions storage\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L4\" data-line=\"4\">storage\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">.\u003c/span>disk_directory \u003cspan class=\"token operator\">=\u003c/span> host_selected_cache_folder\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L5\" data-line=\"5\">storage\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">.\u003c/span>max_stored_bytes \u003cspan class=\"token operator\">=\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token number\">8\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token operator\">*\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token number\">1024\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token operator\">*\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token number\">1024\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L6\" data-line=\"6\">storage\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">.\u003c/span>spool_threshold \u003cspan class=\"token operator\">=\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token number\">1024\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token operator\">*\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token number\">1024\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L7\" data-line=\"7\">storage\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">.\u003c/span>max_disk_bytes \u003cspan class=\"token operator\">=\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token number\">1024ULL\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token operator\">*\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token number\">1024\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token operator\">*\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token number\">1024\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L8\" data-line=\"8\">\u003cspan class=\"token keyword\">auto\u003c/span> resources \u003cspan class=\"token operator\">=\u003c/span> std\u003cspan class=\"token double-colon punctuation\">::\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token generic-function\">\u003cspan class=\"token function\">make_shared\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token generic class-name\">\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">&lt;\u003c/span>cymcp\u003cspan class=\"token double-colon punctuation\">::\u003c/span>ResourceRegistry\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">>\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">(\u003c/span>host_resource_policy\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span> storage\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">)\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L9\" data-line=\"9\">\u003cspan class=\"token keyword\">auto\u003c/span> handle \u003cspan class=\"token operator\">=\u003c/span> resources\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">->\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token function\">store_stream\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">(\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L10\" data-line=\"10\">    \u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">[\u003c/span>snapshot_blocks\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">]\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">(\u003c/span>std\u003cspan class=\"token double-colon punctuation\">::\u003c/span>ostream\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">&amp;\u003c/span> output\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token keyword\">const\u003c/span> cymcp\u003cspan class=\"token double-colon punctuation\">::\u003c/span>CallContext\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">&amp;\u003c/span> context\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">)\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">{\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L11\" data-line=\"11\">        \u003cspan class=\"token keyword\">for\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">(\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token keyword\">const\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token keyword\">auto\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">&amp;\u003c/span> block \u003cspan class=\"token operator\">:\u003c/span> snapshot_blocks\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">)\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">{\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L12\" data-line=\"12\">            context\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">.\u003c/span>cancellation\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">.\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token function\">check\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">(\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">)\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L13\" data-line=\"13\">            output\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">.\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token function\">write\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">(\u003c/span>block\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">.\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token function\">data\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">(\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">)\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span> block\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">.\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token function\">size\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">(\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">)\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">)\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L14\" data-line=\"14\">        \u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">}\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"L15\" data-line=\"15\">    \u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">}\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token string\">\"text/plain\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span> caller_context\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">)\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003c/code>\u003c/pre>\u003c/div>\u003cp>L&#39;hôte choisit le dossier parent. Le SDK crée un sous-dossier aléatoire réservé au propriétaire et\ndes fichiers privés ; les droits du parent restent inchangés. Au-delà du seuil, la production passe\nsur disque. Garder ce cache privé hors des dossiers exposés par d&#39;autres outils de fichiers.\nLe quota inclut fichiers conservés, producteurs actifs et lecteurs qui gardent un\ninstantané. Les anciens résultats peuvent être évincés ; un quota occupé par des opérations\nactives produit une erreur explicite. Quotas RAM/disque distincts, producteur appelé une seule fois,\npublication de la référence seulement après réussite complète.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>Lire la référence par les manifestes/morceaux existants. Pour le binaire, passer true en quatrième\nargument de store_stream : les contenus utilisent base64. Le texte respecte les frontières UTF-8.\nÉchec, annulation, expiration et destruction normale libèrent les fichiers possédés. Le nettoyage\ndisque vérifie les expirations environ chaque seconde ; une lecture active peut conserver son\nfichier immuable. Un arrêt brutal peut laisser un dossier privé orphelin à nettoyer par l&#39;hôte.\nAucun parcours/suppression des dossiers étrangers ni reprise implicite d&#39;un producteur interrompu.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>storage_stats() indique les octets RAM/disque conservés et le nombre de résultats, sans chemin.\nToolGateway sérialise ses gros résultats JSON directement dans le flux via store_json, sans créer\nune deuxième copie sérialisée complète. L&#39;objet JSON du handler reste alloué : pour de plus gros\nvolumes, produire directement une ressource progressive. Si tous les budgets sont dépassés, la\npasserelle garde son repli historique vers le résultat complet en ligne ; l&#39;API de flux directe renvoie\nResourceTooLarge sans tronquer. TTL/LRU sont temporaires et ne remplacent pas des archives.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"performance\">Mesurer sans enregistrer les contenus\u003ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#/fr/runtime-options/performance\" aria-label=\"Lien vers Mesurer sans enregistrer les contenus\">#\u003c/a>\u003c/h2>\u003cdiv class=\"code-block\">\u003cdiv class=\"code-toolbar\">\u003cspan>cpp\u003c/span>\u003cbutton type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copier\u003c/button>\u003c/div>\u003cpre>\u003ccode class=\"language-cpp\">\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-2-L1\" data-line=\"1\">\u003cspan class=\"token macro property\">\u003cspan class=\"token directive-hash\">#\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token directive keyword\">include\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token string\">&lt;cymcp/performance.hpp>\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-2-L2\" data-line=\"2\"> \u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-2-L3\" data-line=\"3\">cymcp\u003cspan class=\"token double-colon punctuation\">::\u003c/span>PerformanceOptions options\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-2-L4\" data-line=\"4\">options\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">.\u003c/span>jsonl_file \u003cspan class=\"token operator\">=\u003c/span> host_selected_private_log_file\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token comment\">// Facultatif : mémoire seule sinon.\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-2-L5\" data-line=\"5\">\u003cspan class=\"token keyword\">auto\u003c/span> performance \u003cspan class=\"token operator\">=\u003c/span> std\u003cspan class=\"token double-colon punctuation\">::\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token generic-function\">\u003cspan class=\"token function\">make_shared\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token generic class-name\">\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">&lt;\u003c/span>cymcp\u003cspan class=\"token double-colon punctuation\">::\u003c/span>PerformanceMonitor\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">>\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">(\u003c/span>options\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">)\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-2-L6\" data-line=\"6\">commands\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">->\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token function\">set_performance_monitor\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">(\u003c/span>performance\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">)\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-2-L7\" data-line=\"7\">\u003cspan class=\"token keyword\">auto\u003c/span> totals \u003cspan class=\"token operator\">=\u003c/span> performance\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">->\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token function\">snapshot\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">(\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">)\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-2-L8\" data-line=\"8\">\u003cspan class=\"token keyword\">auto\u003c/span> recent_records \u003cspan class=\"token operator\">=\u003c/span> performance\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">->\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token function\">drain\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">(\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">)\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003c/code>\u003c/pre>\u003c/div>\u003cp>Autres points d&#39;intégration : CallContext.performance, McpServerOptions.performance,\nMcpClientOptions.performance et ChatConnection.performance. Les lignes contiennent horodatage,\nstage/name, statut, elapsed_ms, input_bytes, output_bytes et cache_hit. Aucun argument, réponse,\nexplication d&#39;erreur, identité, secret ou ID de requête. Les étapes distinguent operation, mcp.server,\nmcp.client et conversation. La sortie d&#39;une conversation compte le texte UTF-8 final ; les autres\ntailles comptent le JSON sérialisé. Ce ne sont pas des nombres de tokens. Le calcul parcourt le\nJSON sans en allouer une copie sérialisée et ne s&#39;effectue que si le moniteur est activé.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>Les statistiques conservent appels/erreurs/cache, volumes, moyenne/maximum et p50_upper_ms,\np95_upper_ms : bornes de classes d&#39;histogramme, pas percentiles exacts. Catégories et lignes sont\nbornées ; les catégories excédentaires vont dans other. La file d&#39;écriture est bornée ;\ndropped_file_records et file_errors signalent les échecs. drain() ne supprime pas les agrégats.\nLe chemin fourni est ouvert comme nouveau fichier privé ; rotation/rétention relèvent de l&#39;hôte.\nLes mesures ne changent ni les droits, ni les appels, ni les règles de cache.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"notifications\">Recevoir les changements\u003ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#/fr/runtime-options/notifications\" aria-label=\"Lien vers Recevoir les changements\">#\u003c/a>\u003c/h2>\u003cdiv class=\"code-block\">\u003cdiv class=\"code-toolbar\">\u003cspan>cpp\u003c/span>\u003cbutton type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copier\u003c/button>\u003c/div>\u003cpre>\u003ccode class=\"language-cpp\">\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-3-L1\" data-line=\"1\">\u003cspan class=\"token macro property\">\u003cspan class=\"token directive-hash\">#\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token directive keyword\">include\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token string\">&lt;cymcp/changes.hpp>\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-3-L2\" data-line=\"2\">\u003cspan class=\"token macro property\">\u003cspan class=\"token directive-hash\">#\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token directive keyword\">include\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token string\">&lt;cymcp/mcp.hpp>\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-3-L3\" data-line=\"3\"> \u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-3-L4\" data-line=\"4\">\u003cspan class=\"token keyword\">auto\u003c/span> changes \u003cspan class=\"token operator\">=\u003c/span> std\u003cspan class=\"token double-colon punctuation\">::\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token generic-function\">\u003cspan class=\"token function\">make_shared\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token generic class-name\">\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">&lt;\u003c/span>cymcp\u003cspan class=\"token double-colon punctuation\">::\u003c/span>ChangeFeed\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">>\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">(\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">)\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-3-L5\" data-line=\"5\">commands\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">->\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token function\">set_change_feed\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">(\u003c/span>changes\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">)\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-3-L6\" data-line=\"6\">resources\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">->\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token function\">set_change_feed\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">(\u003c/span>changes\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">)\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-3-L7\" data-line=\"7\">cymcp\u003cspan class=\"token double-colon punctuation\">::\u003c/span>McpServerOptions options\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-3-L8\" data-line=\"8\">options\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">.\u003c/span>resources \u003cspan class=\"token operator\">=\u003c/span> resources\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-3-L9\" data-line=\"9\">options\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">.\u003c/span>changes \u003cspan class=\"token operator\">=\u003c/span> changes\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-3-L10\" data-line=\"10\">cymcp\u003cspan class=\"token double-colon punctuation\">::\u003c/span>McpServer \u003cspan class=\"token function\">server\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">(\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">*\u003c/span>commands\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token string\">\"My app\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span> options\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">)\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-3-L11\" data-line=\"11\">\u003cspan class=\"token comment\">// Côté client, après connect() :\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-3-L12\" data-line=\"12\">client\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">.\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token function\">start_notifications\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">(\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">{\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">{\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token string\">\"toolsListChanged\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token boolean\">true\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">}\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-3-L13\" data-line=\"13\">    \u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">{\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token string\">\"resourcesListChanged\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token boolean\">true\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">}\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-3-L14\" data-line=\"14\">    \u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">{\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token string\">\"resourceSubscriptions\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span> cymcp\u003cspan class=\"token double-colon punctuation\">::\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token class-name\">Json\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token double-colon punctuation\">::\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token function\">array\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">(\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">{\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token string\">\"app://state\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">}\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">)\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">}\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">}\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">)\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003c/code>\u003c/pre>\u003c/div>\u003cp>add/replace/remove du registre publie les changements d&#39;outils. Les ressources enregistrées\npublient changements de catalogue et d&#39;URI. Pour une modification externe, remplacer l&#39;instantané\nou publier resource avec son URI dans le même journal. Aucun contenu n&#39;est transmis. Les URI\nsont autorisés à l&#39;abonnement ; leur suppression/révocation invalide aussi les abonnements déjà\naccordés. Les lectures appliquent toujours les droits actuels. Les résultats privés générés restent\nabsents des catalogues publics. Un journal débordé signale les événements manqués pour invalider\nlargement plutôt que garder silencieusement des données périmées.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>Le serveur implémente subscriptions/listen MCP 2026 : accusé initial, ID d&#39;abonnement, filtres\nexplicites et annulation. HTTP utilise un POST SSE ; LocalHttpServer fournit le canal. Un transport\npersonnalisé doit fournir CallContext.notifications (null représente un battement de maintien).\nStdio utilise un pool d&#39;abonnements séparé, sans monopoliser le worker des commandes. Par défaut :\ndeux flux actifs et 64 URI par flux, réglables par max_subscriptions/max_resource_subscriptions dans\nMcpServerOptions. Chaque flux HTTP occupe un worker : en prévoir davantage que\nde flux (quatre par défaut). La fermeture du serveur annule les abonnements.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>Le client crée un lecteur uniquement avec start_notifications. Les événements invalident ses\ncaches avant le prochain accès, y compris lorsqu&#39;ils arrivent pendant une requête précédente.\ndrain_notifications sert à l&#39;intégration hôte/UI ; notification_status fournit filtre accepté, état\net code d&#39;erreur terminal. Aucun callback hôte n&#39;est exécuté sur le thread lecteur.\nstop_notifications annule et joint ce thread sans réessayer de commande. Un échec invalide le\ncache et reste visible ; reconnexion explicite. Les pairs MCP 2025 conservent TTL/clear_cache et\nrenvoient Unsupported pour cette API. Un serveur non configuré n&#39;annonce pas les abonnements.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"context\">Borner le contexte API et garder l&#39;historique complet\u003ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#/fr/runtime-options/context\" aria-label=\"Lien vers Borner le contexte API et garder l&#39;historique complet\">#\u003c/a>\u003c/h2>\u003cdiv class=\"code-block\">\u003cdiv class=\"code-toolbar\">\u003cspan>cpp\u003c/span>\u003cbutton type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copier\u003c/button>\u003c/div>\u003cpre>\u003ccode class=\"language-cpp\">\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-4-L1\" data-line=\"1\">cymcp\u003cspan class=\"token double-colon punctuation\">::\u003c/span>ContextOptions context\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-4-L2\" data-line=\"2\">context\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">.\u003c/span>max_bytes \u003cspan class=\"token operator\">=\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token number\">128\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token operator\">*\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token number\">1024\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token comment\">// Octets JSON, pas taille de fenêtre en tokens.\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-4-L3\" data-line=\"3\">context\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">.\u003c/span>recent_turns \u003cspan class=\"token operator\">=\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token number\">8\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-4-L4\" data-line=\"4\">conversation\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">.\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token function\">configure_context\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">(\u003c/span>context\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">)\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">;\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003c/code>\u003c/pre>\u003c/div>\u003cp>Configurer une Conversation inactive, avant utilisation ou restauration. max_bytes=0 désactive la\nprojection. La vue envoyée garde au plus recent_turns tours complets dans le budget. Instructions\nsystème et tour utilisateur actif restent présents. Les appels/résultats d&#39;outils ne sont jamais\nséparés de leur tour. Un message de référence signale l&#39;historique omis. Historique, transcription\net sauvegardes complets restent inchangés ; l&#39;hôte peut exposer des commandes de lecture bornée\nde l&#39;historique si l&#39;IA a besoin des détails anciens. Cela borne la vue envoyée, pas la RAM de toute\nla transcription conservée par l&#39;hôte.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>ContextOptions.summarize est un callback facultatif recevant previous_summary, les nouveaux\nmessages omis et max_bytes. Il ne s&#39;exécute que si nécessaire, ne lance aucune IA implicitement et\ndoit renvoyer un texte UTF-8 borné. Le résumé est une référence assistant, jamais une nouvelle\ninstruction système. Édition, suppression et restauration réinitialisent le résumé incrémental.\nOptions et callbacks restent une configuration de l&#39;hôte, absente des sauvegardes.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>Un système ou message courant trop gros produit ContextTooLarge avant génération. Si un tour\nd&#39;outils actif dépasse le budget, ses appels déjà exécutés et leurs résultats restent conservés,\nsans rejeu. Un nouveau tour utilisateur peut reprendre avec une projection adaptée. Les API\nvérifient le budget entre les tours d&#39;outils. Schémas d&#39;outils et enveloppes fournisseur ajoutent du\nvolume hors de ce budget de messages. Les CLI gardent leur comportement natif ; les configurer\nexplicitement via cette API renvoie Unsupported. ChatController applique ChatConnection.context\nuniquement aux API dont l&#39;historique est géré par l&#39;hôte.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"chat-lab\">Configuration Chat Lab\u003ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#/fr/runtime-options/chat-lab\" aria-label=\"Lien vers Configuration Chat Lab\">#\u003c/a>\u003c/h2>\u003cdiv class=\"code-block\">\u003cdiv class=\"code-toolbar\">\u003cspan>json\u003c/span>\u003cbutton type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copier\u003c/button>\u003c/div>\u003cpre>\u003ccode class=\"language-json\">\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-5-L1\" data-line=\"1\">\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">{\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-5-L2\" data-line=\"2\">  \u003cspan class=\"token property\">\"context\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">:\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">{\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token property\">\"max_bytes\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">:\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token number\">131072\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token property\">\"recent_turns\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">:\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token number\">8\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">}\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-5-L3\" data-line=\"3\">  \u003cspan class=\"token property\">\"performance\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">:\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">{\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token property\">\"enabled\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">:\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token boolean\">true\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">}\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-5-L4\" data-line=\"4\">  \u003cspan class=\"token property\">\"app_commands\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">:\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">{\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-5-L5\" data-line=\"5\">    \u003cspan class=\"token property\">\"notifications\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">:\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token boolean\">true\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-5-L6\" data-line=\"6\">    \u003cspan class=\"token property\">\"storage\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">:\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">{\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token property\">\"directory\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">:\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token string\">\"./private-cache\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">,\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token property\">\"disk_bytes\"\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token operator\">:\u003c/span> \u003cspan class=\"token number\">1073741824\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">}\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-5-L7\" data-line=\"7\">  \u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">}\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"code-line\" id=\"code-5-L8\" data-line=\"8\">\u003cspan class=\"token punctuation\">}\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003c/code>\u003c/pre>\u003c/div>\u003cp>Fusionner uniquement les options souhaitées dans une configuration fournisseur privée existante.\nLes mesures apparaissent dans Logs ; performance.file choisit un fichier JSONL privé séparé.\nLe mode notification expose aussi app://chat-lab/counter, mis à jour par les écritures SDK et MCP.\nLes anciennes configurations et les deux commandes d&#39;origine restent utilisables.\u003c/p>\n","text":"Options indépendantes # Les quatre fonctions sont facultatives. Core fournit ressources, stockage temporaire, journal de changements et mesures sans dépendance graphique ni IA. ContextWindow appartient à AI. Aucune dépendance externe supplémentaire ni modèle de résumé n'est installé. Sans configuration, les apps gardent l'historique API complet, les résultats conservés en RAM et les caches par TTL. Produire les gros volumes progressivement # cpp Copier # include \u003ccymcp/resources.hpp> cymcp :: ResourceOptions storage ; storage . disk_directory = host_selected_cache_folder ; storage . max_stored_bytes = 8 * 1024 * 1024 ; storage . spool_threshold = 1024 * 1024 ; storage . max_disk_bytes = 1024ULL * 1024 * 1024 ; auto resources = std :: make_shared \u003c cymcp :: ResourceRegistry > ( host_resource_policy , storage ) ; auto handle = resources -> store_stream ( [ snapshot_blocks ] ( std :: ostream & output , const cymcp :: CallContext & context ) { for ( const auto & block : snapshot_blocks ) { context . cancellation . check ( ) ; output . write ( block . data ( ) , block . size ( ) ) ; } } , \"text/plain\" , caller_context ) ; L'hôte choisit le dossier parent. Le SDK crée un sous-dossier aléatoire réservé au propriétaire et des fichiers privés ; les droits du parent restent inchangés. Au-delà du seuil, la production passe sur disque. Garder ce cache privé hors des dossiers exposés par d'autres outils de fichiers. Le quota inclut fichiers conservés, producteurs actifs et lecteurs qui gardent un instantané. Les anciens résultats peuvent être évincés ; un quota occupé par des opérations actives produit une erreur explicite. Quotas RAM/disque distincts, producteur appelé une seule fois, publication de la référence seulement après réussite complète. Lire la référence par les manifestes/morceaux existants. Pour le binaire, passer true en quatrième argument de store_stream : les contenus utilisent base64. Le texte respecte les frontières UTF-8. Échec, annulation, expiration et destruction normale libèrent les fichiers possédés. Le nettoyage disque vérifie les expirations environ chaque seconde ; une lecture active peut conserver son fichier immuable. Un arrêt brutal peut laisser un dossier privé orphelin à nettoyer par l'hôte. Aucun parcours/suppression des dossiers étrangers ni reprise implicite d'un producteur interrompu. storage_stats() indique les octets RAM/disque conservés et le nombre de résultats, sans chemin. ToolGateway sérialise ses gros résultats JSON directement dans le flux via store_json, sans créer une deuxième copie sérialisée complète. L'objet JSON du handler reste alloué : pour de plus gros volumes, produire directement une ressource progressive. Si tous les budgets sont dépassés, la passerelle garde son repli historique vers le résultat complet en ligne ; l'API de flux directe renvoie ResourceTooLarge sans tronquer. TTL/LRU sont temporaires et ne remplacent pas des archives. Mesurer sans enregistrer les contenus # cpp Copier # include \u003ccymcp/performance.hpp> cymcp :: PerformanceOptions options ; options . jsonl_file = host_selected_private_log_file ; // Facultatif : mémoire seule sinon. auto performance = std :: make_shared \u003c cymcp :: PerformanceMonitor > ( options ) ; commands -> set_performance_monitor ( performance ) ; auto totals = performance -> snapshot ( ) ; auto recent_records = performance -> drain ( ) ; Autres points d'intégration : CallContext.performance, McpServerOptions.performance, McpClientOptions.performance et ChatConnection.performance. Les lignes contiennent horodatage, stage/name, statut, elapsed_ms, input_bytes, output_bytes et cache_hit. Aucun argument, réponse, explication d'erreur, identité, secret ou ID de requête. Les étapes distinguent operation, mcp.server, mcp.client et conversation. La sortie d'une conversation compte le texte UTF-8 final ; les autres tailles comptent le JSON sérialisé. Ce ne sont pas des nombres de tokens. Le calcul parcourt le JSON sans en allouer une copie sérialisée et ne s'effectue que si le moniteur est activé. Les statistiques conservent appels/erreurs/cache, volumes, moyenne/maximum et p50_upper_ms, p95_upper_ms : bornes de classes d'histogramme, pas percentiles exacts. Catégories et lignes sont bornées ; les catégories excédentaires vont dans other. La file d'écriture est bornée ; dropped_file_records et file_errors signalent les échecs. drain() ne supprime pas les agrégats. Le chemin fourni est ouvert comme nouveau fichier privé ; rotation/rétention relèvent de l'hôte. Les mesures ne changent ni les droits, ni les appels, ni les règles de cache. Recevoir les changements # cpp Copier # include \u003ccymcp/changes.hpp> # include \u003ccymcp/mcp.hpp> auto changes = std :: make_shared \u003c cymcp :: ChangeFeed > ( ) ; commands -> set_change_feed ( changes ) ; resources -> set_change_feed ( changes ) ; cymcp :: McpServerOptions options ; options . resources = resources ; options . changes = changes ; cymcp :: McpServer server ( * commands , \"My app\" , options ) ; // Côté client, après connect() : client . start_notifications ( { { \"toolsListChanged\" , true } , { \"resourcesListChanged\" , true } , { \"resourceSubscriptions\" , cymcp :: Json :: array ( { \"app://state\" } ) } } ) ; add/replace/remove du registre publie les changements d'outils. Les ressources enregistrées publient changements de catalogue et d'URI. Pour une modification externe, remplacer l'instantané ou publier resource avec son URI dans le même journal. Aucun contenu n'est transmis. Les URI sont autorisés à l'abonnement ; leur suppression/révocation invalide aussi les abonnements déjà accordés. Les lectures appliquent toujours les droits actuels. Les résultats privés générés restent absents des catalogues publics. Un journal débordé signale les événements manqués pour invalider largement plutôt que garder silencieusement des données périmées. Le serveur implémente subscriptions/listen MCP 2026 : accusé initial, ID d'abonnement, filtres explicites et annulation. HTTP utilise un POST SSE ; LocalHttpServer fournit le canal. Un transport personnalisé doit fournir CallContext.notifications (null représente un battement de maintien). Stdio utilise un pool d'abonnements séparé, sans monopoliser le worker des commandes. Par défaut : deux flux actifs et 64 URI par flux, réglables par max_subscriptions/max_resource_subscriptions dans McpServerOptions. Chaque flux HTTP occupe un worker : en prévoir davantage que de flux (quatre par défaut). La fermeture du serveur annule les abonnements. Le client crée un lecteur uniquement avec start_notifications. Les événements invalident ses caches avant le prochain accès, y compris lorsqu'ils arrivent pendant une requête précédente. drain_notifications sert à l'intégration hôte/UI ; notification_status fournit filtre accepté, état et code d'erreur terminal. Aucun callback hôte n'est exécuté sur le thread lecteur. stop_notifications annule et joint ce thread sans réessayer de commande. Un échec invalide le cache et reste visible ; reconnexion explicite. Les pairs MCP 2025 conservent TTL/clear_cache et renvoient Unsupported pour cette API. Un serveur non configuré n'annonce pas les abonnements. Borner le contexte API et garder l'historique complet # cpp Copier cymcp :: ContextOptions context ; context . max_bytes = 128 * 1024 ; // Octets JSON, pas taille de fenêtre en tokens. context . recent_turns = 8 ; conversation . configure_context ( context ) ; Configurer une Conversation inactive, avant utilisation ou restauration. max_bytes=0 désactive la projection. La vue envoyée garde au plus recent_turns tours complets dans le budget. Instructions système et tour utilisateur actif restent présents. Les appels/résultats d'outils ne sont jamais séparés de leur tour. Un message de référence signale l'historique omis. Historique, transcription et sauvegardes complets restent inchangés ; l'hôte peut exposer des commandes de lecture bornée de l'historique si l'IA a besoin des détails anciens. Cela borne la vue envoyée, pas la RAM de toute la transcription conservée par l'hôte. ContextOptions.summarize est un callback facultatif recevant previous_summary, les nouveaux messages omis et max_bytes. Il ne s'exécute que si nécessaire, ne lance aucune IA implicitement et doit renvoyer un texte UTF-8 borné. Le résumé est une référence assistant, jamais une nouvelle instruction système. Édition, suppression et restauration réinitialisent le résumé incrémental. Options et callbacks restent une configuration de l'hôte, absente des sauvegardes. Un système ou message courant trop gros produit ContextTooLarge avant génération. Si un tour d'outils actif dépasse le budget, ses appels déjà exécutés et leurs résultats restent conservés, sans rejeu. Un nouveau tour utilisateur peut reprendre avec une projection adaptée. Les API vérifient le budget entre les tours d'outils. Schémas d'outils et enveloppes fournisseur ajoutent du volume hors de ce budget de messages. Les CLI gardent leur comportement natif ; les configurer explicitement via cette API renvoie Unsupported. ChatController applique ChatConnection.context uniquement aux API dont l'historique est géré par l'hôte. Configuration Chat Lab # json Copier { \"context\" : { \"max_bytes\" : 131072 , \"recent_turns\" : 8 } , \"performance\" : { \"enabled\" : true } , \"app_commands\" : { \"notifications\" : true , \"storage\" : { \"directory\" : \"./private-cache\" , \"disk_bytes\" : 1073741824 } } } Fusionner uniquement les options souhaitées dans une configuration fournisseur privée existante. Les mesures apparaissent dans Logs ; performance.file choisit un fichier JSONL privé séparé. Le mode notification expose aussi app://chat-lab/counter, mis à jour par les écritures SDK et MCP. Les anciennes configurations et les deux commandes d'origine restent utilisables. #include \u003ccymcp/resources.hpp> cymcp::ResourceOptions storage; storage.disk_directory = host_selected_cache_folder; storage.max_stored_bytes = 8 * 1024 * 1024; storage.spool_threshold = 1024 * 1024; storage.max_disk_bytes = 1024ULL * 1024 * 1024; auto resources = std::make_shared\u003ccymcp::ResourceRegistry>(host_resource_policy, storage); auto handle = resources->store_stream( [snapshot_blocks](std::ostream& output, const cymcp::CallContext& context) { for (const auto& block : snapshot_blocks) { context.cancellation.check(); output.write(block.data(), block.size()); } }, \"text/plain\", caller_context); #include \u003ccymcp/performance.hpp> cymcp::PerformanceOptions options; options.jsonl_file = host_selected_private_log_file; // Facultatif : mémoire seule sinon. auto performance = std::make_shared\u003ccymcp::PerformanceMonitor>(options); commands->set_performance_monitor(performance); auto totals = performance->snapshot(); auto recent_records = performance->drain(); #include \u003ccymcp/changes.hpp> #include \u003ccymcp/mcp.hpp> auto changes = std::make_shared\u003ccymcp::ChangeFeed>(); commands->set_change_feed(changes); resources->set_change_feed(changes); cymcp::McpServerOptions options; options.resources = resources; options.changes = changes; cymcp::McpServer server(*commands, \"My app\", options); // Côté client, après connect() : client.start_notifications({{\"toolsListChanged\", true}, {\"resourcesListChanged\", true}, {\"resourceSubscriptions\", cymcp::Json::array({\"app://state\"})}}); cymcp::ContextOptions context; context.max_bytes = 128 * 1024; // Octets JSON, pas taille de fenêtre en tokens. context.recent_turns = 8; conversation.configure_context(context); { \"context\": {\"max_bytes\": 131072, \"recent_turns\": 8}, \"performance\": {\"enabled\": true}, \"app_commands\": { \"notifications\": true, \"storage\": {\"directory\": \"./private-cache\", \"disk_bytes\": 1073741824} } }","headings":[{"id":"options","text":"Options indépendantes","level":2},{"id":"disk","text":"Produire les gros volumes progressivement","level":2},{"id":"performance","text":"Mesurer sans enregistrer les contenus","level":2},{"id":"notifications","text":"Recevoir les changements","level":2},{"id":"context","text":"Borner le contexte API et garder l'historique complet","level":2},{"id":"chat-lab","text":"Configuration Chat Lab","level":2}],"anchors":["L1","L2","L3","L4","L5","L6","L7","L8","L9","L10","L11","L12","L13","L14","L15","code-2-L1","code-2-L2","code-2-L3","code-2-L4","code-2-L5","code-2-L6","code-2-L7","code-2-L8","code-3-L1","code-3-L2","code-3-L3","code-3-L4","code-3-L5","code-3-L6","code-3-L7","code-3-L8","code-3-L9","code-3-L10","code-3-L11","code-3-L12","code-3-L13","code-3-L14","code-4-L1","code-4-L2","code-4-L3","code-4-L4","code-5-L1","code-5-L2","code-5-L3","code-5-L4","code-5-L5","code-5-L6","code-5-L7","code-5-L8"],"languages":["cpp","json"],"code":"#include \u003ccymcp/resources.hpp>\n\ncymcp::ResourceOptions storage;\nstorage.disk_directory = host_selected_cache_folder;\nstorage.max_stored_bytes = 8 * 1024 * 1024;\nstorage.spool_threshold = 1024 * 1024;\nstorage.max_disk_bytes = 1024ULL * 1024 * 1024;\nauto resources = std::make_shared\u003ccymcp::ResourceRegistry>(host_resource_policy, storage);\nauto handle = resources->store_stream(\n    [snapshot_blocks](std::ostream& output, const cymcp::CallContext& context) {\n        for (const auto& block : snapshot_blocks) {\n            context.cancellation.check();\n            output.write(block.data(), block.size());\n        }\n    }, \"text/plain\", caller_context);\n#include \u003ccymcp/performance.hpp>\n\ncymcp::PerformanceOptions options;\noptions.jsonl_file = host_selected_private_log_file; // Facultatif : mémoire seule sinon.\nauto performance = std::make_shared\u003ccymcp::PerformanceMonitor>(options);\ncommands->set_performance_monitor(performance);\nauto totals = performance->snapshot();\nauto recent_records = performance->drain();\n#include \u003ccymcp/changes.hpp>\n#include \u003ccymcp/mcp.hpp>\n\nauto changes = std::make_shared\u003ccymcp::ChangeFeed>();\ncommands->set_change_feed(changes);\nresources->set_change_feed(changes);\ncymcp::McpServerOptions options;\noptions.resources = resources;\noptions.changes = changes;\ncymcp::McpServer server(*commands, \"My app\", options);\n// Côté client, après connect() :\nclient.start_notifications({{\"toolsListChanged\", true},\n    {\"resourcesListChanged\", true},\n    {\"resourceSubscriptions\", cymcp::Json::array({\"app://state\"})}});\ncymcp::ContextOptions context;\ncontext.max_bytes = 128 * 1024; // Octets JSON, pas taille de fenêtre en tokens.\ncontext.recent_turns = 8;\nconversation.configure_context(context);\n{\n  \"context\": {\"max_bytes\": 131072, \"recent_turns\": 8},\n  \"performance\": {\"enabled\": true},\n  \"app_commands\": {\n    \"notifications\": true,\n    \"storage\": {\"directory\": \"./private-cache\", \"disk_bytes\": 1073741824}\n  }\n}","assets":[],"links":[],"kind":"guide","revision":"288475a18f97"},{"id":"troubleshooting","title":"Résoudre un problème de connexion","description":"Comprendre les erreurs fournisseur, les interruptions et l'absence du manuel local.","section":"Guides","parent":"overview","order":4,"sourceRevision":"3","locale":"fr","html":"\u003ch2 id=\"connection\">Erreurs de connexion\u003ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#/fr/troubleshooting/connection\" aria-label=\"Lien vers Erreurs de connexion\">#\u003c/a>\u003c/h2>\u003cp>Ouvrir \u003cstrong>Journal\u003c/strong> pour identifier l&#39;étape : détection, protocole, compte, catalogue ou session.\nUtiliser \u003cstrong>Copier le journal\u003c/strong> ou \u003cstrong>Ouvrir le fichier journal\u003c/strong> pour les diagnostics.\nConsulter les \u003ca href=\"#/fr/chat-lab/logs\">commandes du journal\u003c/a>.\u003c/p>\n\u003ctable>\n\u003cthead>\n\u003ctr>\n\u003cth>Erreur ou symptôme\u003c/th>\n\u003cth>Action\u003c/th>\n\u003c/tr>\n\u003c/thead>\n\u003ctbody>\u003ctr>\n\u003ctd>\u003ccode>ExecutableMissing\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>Sélectionner le CLI natif et vérifier son exécution dans le compte/environnement voulu.\u003c/td>\n\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\n\u003ctd>\u003ccode>AuthenticationRequired\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>Pour un fournisseur natif, utiliser \u003cstrong>Se connecter\u003c/strong>, terminer la connexion native puis reconnecter ici. Pour une API, fournir l&#39;identifiant par variable/champ en mémoire.\u003c/td>\n\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\n\u003ctd>\u003ccode>ProviderError\u003c/code> après connexion\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>Vérifier l&#39;ID exact du modèle, les droits du compte et l&#39;erreur native hors de l&#39;app.\u003c/td>\n\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\n\u003ctd>Catalogue \u003ccode>Unsupported\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>Saisir un vrai ID de modèle ; certains transports n&#39;exposent pas la découverte.\u003c/td>\n\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\n\u003ctd>Adresse locale injoignable\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>Démarrer le service et vérifier URL de base, port et format API.\u003c/td>\n\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\n\u003ctd>\u003ccode>UnsupportedContent\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>Choisir un modèle/transport compatible avec cette pièce jointe, ou la retirer.\u003c/td>\n\u003c/tr>\n\u003c/tbody>\u003c/table>\n\u003cp>Le compte CLI d&#39;un processus lancé peut différer de l&#39;environnement d&#39;un autre terminal.\nUtiliser \u003ccode>process.environment\u003c/code> si l&#39;hôte a besoin de valeurs propres à l&#39;enfant. Une connexion\nréussie ne garantit pas que le compte peut effectuer une génération.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"interrupted\">Conversations interrompues\u003ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#/fr/troubleshooting/interrupted\" aria-label=\"Lien vers Conversations interrompues\">#\u003c/a>\u003c/h2>\u003cp>\u003ccode>Cancelled\u003c/code> indique une interruption, pas une réponse finale réussie. Un flux tronqué peut produire\n\u003ccode>UnexpectedEOF\u003c/code>. Conserver le texte partiel, reconnecter explicitement, puis choisir le message suivant.\n\u003ccode>SessionInvalid\u003c/code> indique que la session exacte n&#39;a pas pu être reprise ; garder son historique enregistré.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>\u003ccode>ContextTooLarge\u003c/code> indique désormais une garde mémoire (256 Mio par message) ou la fenêtre de\ncontexte du modèle : démarrer une nouvelle conversation ou réduire les pièces jointes. Une\ninterface lente ou réduite ne fait plus échouer un tour ; un très long historique fait seulement\nsortir ses plus anciens messages de la vue.\nSauvegarder puis créer une conversation, ou réduire les pièces jointes. ChatUI borne ses événements\net son texte affiché ; il ne supprime pas silencieusement une conversation pour respecter son budget.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"help\">Manuel absent\u003ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#/fr/troubleshooting/help\" aria-label=\"Lien vers Manuel absent\">#\u003c/a>\u003c/h2>\u003cp>Conserver \u003ccode>Documentation/Documentation.html\u003c/code> et le dossier complet \u003ccode>Documentation/DocData\u003c/code> à côté\nde Chat Lab. F1 ouvre cette copie installée, sans repli en ligne. Si le dossier manque, le restaurer\ndepuis le paquet applicatif ou reconstruire le paquet. Ouvrir directement le HTML pour vérifier ses\nscripts et images locaux. Le lecteur ne demande ni Node.js ni serveur web.\u003c/p>\n","text":"Erreurs de connexion # Ouvrir Journal pour identifier l'étape : détection, protocole, compte, catalogue ou session. Utiliser Copier le journal ou Ouvrir le fichier journal pour les diagnostics. Consulter les commandes du journal . Erreur ou symptôme Action ExecutableMissing Sélectionner le CLI natif et vérifier son exécution dans le compte/environnement voulu. AuthenticationRequired Pour un fournisseur natif, utiliser Se connecter , terminer la connexion native puis reconnecter ici. Pour une API, fournir l'identifiant par variable/champ en mémoire. ProviderError après connexion Vérifier l'ID exact du modèle, les droits du compte et l'erreur native hors de l'app. Catalogue Unsupported Saisir un vrai ID de modèle ; certains transports n'exposent pas la découverte. Adresse locale injoignable Démarrer le service et vérifier URL de base, port et format API. UnsupportedContent Choisir un modèle/transport compatible avec cette pièce jointe, ou la retirer. Le compte CLI d'un processus lancé peut différer de l'environnement d'un autre terminal. Utiliser process.environment si l'hôte a besoin de valeurs propres à l'enfant. Une connexion réussie ne garantit pas que le compte peut effectuer une génération. Conversations interrompues # Cancelled indique une interruption, pas une réponse finale réussie. Un flux tronqué peut produire UnexpectedEOF . Conserver le texte partiel, reconnecter explicitement, puis choisir le message suivant. SessionInvalid indique que la session exacte n'a pas pu être reprise ; garder son historique enregistré. ContextTooLarge indique désormais une garde mémoire (256 Mio par message) ou la fenêtre de contexte du modèle : démarrer une nouvelle conversation ou réduire les pièces jointes. Une interface lente ou réduite ne fait plus échouer un tour ; un très long historique fait seulement sortir ses plus anciens messages de la vue. Sauvegarder puis créer une conversation, ou réduire les pièces jointes. ChatUI borne ses événements et son texte affiché ; il ne supprime pas silencieusement une conversation pour respecter son budget. Manuel absent # Conserver Documentation/Documentation.html et le dossier complet Documentation/DocData à côté de Chat Lab. F1 ouvre cette copie installée, sans repli en ligne. Si le dossier manque, le restaurer depuis le paquet applicatif ou reconstruire le paquet. Ouvrir directement le HTML pour vérifier ses scripts et images locaux. Le lecteur ne demande ni Node.js ni serveur web.","headings":[{"id":"connection","text":"Erreurs de connexion","level":2},{"id":"interrupted","text":"Conversations interrompues","level":2},{"id":"help","text":"Manuel absent","level":2}],"anchors":[],"languages":[],"code":"","assets":[],"links":["#/fr/chat-lab/logs"],"kind":"guide","revision":"30e111c43ced"}]};
